    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-ud-2a-s4-20260727",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 3402.5,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 342,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-27 (User-defined listener path, 2A-S4): the NON-platform half of the listener rail.\nNEW integrations/event-sources/user-defined-poll.ts is the provider-agnostic sibling of platform-poll.ts:\nit reads the paging contract from the integration PACKAGE's listenerConfig (pollAction/eventArrayField/\ndedupKeyField/cursorField; trigger pollConfig.actionName overrides) and polls through\nintegrations/action-executor.ts executeUserIntegrationAction - the SAME executor, with the SAME injected\nautomation seam, that the automation integration step uses - bound in server.ts to the TRIGGER's org+owner.\nlistener-supervisor.ts's 2A-S1 honest-throw pollUserDefined? seam is REPLACED by a REQUIRED\ncallUserIntegration dep (mirrors callPlatform), so a half-wired rail is a compile error. Same durability\ncontract as the platform branch: cursor written LAST + only when every item is durable, dedup key = the\nitem's own id field, cancel-checked at every step, and NO BACKFILL pinned at INITIALIZATION (an\nobservably-empty establishing poll ARMS the listener; everything seen after it is delivered - pinning on\nthe first SUCCESSFUL poll instead lost events). An automation-backed poll (citius) is unwrapped from the\n{runId,status,summary,output} run envelope before the package's field paths are applied.\nSTILL NOT WORKING, both named in docs/findings.md, neither silent: (a) the IMAP TRANSPORT is DEFERRED -\nIntegrationAction gains optional transport (absent => 'http'), the imap package declares transport:'imap'\nand the executor refuses it with unsupported_transport BEFORE any decrypt, so an IMAP listener fails\nloudly every tick, never a fabricated empty mailbox; (b) CITIUS cannot poll yet - its automationBinding\nid is a template placeholder no lookup resolves (a repo-wide gap, not this rail's) and its captured\nbrowser session lands in 2A-S6. So M365/Google are the only WORKING listener sources today.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-27 (User-defined listener path, 2A-S4): the NON-platform half of the listener rail.\nNEW integrations/event-sources/user-defined-poll.ts is the provider-agnostic sibling of platform-poll.ts:\nit reads the paging contract from the integration PACKAGE's listenerConfig (pollAction/eventArrayField/\ndedupKeyField/cursorField; trigger pollConfig.actionName overrides) and polls through\nintegrations/action-executor.ts executeUserIntegrationAction - the SAME executor, with the SAME injected\nautomation seam, that the automation integration step uses - bound in server.ts to the TRIGGER's org+owner.\nlistener-supervisor.ts's 2A-S1 honest-throw pollUserDefined? seam is REPLACED by a REQUIRED\ncallUserIntegration dep (mirrors callPlatform), so a half-wired rail is a compile error. Same durability\ncontract as the platform branch: cursor written LAST + only when every item is durable, dedup key = the\nitem's own id field, cancel-checked at every step, and NO BACKFILL pinned at INITIALIZATION (an\nobservably-empty establishing poll ARMS the listener; everything seen after it is delivered - pinning on\nthe first SUCCESSFUL poll instead lost events). An automation-backed poll (citius) is unwrapped from the\n{runId,status,summary,output} run envelope before the package's field paths are applied.\nSTILL NOT WORKING, both named in docs/findings.md, neither silent: (a) the IMAP TRANSPORT is DEFERRED -\nIntegrationAction gains optional transport (absent => 'http'), the imap package declares transport:'imap'\nand the executor refuses it with unsupported_transport BEFORE any decrypt, so an IMAP listener fails\nloudly every tick, never a fabricated empty mailbox; (b) CITIUS cannot poll yet - its automationBinding\nid is a template placeholder no lookup resolves (a repo-wide gap, not this rail's) and its captured\nbrowser session lands in 2A-S6. So M365/Google are the only WORKING listener sources today.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-27 (User-defined listener path, 2A-S4): the NON-platform half of the listener rail.\nNEW integrations/event-sources/user-defined-poll.ts is the provider-agnostic sibling of platform-poll.ts:\nit reads the paging contract from the integration PACKAGE's listenerConfig (pollAction/eventArrayField/\ndedupKeyField/cursorField; trigger pollConfig.actionName overrides) and polls through\nintegrations/action-executor.ts executeUserIntegrationAction - the SAME executor, with the SAME injected\nautomation seam, that the automation integration step uses - bound in server.ts to the TRIGGER's org+owner.\nlistener-supervisor.ts's 2A-S1 honest-throw pollUserDefined? seam is REPLACED by a REQUIRED\ncallUserIntegration dep (mirrors callPlatform), so a half-wired rail is a compile error. Same durability\ncontract as the platform branch: cursor written LAST + only when every item is durable, dedup key = the\nitem's own id field, cancel-checked at every step, and NO BACKFILL pinned at INITIALIZATION (an\nobservably-empty establishing poll ARMS the listener; everything seen after it is delivered - pinning on\nthe first SUCCESSFUL poll instead lost events). An automation-backed poll (citius) is unwrapped from the\n{runId,status,summary,output} run envelope before the package's field paths are applied.\nSTILL NOT WORKING, both named in docs/findings.md, neither silent: (a) the IMAP TRANSPORT is DEFERRED -\nIntegrationAction gains optional transport (absent => 'http'), the imap package declares transport:'imap'\nand the executor refuses it with unsupported_transport BEFORE any decrypt, so an IMAP listener fails\nloudly every tick, never a fabricated empty mailbox; (b) CITIUS cannot poll yet - its automationBinding\nid is a template placeholder no lookup resolves (a repo-wide gap, not this rail's) and its captured\nbrowser session lands in 2A-S6. So M365/Google are the only WORKING listener sources today.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
