    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-cofre-endtoend-20260728",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 4984.5,
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 560,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-28 (Cofre reachable end to end - routes, typist, envelope, UI).\n\nroutes/cofre.ts mounts /api/v1/cofre (list/create/delete/grant/lock/lock-all). Thin by design:\nevery authorization decision stays in api/src/cofre/, so there is one place to audit. The six\ndescriptors moved PENDING -> COVERED in the schema-coverage gate in the same change, backed by a\nreal contract test - the gate CAUGHT the first attempt, which landed descriptors with no test.\n\nautomation/typist.ts is THE credential-touching browser capability, and the only one. Sequence:\norigin checked BEFORE any unwrap; a credential window opened on streaming/ (screencast STOPPED,\nviewer input refused, in-flight frames dropped) and the fill REFUSED if suppression cannot be\nconfirmed; unwrap through the Cofre seam; typed via CDP Input.dispatchKeyEvent - NOT\nlocator.fill(), which sets the DOM value where any page script can read it; fill+submit as ONE\nunit, returning only when no password field remains, so read-back is impossible by construction.\nAn unknown form pauses for the relay and is NEVER handed to the fixer LLM (I5).\nPage.startScreencast has NO mask option, so the media channel gets SUPPRESSION where the\nscreenshot path (screenshot-masking.ts) gets masking - two different controls for two different\nmechanisms, not one applied twice.\n\ndata/kms.ts is the KeyWrapper SEAM: LocalKeyWrapper (tenant-bound KEK from ENCRYPTION_KEY) today,\na Cloud KMS wrapper installed via setKeyWrapper with no call-site change. crypto.ts gains a\nVERSIONED envelope (v2.<wrappedDek>.<iv>.<tag>.<ct>) with a fresh DEK per RECORD; v1 rows keep\ndecrypting, so WS-K was adopted with no migration flag day. HONEST LIMIT: under LocalKeyWrapper a\nDB breach plus the env var yields plaintext - that is the property KMS removes.\n\nweb: /cofre is its OWN left-menu item (not a settings sub-page - locking a credential is an\noperational act reached for under time pressure). Four visually DISTINCT states; an indefinite\nunlock must never look like a timed one. A signature identity renders no duration control at all,\nthe third layer of I7 after the shared schema and the service.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-28 (Cofre reachable end to end - routes, typist, envelope, UI).\n\nroutes/cofre.ts mounts /api/v1/cofre (list/create/delete/grant/lock/lock-all). Thin by design:\nevery authorization decision stays in api/src/cofre/, so there is one place to audit. The six\ndescriptors moved PENDING -> COVERED in the schema-coverage gate in the same change, backed by a\nreal contract test - the gate CAUGHT the first attempt, which landed descriptors with no test.\n\nautomation/typist.ts is THE credential-touching browser capability, and the only one. Sequence:\norigin checked BEFORE any unwrap; a credential window opened on streaming/ (screencast STOPPED,\nviewer input refused, in-flight frames dropped) and the fill REFUSED if suppression cannot be\nconfirmed; unwrap through the Cofre seam; typed via CDP Input.dispatchKeyEvent - NOT\nlocator.fill(), which sets the DOM value where any page script can read it; fill+submit as ONE\nunit, returning only when no password field remains, so read-back is impossible by construction.\nAn unknown form pauses for the relay and is NEVER handed to the fixer LLM (I5).\nPage.startScreencast has NO mask option, so the media channel gets SUPPRESSION where the\nscreenshot path (screenshot-masking.ts) gets masking - two different controls for two different\nmechanisms, not one applied twice.\n\ndata/kms.ts is the KeyWrapper SEAM: LocalKeyWrapper (tenant-bound KEK from ENCRYPTION_KEY) today,\na Cloud KMS wrapper installed via setKeyWrapper with no call-site change. crypto.ts gains a\nVERSIONED envelope (v2.<wrappedDek>.<iv>.<tag>.<ct>) with a fresh DEK per RECORD; v1 rows keep\ndecrypting, so WS-K was adopted with no migration flag day. HONEST LIMIT: under LocalKeyWrapper a\nDB breach plus the env var yields plaintext - that is the property KMS removes.\n\nweb: /cofre is its OWN left-menu item (not a settings sub-page - locking a credential is an\noperational act reached for under time pressure). Four visually DISTINCT states; an indefinite\nunlock must never look like a timed one. A signature identity renders no duration control at all,\nthe third layer of I7 after the shared schema and the service.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-28 (Cofre reachable end to end - routes, typist, envelope, UI).\n\nroutes/cofre.ts mounts /api/v1/cofre (list/create/delete/grant/lock/lock-all). Thin by design:\nevery authorization decision stays in api/src/cofre/, so there is one place to audit. The six\ndescriptors moved PENDING -> COVERED in the schema-coverage gate in the same change, backed by a\nreal contract test - the gate CAUGHT the first attempt, which landed descriptors with no test.\n\nautomation/typist.ts is THE credential-touching browser capability, and the only one. Sequence:\norigin checked BEFORE any unwrap; a credential window opened on streaming/ (screencast STOPPED,\nviewer input refused, in-flight frames dropped) and the fill REFUSED if suppression cannot be\nconfirmed; unwrap through the Cofre seam; typed via CDP Input.dispatchKeyEvent - NOT\nlocator.fill(), which sets the DOM value where any page script can read it; fill+submit as ONE\nunit, returning only when no password field remains, so read-back is impossible by construction.\nAn unknown form pauses for the relay and is NEVER handed to the fixer LLM (I5).\nPage.startScreencast has NO mask option, so the media channel gets SUPPRESSION where the\nscreenshot path (screenshot-masking.ts) gets masking - two different controls for two different\nmechanisms, not one applied twice.\n\ndata/kms.ts is the KeyWrapper SEAM: LocalKeyWrapper (tenant-bound KEK from ENCRYPTION_KEY) today,\na Cloud KMS wrapper installed via setKeyWrapper with no call-site change. crypto.ts gains a\nVERSIONED envelope (v2.<wrappedDek>.<iv>.<tag>.<ct>) with a fresh DEK per RECORD; v1 rows keep\ndecrypting, so WS-K was adopted with no migration flag day. HONEST LIMIT: under LocalKeyWrapper a\nDB breach plus the env var yields plaintext - that is the property KMS removes.\n\nweb: /cofre is its OWN left-menu item (not a settings sub-page - locking a credential is an\noperational act reached for under time pressure). Four visually DISTINCT states; an indefinite\nunlock must never look like a timed one. A signature identity renders no duration control at all,\nthe third layer of I7 after the shared schema and the service.",
      "fontSize": 14,
