    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-session-establishment-20260801",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 8530,
      "width": 916,
      "height": 315,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-01 (Cofre session establishment, slice CS5): the typist and the session-checkout\ndecision - both built, both security-tested, both wired to NOTHING - get their first call site.\napi/src/automation/session-establishment.ts is the ONE place \"the session is stale\" becomes \"log in\nagain\": it asks cofre/session-checkout for a verdict, reuses a healthy session with NO browser and NO\npassword, drives typistLogin for the `typist` route, and round-trips the fresh storageState back\nthrough captureSessionToCofre. `attended` and `relay` are TYPED REFUSALS - establishment never\nimprovises and never shows a login form to a model - and `egress-unavailable` is its own refusal,\nbecause a person at a card reader cannot conjure a residential pairing.\n\nNo new module edge: automation/ -> cofre/ and automation/ -> streaming/ already existed (typist.ts).\nWhat is new is the Cofre's public surface - findSessionItemsForOrigin + markSessionUnhealthy - added\nso the query and the health write stay INSIDE the lint-fenced module rather than being re-derived by\na caller that cannot reach cofre/store.ts.\n\nAT MOST ONCE per call, by construction: no loop, no retry, no re-checkout of the item just captured.\nPortal lock-out policies (Caixa Citius among them) are unknown; a second automated attempt after a\nrefusal is how accounts get locked. Health-on-use is a SEPARATE write (markSessionUnhealthy), so this\nmodule cannot notice a mid-run login redirect and silently re-authenticate in a loop.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-01 (Cofre session establishment, slice CS5): the typist and the session-checkout\ndecision - both built, both security-tested, both wired to NOTHING - get their first call site.\napi/src/automation/session-establishment.ts is the ONE place \"the session is stale\" becomes \"log in\nagain\": it asks cofre/session-checkout for a verdict, reuses a healthy session with NO browser and NO\npassword, drives typistLogin for the `typist` route, and round-trips the fresh storageState back\nthrough captureSessionToCofre. `attended` and `relay` are TYPED REFUSALS - establishment never\nimprovises and never shows a login form to a model - and `egress-unavailable` is its own refusal,\nbecause a person at a card reader cannot conjure a residential pairing.\n\nNo new module edge: automation/ -> cofre/ and automation/ -> streaming/ already existed (typist.ts).\nWhat is new is the Cofre's public surface - findSessionItemsForOrigin + markSessionUnhealthy - added\nso the query and the health write stay INSIDE the lint-fenced module rather than being re-derived by\na caller that cannot reach cofre/store.ts.\n\nAT MOST ONCE per call, by construction: no loop, no retry, no re-checkout of the item just captured.\nPortal lock-out policies (Caixa Citius among them) are unknown; a second automated attempt after a\nrefusal is how accounts get locked. Health-on-use is a SEPARATE write (markSessionUnhealthy), so this\nmodule cannot notice a mid-run login redirect and silently re-authenticate in a loop.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-01 (Cofre session establishment, slice CS5): the typist and the session-checkout\ndecision - both built, both security-tested, both wired to NOTHING - get their first call site.\napi/src/automation/session-establishment.ts is the ONE place \"the session is stale\" becomes \"log in\nagain\": it asks cofre/session-checkout for a verdict, reuses a healthy session with NO browser and NO\npassword, drives typistLogin for the `typist` route, and round-trips the fresh storageState back\nthrough captureSessionToCofre. `attended` and `relay` are TYPED REFUSALS - establishment never\nimprovises and never shows a login form to a model - and `egress-unavailable` is its own refusal,\nbecause a person at a card reader cannot conjure a residential pairing.\n\nNo new module edge: automation/ -> cofre/ and automation/ -> streaming/ already existed (typist.ts).\nWhat is new is the Cofre's public surface - findSessionItemsForOrigin + markSessionUnhealthy - added\nso the query and the health write stay INSIDE the lint-fenced module rather than being re-derived by\na caller that cannot reach cofre/store.ts.\n\nAT MOST ONCE per call, by construction: no loop, no retry, no re-checkout of the item just captured.\nPortal lock-out policies (Caixa Citius among them) are unknown; a second automated attempt after a\nrefusal is how accounts get locked. Health-on-use is a SEPARATE write (markSessionUnhealthy), so this\nmodule cannot notice a mid-run login redirect and silently re-authenticate in a loop.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
