    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-b2-cofre-credential-join-20260803",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 9287.5,
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 385,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (integration credential custody, slice B2): the WS-C join, and the ONE egress truth\nmoving off the artifact that authors it.\n\nNEW api/src/cofre/integration-items.ts - the integration half of the Cofre's own public surface (mint with\nthe connect ceremony's single until_locked grant, the owner-scoped + link-checked lookup, the granted-origin\nscope, unwrapForIntegration, discard). It lives INSIDE cofre/ because cofre/store.ts is lint-fenced\n(COFRE_STORE_BAN): a caller in integrations/ wanting 'the item holding this config's credentials' would\notherwise re-derive both the tenancy filter and the link match - the drift the fence exists to prevent, and\nthe explicit CS5 review outcome. It expresses the join as DATA ({integrationKey, configId}), never as a type\ndependency: cofre/ is the lower tier and must not import integrations/.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/credential-cofre.ts - the Rule-10 SHADOW + COMPARATOR (imports cofre/ + security/\n+ its own definition-registry). service.ts createConfig/updateConfig/deleteConfig mint/rotate/destroy the\nshadow item; nothing about the live read changes until the 2026-08-15 cutover.\n\nSEAM RE-POINTED, not added: server.ts setIntegrationOriginResolver now delegates to\negressOriginsForIntegration - the item's boundOrigins while granted, [] (refuse) once locked, and the old\ndefinition-derived list ONLY for a config with no item. The inline derivation is GONE from the composition\nroot, so the body is exercisable by a test instead of living where nothing can reach it (the A2 review's\ndead-code class); a source guard in the security suite pins that production wires the exported function.\nsetIntegrationCredentialLoader is unchanged as a READ and additionally runs the comparator on every read.\nNo new module, no new tier, no new edge direction: integrations/ -> cofre/ already existed.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (integration credential custody, slice B2): the WS-C join, and the ONE egress truth\nmoving off the artifact that authors it.\n\nNEW api/src/cofre/integration-items.ts - the integration half of the Cofre's own public surface (mint with\nthe connect ceremony's single until_locked grant, the owner-scoped + link-checked lookup, the granted-origin\nscope, unwrapForIntegration, discard). It lives INSIDE cofre/ because cofre/store.ts is lint-fenced\n(COFRE_STORE_BAN): a caller in integrations/ wanting 'the item holding this config's credentials' would\notherwise re-derive both the tenancy filter and the link match - the drift the fence exists to prevent, and\nthe explicit CS5 review outcome. It expresses the join as DATA ({integrationKey, configId}), never as a type\ndependency: cofre/ is the lower tier and must not import integrations/.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/credential-cofre.ts - the Rule-10 SHADOW + COMPARATOR (imports cofre/ + security/\n+ its own definition-registry). service.ts createConfig/updateConfig/deleteConfig mint/rotate/destroy the\nshadow item; nothing about the live read changes until the 2026-08-15 cutover.\n\nSEAM RE-POINTED, not added: server.ts setIntegrationOriginResolver now delegates to\negressOriginsForIntegration - the item's boundOrigins while granted, [] (refuse) once locked, and the old\ndefinition-derived list ONLY for a config with no item. The inline derivation is GONE from the composition\nroot, so the body is exercisable by a test instead of living where nothing can reach it (the A2 review's\ndead-code class); a source guard in the security suite pins that production wires the exported function.\nsetIntegrationCredentialLoader is unchanged as a READ and additionally runs the comparator on every read.\nNo new module, no new tier, no new edge direction: integrations/ -> cofre/ already existed.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (integration credential custody, slice B2): the WS-C join, and the ONE egress truth\nmoving off the artifact that authors it.\n\nNEW api/src/cofre/integration-items.ts - the integration half of the Cofre's own public surface (mint with\nthe connect ceremony's single until_locked grant, the owner-scoped + link-checked lookup, the granted-origin\nscope, unwrapForIntegration, discard). It lives INSIDE cofre/ because cofre/store.ts is lint-fenced\n(COFRE_STORE_BAN): a caller in integrations/ wanting 'the item holding this config's credentials' would\notherwise re-derive both the tenancy filter and the link match - the drift the fence exists to prevent, and\nthe explicit CS5 review outcome. It expresses the join as DATA ({integrationKey, configId}), never as a type\ndependency: cofre/ is the lower tier and must not import integrations/.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/credential-cofre.ts - the Rule-10 SHADOW + COMPARATOR (imports cofre/ + security/\n+ its own definition-registry). service.ts createConfig/updateConfig/deleteConfig mint/rotate/destroy the\nshadow item; nothing about the live read changes until the 2026-08-15 cutover.\n\nSEAM RE-POINTED, not added: server.ts setIntegrationOriginResolver now delegates to\negressOriginsForIntegration - the item's boundOrigins while granted, [] (refuse) once locked, and the old\ndefinition-derived list ONLY for a config with no item. The inline derivation is GONE from the composition\nroot, so the body is exercisable by a test instead of living where nothing can reach it (the A2 review's\ndead-code class); a source guard in the security suite pins that production wires the exported function.\nsetIntegrationCredentialLoader is unchanged as a READ and additionally runs the comparator on every read.\nNo new module, no new tier, no new edge direction: integrations/ -> cofre/ already existed.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
