    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260803-b2-review-org-shared-reach",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 10420,
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1010,
      "height": 420,
      "seed": 1,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (B2 fresh-context review response): THE ORG-SHARED CONFIG REACH, and the loader body.\n\nAn org-shared integration config (ownerUserId == null) is USED by the whole org and DELETED by any org-admin,\nbut its Cofre item belongs to the ONE admin who typed the credentials. B2 left that asymmetry open and it was a\nhole in both directions: a peer's run fell through to the DEFINITION-derived origin list (the author-widenable\nartifact the slice exists to stop trusting, so the admin's credential egressed to a host added after the connect),\nand a peer-admin's delete left the item alive with its until_locked grant, extractable by id through the I9\nprocess-injection primitive.\n\ncofre/integration-items.ts now takes an explicit IntegrationItemAccess {sharedConfig} on three operations -\nintegrationOriginScope, updateIntegrationCredentialValue, discardIntegrationCredentialItem - resolved through the\nSERVER-STAMPED join (org + integrationLink must both agree). The asymmetry is the point: RESTRICTION and\nDESTRUCTION cross the owner boundary, DISCLOSURE does not - unwrapForIntegration takes no flag, so the\n2026-07-27 owner-scoped-credential invariant stands where it was written and the VALUE question stays with the\n2026-08-15 review. cofre/items.ts gains module-internal purgeCofreItem (grants swept for the ITEM's owner, not\nthe deleter); cofre/service.ts splits unwrapResolved out of unwrap so the integration read costs ONE getVisible.\n\negressOriginsForIntegration now REFUSES (empty list) whenever a config carries a join it cannot resolve - the\nitem is the authority, and the definition-derived fallback is for configs with NO item only.\n\nintegrations/service.ts gains persistRotatedCredentials (legacy column, THEN the shadow): the provider-rotation\nwriter, wired into server.ts's Zoho backend which previously wrote the legacy column alone. The credential-loader\nBODY also moves out of server.ts into credential-cofre.loadIntegrationCredentialFields, so the comparator no\nlonger sits inside the read's own catch. No new module, no new tier, no new edge direction.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (B2 fresh-context review response): THE ORG-SHARED CONFIG REACH, and the loader body.\n\nAn org-shared integration config (ownerUserId == null) is USED by the whole org and DELETED by any org-admin,\nbut its Cofre item belongs to the ONE admin who typed the credentials. B2 left that asymmetry open and it was a\nhole in both directions: a peer's run fell through to the DEFINITION-derived origin list (the author-widenable\nartifact the slice exists to stop trusting, so the admin's credential egressed to a host added after the connect),\nand a peer-admin's delete left the item alive with its until_locked grant, extractable by id through the I9\nprocess-injection primitive.\n\ncofre/integration-items.ts now takes an explicit IntegrationItemAccess {sharedConfig} on three operations -\nintegrationOriginScope, updateIntegrationCredentialValue, discardIntegrationCredentialItem - resolved through the\nSERVER-STAMPED join (org + integrationLink must both agree). The asymmetry is the point: RESTRICTION and\nDESTRUCTION cross the owner boundary, DISCLOSURE does not - unwrapForIntegration takes no flag, so the\n2026-07-27 owner-scoped-credential invariant stands where it was written and the VALUE question stays with the\n2026-08-15 review. cofre/items.ts gains module-internal purgeCofreItem (grants swept for the ITEM's owner, not\nthe deleter); cofre/service.ts splits unwrapResolved out of unwrap so the integration read costs ONE getVisible.\n\negressOriginsForIntegration now REFUSES (empty list) whenever a config carries a join it cannot resolve - the\nitem is the authority, and the definition-derived fallback is for configs with NO item only.\n\nintegrations/service.ts gains persistRotatedCredentials (legacy column, THEN the shadow): the provider-rotation\nwriter, wired into server.ts's Zoho backend which previously wrote the legacy column alone. The credential-loader\nBODY also moves out of server.ts into credential-cofre.loadIntegrationCredentialFields, so the comparator no\nlonger sits inside the read's own catch. No new module, no new tier, no new edge direction.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (B2 fresh-context review response): THE ORG-SHARED CONFIG REACH, and the loader body.\n\nAn org-shared integration config (ownerUserId == null) is USED by the whole org and DELETED by any org-admin,\nbut its Cofre item belongs to the ONE admin who typed the credentials. B2 left that asymmetry open and it was a\nhole in both directions: a peer's run fell through to the DEFINITION-derived origin list (the author-widenable\nartifact the slice exists to stop trusting, so the admin's credential egressed to a host added after the connect),\nand a peer-admin's delete left the item alive with its until_locked grant, extractable by id through the I9\nprocess-injection primitive.\n\ncofre/integration-items.ts now takes an explicit IntegrationItemAccess {sharedConfig} on three operations -\nintegrationOriginScope, updateIntegrationCredentialValue, discardIntegrationCredentialItem - resolved through the\nSERVER-STAMPED join (org + integrationLink must both agree). The asymmetry is the point: RESTRICTION and\nDESTRUCTION cross the owner boundary, DISCLOSURE does not - unwrapForIntegration takes no flag, so the\n2026-07-27 owner-scoped-credential invariant stands where it was written and the VALUE question stays with the\n2026-08-15 review. cofre/items.ts gains module-internal purgeCofreItem (grants swept for the ITEM's owner, not\nthe deleter); cofre/service.ts splits unwrapResolved out of unwrap so the integration read costs ONE getVisible.\n\negressOriginsForIntegration now REFUSES (empty list) whenever a config carries a join it cannot resolve - the\nitem is the authority, and the definition-derived fallback is for configs with NO item only.\n\nintegrations/service.ts gains persistRotatedCredentials (legacy column, THEN the shadow): the provider-rotation\nwriter, wired into server.ts's Zoho backend which previously wrote the legacy column alone. The credential-loader\nBODY also moves out of server.ts into credential-cofre.loadIntegrationCredentialFields, so the comparator no\nlonger sits inside the read's own catch. No new module, no new tier, no new edge direction.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
