      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-06 (ekoa-dev peer-parity run) - TWO NEW SERVED-APP PLANES, AND A CAPABILITY VOCABULARY.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/app-email.ts (tier 3, integrations/) - the served-app EMAIL plane,\nmounted at /api/app-email/* by server.ts with resolveAppScope + resolveOwnerOrgId + the workspace\nstatus seam injected (integrations/ never imports apps/). A served page asks WHAT it can send with,\npicks one, and the platform executes it under the OWNER's connection; no token ever reaches the page.\n  GET  /api/app-email/integrations   - email-capable actions + live connected/needsReauth state\n  POST /api/app-email/send           - execute one send through a declared email-capable action\n  POST /api/app-email/draft          - park a provider-side draft for a human to review and send\n  POST /api/app-email/draft/send     - send an existing draft, including edits made in the client\n  GET  /api/app-email/inbox          - the workspace's own mailbox address (a READ)\n\nNEW api/src/apps/app-vision.ts + apps/app-vision-route.ts (tier 4, apps/) - served-app DOCUMENT\nEXTRACTION at POST /api/app-vision/extract, on the SAME admission plane as the assistant. Images go\nto the model; PDFs are read server-side by NEW api/src/services/pdf-text.ts (pdfjs text layer) and a\nSCAN is refused as no_text_layer rather than guessed at. Model egress is the llm/ chokepoint one-shot,\nbilled to the app OWNER (new agentType app-vision-extract). No OCR, deliberately: officeparser v7\nbundles tesseract.js, which fetches trained data at runtime - a second egress path this repo will not\nhave.\n\nNEW api/src/apps/served-app-admission.ts (tier 4, apps/) - the ONE front half the header-scoped apps/\nplanes share (header charset + artifact-backed resolution + owner-activation gate + owner org).\napp-assistant-route.ts and app-vision-route.ts both admit through it; a gate each caller re-implements\nis a gate that drifts.\n\nTHE CAPABILITY VOCABULARY: IntegrationAction gains `capabilities?: string[]` (integrations/\ndefinitions.ts). An action is an email sender because it DECLARES 'email-send', not because it is\nspelled send_email - the coupling this removes is every app hardcoding a per-provider action name.\n'email-draft' / 'email-draft-send' classify the draft pair. It is NOT an authorisation input: what an\naction IS never decides who may run it.\n\nTHE WRITE GATE STILL BINDS, AND THAT IS THE DIVERGENCE FROM UPSTREAM. ekoa-dev's version of this\nplane dispatches with a synthesised admin actor and no gate, so a served page could send mail as the\nworkspace unconditionally. Here a send is a WRITE: app-email passes the OWNER as actingUserId to\ncallPlatformIntegration, C2's consent gate answers first, and an unapproved send is refused with\nawaiting_consent and ZERO provider traffic. Both providers' drafts write to the mailbox and are gated\ntoo; only get_profile joins the read allowlist.\n\nPorted from dev-madrid commits 1d4eaf64 + fd209f70 + c4f7f2c6, none of which were ever pushed to\nGitHub - see docs/dev-parity.md, whose audit now fetches peer checkouts for exactly that reason.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-06 (ekoa-dev peer-parity run) - TWO NEW SERVED-APP PLANES, AND A CAPABILITY VOCABULARY.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/app-email.ts (tier 3, integrations/) - the served-app EMAIL plane,\nmounted at /api/app-email/* by server.ts with resolveAppScope + resolveOwnerOrgId + the workspace\nstatus seam injected (integrations/ never imports apps/). A served page asks WHAT it can send with,\npicks one, and the platform executes it under the OWNER's connection; no token ever reaches the page.\n  GET  /api/app-email/integrations   - email-capable actions + live connected/needsReauth state\n  POST /api/app-email/send           - execute one send through a declared email-capable action\n  POST /api/app-email/draft          - park a provider-side draft for a human to review and send\n  POST /api/app-email/draft/send     - send an existing draft, including edits made in the client\n  GET  /api/app-email/inbox          - the workspace's own mailbox address (a READ)\n\nNEW api/src/apps/app-vision.ts + apps/app-vision-route.ts (tier 4, apps/) - served-app DOCUMENT\nEXTRACTION at POST /api/app-vision/extract, on the SAME admission plane as the assistant. Images go\nto the model; PDFs are read server-side by NEW api/src/services/pdf-text.ts (pdfjs text layer) and a\nSCAN is refused as no_text_layer rather than guessed at. Model egress is the llm/ chokepoint one-shot,\nbilled to the app OWNER (new agentType app-vision-extract). No OCR, deliberately: officeparser v7\nbundles tesseract.js, which fetches trained data at runtime - a second egress path this repo will not\nhave.\n\nNEW api/src/apps/served-app-admission.ts (tier 4, apps/) - the ONE front half the header-scoped apps/\nplanes share (header charset + artifact-backed resolution + owner-activation gate + owner org).\napp-assistant-route.ts and app-vision-route.ts both admit through it; a gate each caller re-implements\nis a gate that drifts.\n\nTHE CAPABILITY VOCABULARY: IntegrationAction gains `capabilities?: string[]` (integrations/\ndefinitions.ts). An action is an email sender because it DECLARES 'email-send', not because it is\nspelled send_email - the coupling this removes is every app hardcoding a per-provider action name.\n'email-draft' / 'email-draft-send' classify the draft pair. It is NOT an authorisation input: what an\naction IS never decides who may run it.\n\nTHE WRITE GATE STILL BINDS, AND THAT IS THE DIVERGENCE FROM UPSTREAM. ekoa-dev's version of this\nplane dispatches with a synthesised admin actor and no gate, so a served page could send mail as the\nworkspace unconditionally. Here a send is a WRITE: app-email passes the OWNER as actingUserId to\ncallPlatformIntegration, C2's consent gate answers first, and an unapproved send is refused with\nawaiting_consent and ZERO provider traffic. Both providers' drafts write to the mailbox and are gated\ntoo; only get_profile joins the read allowlist.\n\nPorted from dev-madrid commits 1d4eaf64 + fd209f70 + c4f7f2c6, none of which were ever pushed to\nGitHub - see docs/dev-parity.md, whose audit now fetches peer checkouts for exactly that reason.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-06 (ekoa-dev peer-parity run) - TWO NEW SERVED-APP PLANES, AND A CAPABILITY VOCABULARY.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/app-email.ts (tier 3, integrations/) - the served-app EMAIL plane,\nmounted at /api/app-email/* by server.ts with resolveAppScope + resolveOwnerOrgId + the workspace\nstatus seam injected (integrations/ never imports apps/). A served page asks WHAT it can send with,\npicks one, and the platform executes it under the OWNER's connection; no token ever reaches the page.\n  GET  /api/app-email/integrations   - email-capable actions + live connected/needsReauth state\n  POST /api/app-email/send           - execute one send through a declared email-capable action\n  POST /api/app-email/draft          - park a provider-side draft for a human to review and send\n  POST /api/app-email/draft/send     - send an existing draft, including edits made in the client\n  GET  /api/app-email/inbox          - the workspace's own mailbox address (a READ)\n\nNEW api/src/apps/app-vision.ts + apps/app-vision-route.ts (tier 4, apps/) - served-app DOCUMENT\nEXTRACTION at POST /api/app-vision/extract, on the SAME admission plane as the assistant. Images go\nto the model; PDFs are read server-side by NEW api/src/services/pdf-text.ts (pdfjs text layer) and a\nSCAN is refused as no_text_layer rather than guessed at. Model egress is the llm/ chokepoint one-shot,\nbilled to the app OWNER (new agentType app-vision-extract). No OCR, deliberately: officeparser v7\nbundles tesseract.js, which fetches trained data at runtime - a second egress path this repo will not\nhave.\n\nNEW api/src/apps/served-app-admission.ts (tier 4, apps/) - the ONE front half the header-scoped apps/\nplanes share (header charset + artifact-backed resolution + owner-activation gate + owner org).\napp-assistant-route.ts and app-vision-route.ts both admit through it; a gate each caller re-implements\nis a gate that drifts.\n\nTHE CAPABILITY VOCABULARY: IntegrationAction gains `capabilities?: string[]` (integrations/\ndefinitions.ts). An action is an email sender because it DECLARES 'email-send', not because it is\nspelled send_email - the coupling this removes is every app hardcoding a per-provider action name.\n'email-draft' / 'email-draft-send' classify the draft pair. It is NOT an authorisation input: what an\naction IS never decides who may run it.\n\nTHE WRITE GATE STILL BINDS, AND THAT IS THE DIVERGENCE FROM UPSTREAM. ekoa-dev's version of this\nplane dispatches with a synthesised admin actor and no gate, so a served page could send mail as the\nworkspace unconditionally. Here a send is a WRITE: app-email passes the OWNER as actingUserId to\ncallPlatformIntegration, C2's consent gate answers first, and an unapproved send is refused with\nawaiting_consent and ZERO provider traffic. Both providers' drafts write to the mailbox and are gated\ntoo; only get_profile joins the read allowlist.\n\nPorted from dev-madrid commits 1d4eaf64 + fd209f70 + c4f7f2c6, none of which were ever pushed to\nGitHub - see docs/dev-parity.md, whose audit now fetches peer checkouts for exactly that reason.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 837462951,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "annot-uploads-ws4a-20260808",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 13643,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 370,
      "seed": 384756219,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1754630400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS4a, chat-attachment upload staging): api/src/uploads/ is a NEW tier-3 domain module\n(knowledge/'s family - imports data/ + config only, no llm/ path) behind routes/uploads.ts, mounted by\nserver.ts at /api/v1/uploads (auth: 'user' - platform session only, no gateway-key admission).\nshared/src/uploads.ts's POST create was declared but never mounted (mount-coverage.test.ts's DESCOPED set);\nthis slice mounts it and shrinks that list.\n\nTwo files. paths.ts is the path-resolution point - per-USER, not per-org:\n<EKOA_DATA_DIR>/uploads/<userId>/<uploadId>/<file> for a single upload, .../folders/<folder>/<relPath> for a\npicked-folder batch. filename/folder segments are sanitized; uploadId/userId are server-generated so\ninherently path-safe. service.ts does the blob write (stageUpload) and two reads: resolveUpload (uploadId ->\nabsolute path, single-file uploads only) and stageRunAttachments - the fix for the 'text-attachments' run\nclass's long-documented gap (agents/tools.ts's DOCX_TOOLS comment used to say it 'mounts no in-process tools\nand has no attachment-path plumbing'). agents/chat.ts now copies a chat run's referenced blobs into a FRESH\ntemp dir and points the Agent SDK subprocess's cwd/homeDir at it (the F25 sandbox convention, llm/client.ts)\n- never the user's whole upload history - and discards it through the run's existing cleanup() path.\n\nClient-side, the same slice closes a second bug: chat-runtime.tsx and useAgentExecution.ts were sending the\ncomposer's CLIENT-side chip id (FileAttachment.attachmentId) as the wire uploadId instead of the real\nserver-issued id (FileAttachment.path) - every attachment silently failed to resolve even before this\nendpoint existed to answer it.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS4a, chat-attachment upload staging): api/src/uploads/ is a NEW tier-3 domain module\n(knowledge/'s family - imports data/ + config only, no llm/ path) behind routes/uploads.ts, mounted by\nserver.ts at /api/v1/uploads (auth: 'user' - platform session only, no gateway-key admission).\nshared/src/uploads.ts's POST create was declared but never mounted (mount-coverage.test.ts's DESCOPED set);\nthis slice mounts it and shrinks that list.\n\nTwo files. paths.ts is the path-resolution point - per-USER, not per-org:\n<EKOA_DATA_DIR>/uploads/<userId>/<uploadId>/<file> for a single upload, .../folders/<folder>/<relPath> for a\npicked-folder batch. filename/folder segments are sanitized; uploadId/userId are server-generated so\ninherently path-safe. service.ts does the blob write (stageUpload) and two reads: resolveUpload (uploadId ->\nabsolute path, single-file uploads only) and stageRunAttachments - the fix for the 'text-attachments' run\nclass's long-documented gap (agents/tools.ts's DOCX_TOOLS comment used to say it 'mounts no in-process tools\nand has no attachment-path plumbing'). agents/chat.ts now copies a chat run's referenced blobs into a FRESH\ntemp dir and points the Agent SDK subprocess's cwd/homeDir at it (the F25 sandbox convention, llm/client.ts)\n- never the user's whole upload history - and discards it through the run's existing cleanup() path.\n\nClient-side, the same slice closes a second bug: chat-runtime.tsx and useAgentExecution.ts were sending the\ncomposer's CLIENT-side chip id (FileAttachment.attachmentId) as the wire uploadId instead of the real\nserver-issued id (FileAttachment.path) - every attachment silently failed to resolve even before this\nendpoint existed to answer it.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS4a, chat-attachment upload staging): api/src/uploads/ is a NEW tier-3 domain module\n(knowledge/'s family - imports data/ + config only, no llm/ path) behind routes/uploads.ts, mounted by\nserver.ts at /api/v1/uploads (auth: 'user' - platform session only, no gateway-key admission).\nshared/src/uploads.ts's POST create was declared but never mounted (mount-coverage.test.ts's DESCOPED set);\nthis slice mounts it and shrinks that list.\n\nTwo files. paths.ts is the path-resolution point - per-USER, not per-org:\n<EKOA_DATA_DIR>/uploads/<userId>/<uploadId>/<file> for a single upload, .../folders/<folder>/<relPath> for a\npicked-folder batch. filename/folder segments are sanitized; uploadId/userId are server-generated so\ninherently path-safe. service.ts does the blob write (stageUpload) and two reads: resolveUpload (uploadId ->\nabsolute path, single-file uploads only) and stageRunAttachments - the fix for the 'text-attachments' run\nclass's long-documented gap (agents/tools.ts's DOCX_TOOLS comment used to say it 'mounts no in-process tools\nand has no attachment-path plumbing'). agents/chat.ts now copies a chat run's referenced blobs into a FRESH\ntemp dir and points the Agent SDK subprocess's cwd/homeDir at it (the F25 sandbox convention, llm/client.ts)\n- never the user's whole upload history - and discards it through the run's existing cleanup() path.\n\nClient-side, the same slice closes a second bug: chat-runtime.tsx and useAgentExecution.ts were sending the\ncomposer's CLIENT-side chip id (FileAttachment.attachmentId) as the wire uploadId instead of the real\nserver-issued id (FileAttachment.path) - every attachment silently failed to resolve even before this\nendpoint existed to answer it.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2039374758,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "annot-salomao-s1-s2-2026-08-14",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 14053,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 820,
      "height": 245.0,
      "seed": 2050480981,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786748302501,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-14 (salomao migration S1+S2):\n- S1: server.ts (composition root) now CONSTRUCTS WorkerThreadRuntime and calls\n  setArtifactBackendRuntime - the backend-runtime module's Null default is finally replaced at\n  boot (findings artifact-backend-runtime-never-wired, closed). Seams bound there and ONLY there:\n  appData -> AppDataAccess; model -> llm/ public entry (completeFast, user_work\n  'artifact-backend:<entrypoint>', billed to the artifact owner); notify.email -> the\n  consent-gated app-email plane with the OWNER as actor; notify.inApp -> notifications SSE.\n  resolveOwner/resolveBundlePath stay on the runtime's own defaults. No integration seam.\n  Disposed on shutdown + factory re-composition (fail-closed back to the Null runtime).\n- S2: events/service.ts createTrigger now READS integrations/event-sources/platform-poll\n  (platformListenerConfig) to stamp kind:'listener' + pollConfig at CREATE for platform\n  providers - the create path feeds the listener supervisor's poll loop, not only webhook\n  ingress. (tests: apps/backend-runtime-wiring, events/trigger-create-inference,\n  contract/triggers-listener-create)",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-14 (salomao migration S1+S2):\n- S1: server.ts (composition root) now CONSTRUCTS WorkerThreadRuntime and calls\n  setArtifactBackendRuntime - the backend-runtime module's Null default is finally replaced at\n  boot (findings artifact-backend-runtime-never-wired, closed). Seams bound there and ONLY there:\n  appData -> AppDataAccess; model -> llm/ public entry (completeFast, user_work\n  'artifact-backend:<entrypoint>', billed to the artifact owner); notify.email -> the\n  consent-gated app-email plane with the OWNER as actor; notify.inApp -> notifications SSE.\n  resolveOwner/resolveBundlePath stay on the runtime's own defaults. No integration seam.\n  Disposed on shutdown + factory re-composition (fail-closed back to the Null runtime).\n- S2: events/service.ts createTrigger now READS integrations/event-sources/platform-poll\n  (platformListenerConfig) to stamp kind:'listener' + pollConfig at CREATE for platform\n  providers - the create path feeds the listener supervisor's poll loop, not only webhook\n  ingress. (tests: apps/backend-runtime-wiring, events/trigger-create-inference,\n  contract/triggers-listener-create)",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-14 (salomao migration S1+S2):\n- S1: server.ts (composition root) now CONSTRUCTS WorkerThreadRuntime and calls\n  setArtifactBackendRuntime - the backend-runtime module's Null default is finally replaced at\n  boot (findings artifact-backend-runtime-never-wired, closed). Seams bound there and ONLY there:\n  appData -> AppDataAccess; model -> llm/ public entry (completeFast, user_work\n  'artifact-backend:<entrypoint>', billed to the artifact owner); notify.email -> the\n  consent-gated app-email plane with the OWNER as actor; notify.inApp -> notifications SSE.\n  resolveOwner/resolveBundlePath stay on the runtime's own defaults. No integration seam.\n  Disposed on shutdown + factory re-composition (fail-closed back to the Null runtime).\n- S2: events/service.ts createTrigger now READS integrations/event-sources/platform-poll\n  (platformListenerConfig) to stamp kind:'listener' + pollConfig at CREATE for platform\n  providers - the create path feeds the listener supervisor's poll loop, not only webhook\n  ingress. (tests: apps/backend-runtime-wiring, events/trigger-create-inference,\n  contract/triggers-listener-create)",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608171,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "annot-schedules-20260817",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 14358.0,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 332.5,
      "seed": 202608172,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755442800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-17 (schedules): api/src/schedules/ is a NEW TIER-4 rail beside events/ - the timer rail.\nONE Schedule entity (one-time + recurring; recurrence self-rolled on Intl, IANA wall-clock, DST pinned by\ntests/schedules/recurrence.test.ts) firing a target union: manual (pending human task), automation (via the\ninjected startRunForTrigger seam, triggeredBy:'schedule' - both unions widened additively), and\nintegration_action (via the injected executeUserIntegrationAction seam + the ONE runAutomationBackedAction\nbinding; awaiting_consent -> a 'blocked' run, never approved or retried from here). Files: recurrence.ts\n(pure math), store.ts (schedules + schedule_runs over data/stores), service.ts (validation + wire),\nsupervisor.ts (30s tick; deterministic run-id insert per (schedule, occurrence) = at-most-once claim;\npointer advances BEFORE execution; no backfill past a 5-min grace, measured from FIRST SIGHT of the\noccurrence so the supervisor's own backpressure cannot drop the tail of the due list - a pass with every\nfire slot busy DEFERS the rest to the next tick, never blocks on a fire; stale recovery adopts the present\nin ONE pointer jump (not one cadence step per tick); a missed `once`, having no next occurrence, lands a\nterminal failed/missed run row instead of vanishing; stop() drains the pass in flight then every fire, so\nno claimed occurrence is orphaned in `running`; 20-strike auto-pause), routes/schedules.ts\n(user-or-key, whole family). Wired ONLY in server.ts: configureScheduleSupervisor (two one-liner seams),\nmount at /api/v1/schedules, started post-listen, stopped in shutdown; env kill EKOA_SCHEDULES_DISABLED=1.\nLint: schedules/ added to the never-import-routes/server zone + a zone banning automation/agents/apps\nimports (seams only). Suites: recurrence + supervisor units, contract/schedules.test.ts (both admissions),\nsecurity/schedules-isolation.test.ts (Rule 5 memvault class). decisions.md 2026-08-17.",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-17 (schedules): api/src/schedules/ is a NEW TIER-4 rail beside events/ - the timer rail.\nONE Schedule entity (one-time + recurring; recurrence self-rolled on Intl, IANA wall-clock, DST pinned by\ntests/schedules/recurrence.test.ts) firing a target union: manual (pending human task), automation (via the\ninjected startRunForTrigger seam, triggeredBy:'schedule' - both unions widened additively), and\nintegration_action (via the injected executeUserIntegrationAction seam + the ONE runAutomationBackedAction\nbinding; awaiting_consent -> a 'blocked' run, never approved or retried from here). Files: recurrence.ts\n(pure math), store.ts (schedules + schedule_runs over data/stores), service.ts (validation + wire),\nsupervisor.ts (30s tick; deterministic run-id insert per (schedule, occurrence) = at-most-once claim;\npointer advances BEFORE execution; no backfill past a 5-min grace, measured from FIRST SIGHT of the\noccurrence so the supervisor's own backpressure cannot drop the tail of the due list - a pass with every\nfire slot busy DEFERS the rest to the next tick, never blocks on a fire; stale recovery adopts the present\nin ONE pointer jump (not one cadence step per tick); a missed `once`, having no next occurrence, lands a\nterminal failed/missed run row instead of vanishing; stop() drains the pass in flight then every fire, so\nno claimed occurrence is orphaned in `running`; 20-strike auto-pause), routes/schedules.ts\n(user-or-key, whole family). Wired ONLY in server.ts: configureScheduleSupervisor (two one-liner seams),\nmount at /api/v1/schedules, started post-listen, stopped in shutdown; env kill EKOA_SCHEDULES_DISABLED=1.\nLint: schedules/ added to the never-import-routes/server zone + a zone banning automation/agents/apps\nimports (seams only). Suites: recurrence + supervisor units, contract/schedules.test.ts (both admissions),\nsecurity/schedules-isolation.test.ts (Rule 5 memvault class). decisions.md 2026-08-17.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-17 (schedules): api/src/schedules/ is a NEW TIER-4 rail beside events/ - the timer rail.\nONE Schedule entity (one-time + recurring; recurrence self-rolled on Intl, IANA wall-clock, DST pinned by\ntests/schedules/recurrence.test.ts) firing a target union: manual (pending human task), automation (via the\ninjected startRunForTrigger seam, triggeredBy:'schedule' - both unions widened additively), and\nintegration_action (via the injected executeUserIntegrationAction seam + the ONE runAutomationBackedAction\nbinding; awaiting_consent -> a 'blocked' run, never approved or retried from here). Files: recurrence.ts\n(pure math), store.ts (schedules + schedule_runs over data/stores), service.ts (validation + wire),\nsupervisor.ts (30s tick; deterministic run-id insert per (schedule, occurrence) = at-most-once claim;\npointer advances BEFORE execution; no backfill past a 5-min grace, measured from FIRST SIGHT of the\noccurrence so the supervisor's own backpressure cannot drop the tail of the due list - a pass with every\nfire slot busy DEFERS the rest to the next tick, never blocks on a fire; stale recovery adopts the present\nin ONE pointer jump (not one cadence step per tick); a missed `once`, having no next occurrence, lands a\nterminal failed/missed run row instead of vanishing; stop() drains the pass in flight then every fire, so\nno claimed occurrence is orphaned in `running`; 20-strike auto-pause), routes/schedules.ts\n(user-or-key, whole family). Wired ONLY in server.ts: configureScheduleSupervisor (two one-liner seams),\nmount at /api/v1/schedules, started post-listen, stopped in shutdown; env kill EKOA_SCHEDULES_DISABLED=1.\nLint: schedules/ added to the never-import-routes/server zone + a zone banning automation/agents/apps\nimports (seams only). Suites: recurrence + supervisor units, contract/schedules.test.ts (both admissions),\nsecurity/schedules-isolation.test.ts (Rule 5 memvault class). decisions.md 2026-08-17.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
