      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (schedules: preview anchor + the declared run filter). POST /preview gained an\noptional scheduleId, so the endpoint is no longer store-free: service.previewSpec reads the row through\nstore.getSchedule (actor-scoped; an unreadable id answers the uniform NOT_FOUND, so preview is no wider\nan oracle than GET /:id) and anchors the occurrence math on its createdAt - the SAME anchor\nsupervisor.advance and the PATCH recompute use, so the edit dialog can only show instants the\nsupervisor will fire. Without the id the anchor stays the request instant (the create form, where no row\nexists yet). The anchor is deliberately not a body timestamp: a caller-chosen anchor would be a second\nsource of occurrence truth. GET /:id/runs now forwards the WHOLE declared ScheduleRunListQuery (status\nAND limit) to store.listRunsForSchedule, which filters before the slice - the org feed's shape. Spec\nregenerated (docs/openapi) + cortex-cli regenerated; pinned by contract/schedules.test.ts.",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (schedules: preview anchor + the declared run filter). POST /preview gained an\noptional scheduleId, so the endpoint is no longer store-free: service.previewSpec reads the row through\nstore.getSchedule (actor-scoped; an unreadable id answers the uniform NOT_FOUND, so preview is no wider\nan oracle than GET /:id) and anchors the occurrence math on its createdAt - the SAME anchor\nsupervisor.advance and the PATCH recompute use, so the edit dialog can only show instants the\nsupervisor will fire. Without the id the anchor stays the request instant (the create form, where no row\nexists yet). The anchor is deliberately not a body timestamp: a caller-chosen anchor would be a second\nsource of occurrence truth. GET /:id/runs now forwards the WHOLE declared ScheduleRunListQuery (status\nAND limit) to store.listRunsForSchedule, which filters before the slice - the org feed's shape. Spec\nregenerated (docs/openapi) + cortex-cli regenerated; pinned by contract/schedules.test.ts.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (schedules: preview anchor + the declared run filter). POST /preview gained an\noptional scheduleId, so the endpoint is no longer store-free: service.previewSpec reads the row through\nstore.getSchedule (actor-scoped; an unreadable id answers the uniform NOT_FOUND, so preview is no wider\nan oracle than GET /:id) and anchors the occurrence math on its createdAt - the SAME anchor\nsupervisor.advance and the PATCH recompute use, so the edit dialog can only show instants the\nsupervisor will fire. Without the id the anchor stays the request instant (the create form, where no row\nexists yet). The anchor is deliberately not a body timestamp: a caller-chosen anchor would be a second\nsource of occurrence truth. GET /:id/runs now forwards the WHOLE declared ScheduleRunListQuery (status\nAND limit) to store.listRunsForSchedule, which filters before the slice - the org feed's shape. Spec\nregenerated (docs/openapi) + cortex-cli regenerated; pinned by contract/schedules.test.ts.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
