      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 (b) - P2 RE-CUT. SUPERSEDES the P2.1-P2.4 note above, which described a spine no\nproduction path could reach. Read this one; that one is the record of what was tried.\n\nWHAT CHANGED, AND WHY. The first cut built a SECOND driving loop - a goal-driven exploration pass\n(discovery.ts + discovery-goal-verify.ts + discovery-service.ts) that authored a recipe. Nothing in the\nproduct called it: runAutomationForAction always has an automation binding, so a goal loop had no entry,\nand the replay it fed could therefore never find a recipe. Those three modules are DELETED. The learning\npass is now the ordinary automation run, instrumented - which costs one extra frame instead of a second\nexpensive pass, and which rehearsal.ts already adapts when the site's UI moves.\n\nTHE ONE LOOP. api/src/automation/service.ts runAutomationForAction is the whole spine:\n  1. REPLAY the compiled recipe (replay-action.ts -> executors/injected-call.ts). ok short-circuits;\n     write-gate REFUSES; everything else falls through, so the worst case is the run as it was pre-P2.\n  2. RUN the authored automation with observeNetwork armed - the NEW ENGINE SEAM below.\n  3. COMPILE what the page fetched (network-capture.ts, model-free) and store it: putRecipe normally,\n     supersedeRecipe (self-heal.ts) when step 1 reported drift. Nothing is written when the run failed or\n     captured no internal API call, so a bad pass never becomes a permanent bad recipe.\n\nNEW SEAMS\n  RunAutomationOptions.observeNetwork (api/src/automation/engine.ts)\n    A sink the run hands its captured exchanges to, on the way out, whatever its outcome - the CALLER\n    decides whether the pass is worth compiling from. Armed lazily, and only before a step whose type\n    drives a page: arming takes the machine's lease, so an api_call-only automation must not pay for one.\n  automationBackedActionHandler (api/src/automation/service.ts)\n    The ONE mapping from the integrations executor's automation seam onto a run. It moved out of\n    server.ts because WHICH fields cross it is a security decision - the action's identity and the\n    owner's writeAssent both ride it - and a mapping inside the composition root is one no test can\n    enter through. server.ts binds it; the acceptance suite enters through it.\n  ProfileManager.onLeaseEnd (clients/bridge/src/browser/profile.ts)\n    Per-lease cleanup registered by whoever creates a per-lease holding. releaseRun is the single funnel\n    for ALL THREE ways a lease ends - the explicit frame, the idle backstop, and closeAll at shutdown -\n    and the network recorder (which holds live header VALUES) registers here at the moment it is armed.\n    Wiring only the frame handler, as the first cut did, left the values resident on the two silent routes.\n\nSTILL AS DESCRIBED ABOVE: network-capture.ts, response-shape.ts, recipe.ts, the two stores, the machine\nhalf (capture.ts / inject.ts), and the values-never-cross-the-wire property.\n\nTIGHTENED IN THE REPLAY (executors/injected-call.ts)\n  - POSTURE IS PER CALL. classify is a FUNCTION asked about each call's own origin, and the whole ladder\n    is resolved before the first call is sent. A permissive first hop no longer authorises server-side\n    egress to the third-party host a later hop targets.\n  - THE WRITE GATE HAS A KEY. writeAssent comes from integrations/action-consent.ts via the seam, and it\n    is true only when a human approved a MUTATING action (not_mutating is not an approval). The gate also\n    covers SCRIPTED DOM STEPS, which the first cut replayed with no gate at all.\n  - AN ARGUMENT MAY NOT WIDEN OR REDIRECT A CALL. A hole the run did not supply refuses (rendering it ''\n    turns ?ref={{input.ref}} into ?ref=, which most APIs read as \"everything\"), and a resolved URL whose\n    origin differs from the template's literal origin refuses.",
