      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 (d) - P2 ROUND FOUR: WHAT DISCOVERY MAY WRITE DOWN. AMENDS (c). (c) settled where\nthe replay EXECUTES; this settles which recipes may exist at all. Every item is a way of learning\nsomething confidently wrong rather than a way of failing.\n\n1. A RECIPE MAY NOT BE A SUBSET OF ITS ACTION.\n   A `mutates` action's pass captures the READS its page made - the write is a form post, or answers\n   HTML, or has a login-shaped body the compile drops. The read-only recipe was stored, and every\n   later run replayed it, answered ok, and reported SUCCESS while the write never happened.\n   NEW FACT ON THE SEAM: IntegrationAction.mutates, carried\n     action-executor.ts -> AutomationBackedHandler.mutates\n     -> service.ts automationBackedActionHandler -> ActionRunInput.mutates\n     -> replay-action.ts ReplayActionInput.mutates -> executors/injected-call.ts ReplayInput.mutates\n   It is NOT writeAssent. An assent is a fact about a human; mutates is a fact about the action.\n   TWO REFUSALS, one rule from both sides:\n     learnFromRun     refuses a compile with NO write for a mutating action (and still refuses one\n                      WITH a write, for any action) - so a mutating action stores no recipe at all.\n     replayCompiled-  answers the new outcome `does-not-cover` for a stored one, which the mount\n       Action         CLEARS and falls through on, loudly, to the authored steps that DO write.\n   self-heal.classifyReplayDrift maps does-not-cover -> refused: re-driving the same steps would\n   re-capture the same read-only traffic, so a heal must not route around it.\n\n2. AN ARGUMENT FILLS A VALUE; IT DOES NOT CHOOSE AN ENDPOINT.\n   fillCall interpolated the whole template then compared origins, so `/cases/{{input.id}}` with\n   `id=../../admin/secrets` reached `/admin/secrets` - same origin, different endpoint, inside the\n   user's live authenticated page. The URL is now templated and filled COMPONENT-WISE:\n     network-capture.templateUrl   origin copied literally, never offered a hole; query NAMES\n                                   literal; holes only in path segments and query values.\n     injected-call.parseUrlTemplate  splits by grammar, NOT with new URL - `{` and `}` are in the\n                                   WHATWG path percent-encode set, so parsing a template turned every\n                                   PATH hole into %7B%7B..%7D%7D (query holes survived, which is why\n                                   no suite saw it). Refuses userinfo, a non-http scheme, a hole in\n                                   the origin, a hole in a parameter name, a non-input placeholder.\n     injected-call.renderUrlTemplate  percent-encodes every hole value, then proves the result\n                                   against a CONTROL render of the same template with the arguments\n                                   taken out: structureOf(actual) === structureOf(control), plus a\n                                   hole-value guard (an empty, `.` or `..` segment is refused).\n     renderBodyTemplate            JSON-escapes into a JSON body and re-parses it; percent-encodes\n                                   otherwise. A `\"` in an argument cannot open a sibling field.\n\n3. AN ARGUMENT THE PASS COULD NOT FIND REFUSES THE COMPILE.\n   compileInjectedCalls now answers {calls, refusedBecause?} instead of a bare list. An input that\n   was located in no compiled URL or body would have made the call a CONSTANT - later runs returning\n   the first run's data whatever the caller asked. A non-scalar argument refuses for the same reason.\n\n4. EVIDENCE IS DURABLE ONLY IF THE RECIPE IS.\n   Order stays evidence-then-recipe (the recipe points INTO the evidence), and the orphan that order\n   creates is now COLLECTED: learnFromRun drops the evidence it just wrote when the write did not\n   land - which is the COMMON case, since putRecipe refuses to overwrite by design. One helper,\n   discardEvidence, serves both ends of the lifecycle.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 (d) - P2 ROUND FOUR: WHAT DISCOVERY MAY WRITE DOWN. AMENDS (c). (c) settled where\nthe replay EXECUTES; this settles which recipes may exist at all. Every item is a way of learning\nsomething confidently wrong rather than a way of failing.\n\n1. A RECIPE MAY NOT BE A SUBSET OF ITS ACTION.\n   A `mutates` action's pass captures the READS its page made - the write is a form post, or answers\n   HTML, or has a login-shaped body the compile drops. The read-only recipe was stored, and every\n   later run replayed it, answered ok, and reported SUCCESS while the write never happened.\n   NEW FACT ON THE SEAM: IntegrationAction.mutates, carried\n     action-executor.ts -> AutomationBackedHandler.mutates\n     -> service.ts automationBackedActionHandler -> ActionRunInput.mutates\n     -> replay-action.ts ReplayActionInput.mutates -> executors/injected-call.ts ReplayInput.mutates\n   It is NOT writeAssent. An assent is a fact about a human; mutates is a fact about the action.\n   TWO REFUSALS, one rule from both sides:\n     learnFromRun     refuses a compile with NO write for a mutating action (and still refuses one\n                      WITH a write, for any action) - so a mutating action stores no recipe at all.\n     replayCompiled-  answers the new outcome `does-not-cover` for a stored one, which the mount\n       Action         CLEARS and falls through on, loudly, to the authored steps that DO write.\n   self-heal.classifyReplayDrift maps does-not-cover -> refused: re-driving the same steps would\n   re-capture the same read-only traffic, so a heal must not route around it.\n\n2. AN ARGUMENT FILLS A VALUE; IT DOES NOT CHOOSE AN ENDPOINT.\n   fillCall interpolated the whole template then compared origins, so `/cases/{{input.id}}` with\n   `id=../../admin/secrets` reached `/admin/secrets` - same origin, different endpoint, inside the\n   user's live authenticated page. The URL is now templated and filled COMPONENT-WISE:\n     network-capture.templateUrl   origin copied literally, never offered a hole; query NAMES\n                                   literal; holes only in path segments and query values.\n     injected-call.parseUrlTemplate  splits by grammar, NOT with new URL - `{` and `}` are in the\n                                   WHATWG path percent-encode set, so parsing a template turned every\n                                   PATH hole into %7B%7B..%7D%7D (query holes survived, which is why\n                                   no suite saw it). Refuses userinfo, a non-http scheme, a hole in\n                                   the origin, a hole in a parameter name, a non-input placeholder.\n     injected-call.renderUrlTemplate  percent-encodes every hole value, then proves the result\n                                   against a CONTROL render of the same template with the arguments\n                                   taken out: structureOf(actual) === structureOf(control), plus a\n                                   hole-value guard (an empty, `.` or `..` segment is refused).\n     renderBodyTemplate            JSON-escapes into a JSON body and re-parses it; percent-encodes\n                                   otherwise. A `\"` in an argument cannot open a sibling field.\n\n3. AN ARGUMENT THE PASS COULD NOT FIND REFUSES THE COMPILE.\n   compileInjectedCalls now answers {calls, refusedBecause?} instead of a bare list. An input that\n   was located in no compiled URL or body would have made the call a CONSTANT - later runs returning\n   the first run's data whatever the caller asked. A non-scalar argument refuses for the same reason.\n\n4. EVIDENCE IS DURABLE ONLY IF THE RECIPE IS.\n   Order stays evidence-then-recipe (the recipe points INTO the evidence), and the orphan that order\n   creates is now COLLECTED: learnFromRun drops the evidence it just wrote when the write did not\n   land - which is the COMMON case, since putRecipe refuses to overwrite by design. One helper,\n   discardEvidence, serves both ends of the lifecycle.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 (d) - P2 ROUND FOUR: WHAT DISCOVERY MAY WRITE DOWN. AMENDS (c). (c) settled where\nthe replay EXECUTES; this settles which recipes may exist at all. Every item is a way of learning\nsomething confidently wrong rather than a way of failing.\n\n1. A RECIPE MAY NOT BE A SUBSET OF ITS ACTION.\n   A `mutates` action's pass captures the READS its page made - the write is a form post, or answers\n   HTML, or has a login-shaped body the compile drops. The read-only recipe was stored, and every\n   later run replayed it, answered ok, and reported SUCCESS while the write never happened.\n   NEW FACT ON THE SEAM: IntegrationAction.mutates, carried\n     action-executor.ts -> AutomationBackedHandler.mutates\n     -> service.ts automationBackedActionHandler -> ActionRunInput.mutates\n     -> replay-action.ts ReplayActionInput.mutates -> executors/injected-call.ts ReplayInput.mutates\n   It is NOT writeAssent. An assent is a fact about a human; mutates is a fact about the action.\n   TWO REFUSALS, one rule from both sides:\n     learnFromRun     refuses a compile with NO write for a mutating action (and still refuses one\n                      WITH a write, for any action) - so a mutating action stores no recipe at all.\n     replayCompiled-  answers the new outcome `does-not-cover` for a stored one, which the mount\n       Action         CLEARS and falls through on, loudly, to the authored steps that DO write.\n   self-heal.classifyReplayDrift maps does-not-cover -> refused: re-driving the same steps would\n   re-capture the same read-only traffic, so a heal must not route around it.\n\n2. AN ARGUMENT FILLS A VALUE; IT DOES NOT CHOOSE AN ENDPOINT.\n   fillCall interpolated the whole template then compared origins, so `/cases/{{input.id}}` with\n   `id=../../admin/secrets` reached `/admin/secrets` - same origin, different endpoint, inside the\n   user's live authenticated page. The URL is now templated and filled COMPONENT-WISE:\n     network-capture.templateUrl   origin copied literally, never offered a hole; query NAMES\n                                   literal; holes only in path segments and query values.\n     injected-call.parseUrlTemplate  splits by grammar, NOT with new URL - `{` and `}` are in the\n                                   WHATWG path percent-encode set, so parsing a template turned every\n                                   PATH hole into %7B%7B..%7D%7D (query holes survived, which is why\n                                   no suite saw it). Refuses userinfo, a non-http scheme, a hole in\n                                   the origin, a hole in a parameter name, a non-input placeholder.\n     injected-call.renderUrlTemplate  percent-encodes every hole value, then proves the result\n                                   against a CONTROL render of the same template with the arguments\n                                   taken out: structureOf(actual) === structureOf(control), plus a\n                                   hole-value guard (an empty, `.` or `..` segment is refused).\n     renderBodyTemplate            JSON-escapes into a JSON body and re-parses it; percent-encodes\n                                   otherwise. A `\"` in an argument cannot open a sibling field.\n\n3. AN ARGUMENT THE PASS COULD NOT FIND REFUSES THE COMPILE.\n   compileInjectedCalls now answers {calls, refusedBecause?} instead of a bare list. An input that\n   was located in no compiled URL or body would have made the call a CONSTANT - later runs returning\n   the first run's data whatever the caller asked. A non-scalar argument refuses for the same reason.\n\n4. EVIDENCE IS DURABLE ONLY IF THE RECIPE IS.\n   Order stays evidence-then-recipe (the recipe points INTO the evidence), and the orphan that order\n   creates is now COLLECTED: learnFromRun drops the evidence it just wrote when the write did not\n   land - which is the COMMON case, since putRecipe refuses to overwrite by design. One helper,\n   discardEvidence, serves both ends of the lifecycle.",
