    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 481204888,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820g-p2-answer-and-lifecycle",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 24150.0,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1010.0,
      "height": 875.0,
      "seed": 733911353,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787323200000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (g) - P2 ROUND SEVEN: the answer moves with the argument, and a removed recipe\ntakes its evidence. AMENDS (f). ONE NEW MODULE, two new endpoints, no stored shape change.\n\nTHE ANSWER-BEARING CALL MUST CARRY EVERY HOLE (network-capture.ts + executors/injected-call.ts)\n  The located-argument rule was checked over the WHOLE recipe (`placed`, a union over every compiled\n  call) while `answerCallIndex` names ONE - and the two were never compared. `answerOf` hands the\n  caller that call's body and NOTHING chains one replayed call into the next (every template is\n  filled from the run's arguments alone), so an argument absent from the answer-bearing call cannot\n  change what the action RETURNS however faithfully the other calls carry it.\n  THE REACHABLE SHAPE: a page fetches GET /api/cases?ref=2024-1 and a GET /api/summary serving the\n  same document. The run's answer identity-matches BOTH; last-match-wins names the summary, which\n  has no hole at all; `ref` was placed by call 0 so every check passed. A caller asking about 2025-9\n  was handed the 2024-1 document under success:true, replayed:true - no drift (both calls still 200\n  with an unchanged shape), nothing to clear it, no other symptom.\n  compileInjectedCalls now records `placedByCall` and refuses when the answer call misses a hole;\n  argumentCoverage runs the same comparison at REPLAY, where an older build's recipe arrives already\n  stored, and answers `arguments-uncovered` so the caller clears it.\n  THE RECIPE-WIDE RULE STAYS: it is the only rule when a recipe names no answer (every browser-only\n  automation ships that way), and a per-call reading of it would refuse an ordinary multi-hop recipe\n  whose opening hop takes no argument. Two rules, two units; neither subsumes the other.\n\nNEW MODULE integrations/recipe-lifecycle.ts (tier 3) - forgetRecipe()\n  THE ONE WAY A RECIPE IS REMOVED. Invariant: nothing durable outlives the thing it is evidence for.\n  The spine closed that family twice (the evidence behind a REPLACED recipe; the evidence behind one\n  that never LANDED). Clearing was the third path and had no collector: IntegrationRecipeStore\n  .clearRecipe returned the dropped recipe and automation/service.ts narrowed it to a boolean, so\n  `capturedCallsRef` - the ONLY index into integration_captured_calls, a collection with no TTL -\n  was discarded. Nothing could reach the pile afterwards (priorCaptureRef reads the CURRENT recipe,\n  now absent), and `arguments-uncovered` is the ordinary listener shape, so the piles accumulated.\n  clearRecipe now answers IntegrationActionRecipe|null and takes an optional `visibleTo` actor gate\n  (applied before the CAS and re-asserted inside it, beside the orgId re-assert). forgetRecipe pairs\n  clear-then-discard; both removal paths go through it. Discard failure is swallowed and loud; clear\n  failure is not.\n\nTWO NEW ENDPOINTS (shared/src/integrations.ts + routes/integrations.ts), both auth:'user'\n  GET    /api/v1/integrations/recipes                         -> IntegrationRecipeListResponse\n  DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/recipe  -> ForgetIntegrationRecipeResponse\n  THE ONLY EXIT a recipe that keeps answering `ok` and answers WRONGLY has: putRecipe refuses to\n  overwrite, a supersede needs a drift that cannot fire while the calls keep returning 200 with an\n  unchanged shape, nothing expires it. The read is a SUMMARY whitelist (METHOD urlTemplate per call,\n  the answer index, lessons, lineage) - no header names, no body templates, no capturedCallsRef. The\n  delete is IDEMPOTENT: an action that learned nothing answers ok, not 404, which would be an\n  existence oracle. NOT user-or-key, for the approveAction/setLessons reason. NO dashboard surface\n  in this slice, stated rather than implied (docs/decisions.md).\n  The list route mounts on a LITERAL first segment and therefore sits ABOVE `GET /:key`, which would\n  otherwise swallow it - the same positional rule the configs block states. It is also what makes\n  recipe-store.listRecipesForActor reachable at last; it had no caller.\n\nNO STORED SHAPE CHANGED. answersWith and capturedCallsRef are READ here, never altered, so\n05-data-model.excalidraw is untouched - recorded as a check made, not a check skipped.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (g) - P2 ROUND SEVEN: the answer moves with the argument, and a removed recipe\ntakes its evidence. AMENDS (f). ONE NEW MODULE, two new endpoints, no stored shape change.\n\nTHE ANSWER-BEARING CALL MUST CARRY EVERY HOLE (network-capture.ts + executors/injected-call.ts)\n  The located-argument rule was checked over the WHOLE recipe (`placed`, a union over every compiled\n  call) while `answerCallIndex` names ONE - and the two were never compared. `answerOf` hands the\n  caller that call's body and NOTHING chains one replayed call into the next (every template is\n  filled from the run's arguments alone), so an argument absent from the answer-bearing call cannot\n  change what the action RETURNS however faithfully the other calls carry it.\n  THE REACHABLE SHAPE: a page fetches GET /api/cases?ref=2024-1 and a GET /api/summary serving the\n  same document. The run's answer identity-matches BOTH; last-match-wins names the summary, which\n  has no hole at all; `ref` was placed by call 0 so every check passed. A caller asking about 2025-9\n  was handed the 2024-1 document under success:true, replayed:true - no drift (both calls still 200\n  with an unchanged shape), nothing to clear it, no other symptom.\n  compileInjectedCalls now records `placedByCall` and refuses when the answer call misses a hole;\n  argumentCoverage runs the same comparison at REPLAY, where an older build's recipe arrives already\n  stored, and answers `arguments-uncovered` so the caller clears it.\n  THE RECIPE-WIDE RULE STAYS: it is the only rule when a recipe names no answer (every browser-only\n  automation ships that way), and a per-call reading of it would refuse an ordinary multi-hop recipe\n  whose opening hop takes no argument. Two rules, two units; neither subsumes the other.\n\nNEW MODULE integrations/recipe-lifecycle.ts (tier 3) - forgetRecipe()\n  THE ONE WAY A RECIPE IS REMOVED. Invariant: nothing durable outlives the thing it is evidence for.\n  The spine closed that family twice (the evidence behind a REPLACED recipe; the evidence behind one\n  that never LANDED). Clearing was the third path and had no collector: IntegrationRecipeStore\n  .clearRecipe returned the dropped recipe and automation/service.ts narrowed it to a boolean, so\n  `capturedCallsRef` - the ONLY index into integration_captured_calls, a collection with no TTL -\n  was discarded. Nothing could reach the pile afterwards (priorCaptureRef reads the CURRENT recipe,\n  now absent), and `arguments-uncovered` is the ordinary listener shape, so the piles accumulated.\n  clearRecipe now answers IntegrationActionRecipe|null and takes an optional `visibleTo` actor gate\n  (applied before the CAS and re-asserted inside it, beside the orgId re-assert). forgetRecipe pairs\n  clear-then-discard; both removal paths go through it. Discard failure is swallowed and loud; clear\n  failure is not.\n\nTWO NEW ENDPOINTS (shared/src/integrations.ts + routes/integrations.ts), both auth:'user'\n  GET    /api/v1/integrations/recipes                         -> IntegrationRecipeListResponse\n  DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/recipe  -> ForgetIntegrationRecipeResponse\n  THE ONLY EXIT a recipe that keeps answering `ok` and answers WRONGLY has: putRecipe refuses to\n  overwrite, a supersede needs a drift that cannot fire while the calls keep returning 200 with an\n  unchanged shape, nothing expires it. The read is a SUMMARY whitelist (METHOD urlTemplate per call,\n  the answer index, lessons, lineage) - no header names, no body templates, no capturedCallsRef. The\n  delete is IDEMPOTENT: an action that learned nothing answers ok, not 404, which would be an\n  existence oracle. NOT user-or-key, for the approveAction/setLessons reason. NO dashboard surface\n  in this slice, stated rather than implied (docs/decisions.md).\n  The list route mounts on a LITERAL first segment and therefore sits ABOVE `GET /:key`, which would\n  otherwise swallow it - the same positional rule the configs block states. It is also what makes\n  recipe-store.listRecipesForActor reachable at last; it had no caller.\n\nNO STORED SHAPE CHANGED. answersWith and capturedCallsRef are READ here, never altered, so\n05-data-model.excalidraw is untouched - recorded as a check made, not a check skipped.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (g) - P2 ROUND SEVEN: the answer moves with the argument, and a removed recipe\ntakes its evidence. AMENDS (f). ONE NEW MODULE, two new endpoints, no stored shape change.\n\nTHE ANSWER-BEARING CALL MUST CARRY EVERY HOLE (network-capture.ts + executors/injected-call.ts)\n  The located-argument rule was checked over the WHOLE recipe (`placed`, a union over every compiled\n  call) while `answerCallIndex` names ONE - and the two were never compared. `answerOf` hands the\n  caller that call's body and NOTHING chains one replayed call into the next (every template is\n  filled from the run's arguments alone), so an argument absent from the answer-bearing call cannot\n  change what the action RETURNS however faithfully the other calls carry it.\n  THE REACHABLE SHAPE: a page fetches GET /api/cases?ref=2024-1 and a GET /api/summary serving the\n  same document. The run's answer identity-matches BOTH; last-match-wins names the summary, which\n  has no hole at all; `ref` was placed by call 0 so every check passed. A caller asking about 2025-9\n  was handed the 2024-1 document under success:true, replayed:true - no drift (both calls still 200\n  with an unchanged shape), nothing to clear it, no other symptom.\n  compileInjectedCalls now records `placedByCall` and refuses when the answer call misses a hole;\n  argumentCoverage runs the same comparison at REPLAY, where an older build's recipe arrives already\n  stored, and answers `arguments-uncovered` so the caller clears it.\n  THE RECIPE-WIDE RULE STAYS: it is the only rule when a recipe names no answer (every browser-only\n  automation ships that way), and a per-call reading of it would refuse an ordinary multi-hop recipe\n  whose opening hop takes no argument. Two rules, two units; neither subsumes the other.\n\nNEW MODULE integrations/recipe-lifecycle.ts (tier 3) - forgetRecipe()\n  THE ONE WAY A RECIPE IS REMOVED. Invariant: nothing durable outlives the thing it is evidence for.\n  The spine closed that family twice (the evidence behind a REPLACED recipe; the evidence behind one\n  that never LANDED). Clearing was the third path and had no collector: IntegrationRecipeStore\n  .clearRecipe returned the dropped recipe and automation/service.ts narrowed it to a boolean, so\n  `capturedCallsRef` - the ONLY index into integration_captured_calls, a collection with no TTL -\n  was discarded. Nothing could reach the pile afterwards (priorCaptureRef reads the CURRENT recipe,\n  now absent), and `arguments-uncovered` is the ordinary listener shape, so the piles accumulated.\n  clearRecipe now answers IntegrationActionRecipe|null and takes an optional `visibleTo` actor gate\n  (applied before the CAS and re-asserted inside it, beside the orgId re-assert). forgetRecipe pairs\n  clear-then-discard; both removal paths go through it. Discard failure is swallowed and loud; clear\n  failure is not.\n\nTWO NEW ENDPOINTS (shared/src/integrations.ts + routes/integrations.ts), both auth:'user'\n  GET    /api/v1/integrations/recipes                         -> IntegrationRecipeListResponse\n  DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/recipe  -> ForgetIntegrationRecipeResponse\n  THE ONLY EXIT a recipe that keeps answering `ok` and answers WRONGLY has: putRecipe refuses to\n  overwrite, a supersede needs a drift that cannot fire while the calls keep returning 200 with an\n  unchanged shape, nothing expires it. The read is a SUMMARY whitelist (METHOD urlTemplate per call,\n  the answer index, lessons, lineage) - no header names, no body templates, no capturedCallsRef. The\n  delete is IDEMPOTENT: an action that learned nothing answers ok, not 404, which would be an\n  existence oracle. NOT user-or-key, for the approveAction/setLessons reason. NO dashboard surface\n  in this slice, stated rather than implied (docs/decisions.md).\n  The list route mounts on a LITERAL first segment and therefore sits ABOVE `GET /:key`, which would\n  otherwise swallow it - the same positional rule the configs block states. It is also what makes\n  recipe-store.listRecipesForActor reachable at last; it had no caller.\n\nNO STORED SHAPE CHANGED. answersWith and capturedCallsRef are READ here, never altered, so\n05-data-model.excalidraw is untouched - recorded as a check made, not a check skipped.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 481204901,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820h-p2-exception-safe-collection",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 25212.5,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1010.0,
      "height": 1067.5,
      "seed": 733911401,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787323200000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (h) - P2 ROUND EIGHT: every EXIT collects, and the removal paths are counted\nfrom the code. AMENDS (g). No new module, no stored shape change, ONE new runtime edge.\n\nTHE COLLECTOR HANDLED EVERY EXIT THAT RETURNED AND NONE THAT THREW (automation/service.ts)\n  learnFromRun writes the evidence FIRST (the recipe carries capturedCallsRef INTO it) and collected\n  the orphan with `if (!stored) discardEvidence(...)` - reached only when the write RETURNED a\n  verdict. putRecipe/supersedeRecipe do not always return: assertCarriesNoValues THROWS, which is\n  that module's entire posture (refusal, never redaction), and so does any store error. The throw\n  propagates to runAutomationForAction's .catch, which logs a warning and reports the run as the\n  success it was - so the discard never ran at all.\n  AND IT REPEATS. The refusal is decided AT THE STORE from what the pass captured, so it is a\n  property of the pass: the recipe is never written, priorCaptureRef reads a recipe that is absent,\n  and EVERY later run writes a fresh pile of full redacted request AND response bodies. No TTL, no\n  other index, the owner's DELETE answers evidenceDiscarded:0, listCaptureIds has no caller.\n  THE REACHABLE SHAPE, proved end to end against the real stores: a page fetches GET /api/cases?ref=\n  2024-1 plus an ordinary GET /api/view?state=<38-char page-state token>. No redaction leg touches\n  it (the run never held it; `state` is in no name pattern), the compile leaves it literal because it\n  is not one of the run's arguments, and looksLikeLiteralSecret then refuses the whole recipe.\n  FIX: the write, the supersede-discard and the outcome now sit in a try, and the orphan collection\n  in its `finally`. discardEvidence swallows and logs its own failures, so it can never replace the\n  exception on its way past.\n\nTHE REMOVAL PATHS, ENUMERATED FROM THE CODE - THERE ARE FOUR, NOT THREE\n  (g) said forgetRecipe was reached by BOTH removal paths \"so a future third cannot forget\". Both\n  counts were wrong. Grep `recipe` across integrations/ and the paths are:\n    1 THE CLEAR              recipe-store.clearRecipe, via the owner's DELETE route and the run\n                             loop's clearRefusedRecipe.        collector: forgetRecipe\n    2 THE SUPERSEDE          recipe-store.supersedeRecipe.     collector: learnFromRun priorCaptureRef\n    3 THE WRITE THAT NEVER   putRecipe/supersedeRecipe answering exists/notfound - OR THROWING.\n      LANDS                                                    collector: learnFromRun finally (above)\n    4 THE ACTION SET         IntegrationDefinitionStore.create(onConflict:'replace') - the ordinary\n      REWRITTEN              builder save (definition-save.ts) and achieve's in-place write.\n                             carryRecipesForward re-attaches BY ACTION NAME, so an action the\n                             incoming set no longer names (renamed or removed - an ordinary edit, and\n                             what an agent re-authoring an integration does routinely) loses its\n                             recipe.                           collector: NEW, in create itself\n  Path 4 is newly REACHABLE because of this spine: before it, appendCapturedCall had no production\n  caller at all, so the collection was always empty and this path removed nothing.\n\nTHE PAIRING IS ONE FUNCTION, AND IT MOVED DOWN A MODULE\n  NEW export captured-calls-store.discardEvidenceOfRemovedRecipes(scope, removed[], deps) - given\n  recipes that are ALREADY gone, drop what each named, best-effort and loud, one failure never\n  abandoning the batch. forgetRecipe delegates to it; definition-store.create calls it directly.\n  WHY NOT IN recipe-lifecycle.ts: paths 2 and 4 remove a recipe as a SIDE EFFECT of a write that\n  rewrote something else, and only the writer knows what it dropped - so the pairing must be callable\n  from definition-store.ts, which stands deliberately on the database alone. Importing\n  recipe-lifecycle would drag recipe-store -> definitions.ts (the file-based registry, with its two\n  synchronous disk tiers) into it and close a cycle. captured-calls-store imports data/ and\n  security/ only, so THE ONE NEW RUNTIME EDGE (definition-store -> captured-calls-store, tier 3 to\n  tier 3) keeps that claim true.\n\nTHE SUPERSEDE'S OWN FIELD NOW GOES THROUGH THE PERSISTENCE-BOUNDARY PROOF (recipe-store.ts)\n  supersedeRecipe destructured `reason` OUT of the payload before assertCarriesNoValues, so the one\n  string in a supersede this repo did NOT compile was exempt from all three legs at once: the run's\n  SecretRegistry, looksLikeLiteralSecret, and LIMITS.stringChars. It is the LEAST trusted string\n  there - classifyReplayDrift's signal reason, i.e. daemon-supplied or fetch-error text - it is\n  written as supersedes.reason onto the DEFINITION document (so it rides every read and every CAS of\n  that row: Trap T2, the whole bounded-recipe argument), and recipeSummary puts it on the wire to the\n  owner. The proof is now handed `next`, not `draft`. \"Every write goes through it\" is true.\n\nNO STORED SHAPE CHANGED, so 05-data-model.excalidraw is untouched - a check made, not skipped.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (h) - P2 ROUND EIGHT: every EXIT collects, and the removal paths are counted\nfrom the code. AMENDS (g). No new module, no stored shape change, ONE new runtime edge.\n\nTHE COLLECTOR HANDLED EVERY EXIT THAT RETURNED AND NONE THAT THREW (automation/service.ts)\n  learnFromRun writes the evidence FIRST (the recipe carries capturedCallsRef INTO it) and collected\n  the orphan with `if (!stored) discardEvidence(...)` - reached only when the write RETURNED a\n  verdict. putRecipe/supersedeRecipe do not always return: assertCarriesNoValues THROWS, which is\n  that module's entire posture (refusal, never redaction), and so does any store error. The throw\n  propagates to runAutomationForAction's .catch, which logs a warning and reports the run as the\n  success it was - so the discard never ran at all.\n  AND IT REPEATS. The refusal is decided AT THE STORE from what the pass captured, so it is a\n  property of the pass: the recipe is never written, priorCaptureRef reads a recipe that is absent,\n  and EVERY later run writes a fresh pile of full redacted request AND response bodies. No TTL, no\n  other index, the owner's DELETE answers evidenceDiscarded:0, listCaptureIds has no caller.\n  THE REACHABLE SHAPE, proved end to end against the real stores: a page fetches GET /api/cases?ref=\n  2024-1 plus an ordinary GET /api/view?state=<38-char page-state token>. No redaction leg touches\n  it (the run never held it; `state` is in no name pattern), the compile leaves it literal because it\n  is not one of the run's arguments, and looksLikeLiteralSecret then refuses the whole recipe.\n  FIX: the write, the supersede-discard and the outcome now sit in a try, and the orphan collection\n  in its `finally`. discardEvidence swallows and logs its own failures, so it can never replace the\n  exception on its way past.\n\nTHE REMOVAL PATHS, ENUMERATED FROM THE CODE - THERE ARE FOUR, NOT THREE\n  (g) said forgetRecipe was reached by BOTH removal paths \"so a future third cannot forget\". Both\n  counts were wrong. Grep `recipe` across integrations/ and the paths are:\n    1 THE CLEAR              recipe-store.clearRecipe, via the owner's DELETE route and the run\n                             loop's clearRefusedRecipe.        collector: forgetRecipe\n    2 THE SUPERSEDE          recipe-store.supersedeRecipe.     collector: learnFromRun priorCaptureRef\n    3 THE WRITE THAT NEVER   putRecipe/supersedeRecipe answering exists/notfound - OR THROWING.\n      LANDS                                                    collector: learnFromRun finally (above)\n    4 THE ACTION SET         IntegrationDefinitionStore.create(onConflict:'replace') - the ordinary\n      REWRITTEN              builder save (definition-save.ts) and achieve's in-place write.\n                             carryRecipesForward re-attaches BY ACTION NAME, so an action the\n                             incoming set no longer names (renamed or removed - an ordinary edit, and\n                             what an agent re-authoring an integration does routinely) loses its\n                             recipe.                           collector: NEW, in create itself\n  Path 4 is newly REACHABLE because of this spine: before it, appendCapturedCall had no production\n  caller at all, so the collection was always empty and this path removed nothing.\n\nTHE PAIRING IS ONE FUNCTION, AND IT MOVED DOWN A MODULE\n  NEW export captured-calls-store.discardEvidenceOfRemovedRecipes(scope, removed[], deps) - given\n  recipes that are ALREADY gone, drop what each named, best-effort and loud, one failure never\n  abandoning the batch. forgetRecipe delegates to it; definition-store.create calls it directly.\n  WHY NOT IN recipe-lifecycle.ts: paths 2 and 4 remove a recipe as a SIDE EFFECT of a write that\n  rewrote something else, and only the writer knows what it dropped - so the pairing must be callable\n  from definition-store.ts, which stands deliberately on the database alone. Importing\n  recipe-lifecycle would drag recipe-store -> definitions.ts (the file-based registry, with its two\n  synchronous disk tiers) into it and close a cycle. captured-calls-store imports data/ and\n  security/ only, so THE ONE NEW RUNTIME EDGE (definition-store -> captured-calls-store, tier 3 to\n  tier 3) keeps that claim true.\n\nTHE SUPERSEDE'S OWN FIELD NOW GOES THROUGH THE PERSISTENCE-BOUNDARY PROOF (recipe-store.ts)\n  supersedeRecipe destructured `reason` OUT of the payload before assertCarriesNoValues, so the one\n  string in a supersede this repo did NOT compile was exempt from all three legs at once: the run's\n  SecretRegistry, looksLikeLiteralSecret, and LIMITS.stringChars. It is the LEAST trusted string\n  there - classifyReplayDrift's signal reason, i.e. daemon-supplied or fetch-error text - it is\n  written as supersedes.reason onto the DEFINITION document (so it rides every read and every CAS of\n  that row: Trap T2, the whole bounded-recipe argument), and recipeSummary puts it on the wire to the\n  owner. The proof is now handed `next`, not `draft`. \"Every write goes through it\" is true.\n\nNO STORED SHAPE CHANGED, so 05-data-model.excalidraw is untouched - a check made, not skipped.",
