      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND TWO, corrections to the S1 note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): one new edge and one named binding.\n\nNEW EDGE, integrations/definition-store.ts -> integrations/action-evidence-store.ts. The module's\nstanding claim (no runtime dependency on the file-based registry; database-only) is unchanged - the\nevidence store stands on data/ and security/ alone, exactly as captured-calls-store.ts does. The edge\nexists because create()'s replace branch is the ONE removal path an action has, so it is the one\nplace that knows which actions a write dropped: it calls discardEvidenceOfRemovedActions(\n{orgId, integrationKey}, actionsDroppedBy(incoming, existing)) AFTER the put, beside the recipe\ncollector. actionsDroppedBy is a SEPARATE predicate from recipesDroppedBy on purpose - that one\nfilters to actions carrying a compiled recipe, which would skip the commonest evidence-bearing action\nthere is, a plain api-call.\n\nTHE BOOT COMPOSITION IS NAMED AND AWAITED. server.ts exports sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence(),\nthe ONE production composition of actionEvidenceStore.pinnedRunIdsForRetention() ->\nautomation/screenshot-plane.ts sweepExpiredScreenshots({now, pinnedRunIds}), and bootState AWAITS it\n(it was fire-and-forget, so no caller could wait on it and no test could observe it). Two changes make\nthat binding provable rather than assumed: sweepExpiredScreenshots' `pinnedRunIds` option is now\nREQUIRED, so a call that drops or renames it does not compile; and the pin read degrades to an empty\nset on failure, so a mongo blip at boot cannot turn into an UNPINNED sweep - the one failure mode that\ndestroys data. Suite: api/tests/automation/composition-root-screenshot-pins.test.ts, entered at the\nREAL bootState. The direction of the edge is unchanged: screenshot-plane.ts still holds NO import edge\nto integrations/ - the pins are supplied by the composition root.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND TWO, corrections to the S1 note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): one new edge and one named binding.\n\nNEW EDGE, integrations/definition-store.ts -> integrations/action-evidence-store.ts. The module's\nstanding claim (no runtime dependency on the file-based registry; database-only) is unchanged - the\nevidence store stands on data/ and security/ alone, exactly as captured-calls-store.ts does. The edge\nexists because create()'s replace branch is the ONE removal path an action has, so it is the one\nplace that knows which actions a write dropped: it calls discardEvidenceOfRemovedActions(\n{orgId, integrationKey}, actionsDroppedBy(incoming, existing)) AFTER the put, beside the recipe\ncollector. actionsDroppedBy is a SEPARATE predicate from recipesDroppedBy on purpose - that one\nfilters to actions carrying a compiled recipe, which would skip the commonest evidence-bearing action\nthere is, a plain api-call.\n\nTHE BOOT COMPOSITION IS NAMED AND AWAITED. server.ts exports sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence(),\nthe ONE production composition of actionEvidenceStore.pinnedRunIdsForRetention() ->\nautomation/screenshot-plane.ts sweepExpiredScreenshots({now, pinnedRunIds}), and bootState AWAITS it\n(it was fire-and-forget, so no caller could wait on it and no test could observe it). Two changes make\nthat binding provable rather than assumed: sweepExpiredScreenshots' `pinnedRunIds` option is now\nREQUIRED, so a call that drops or renames it does not compile; and the pin read degrades to an empty\nset on failure, so a mongo blip at boot cannot turn into an UNPINNED sweep - the one failure mode that\ndestroys data. Suite: api/tests/automation/composition-root-screenshot-pins.test.ts, entered at the\nREAL bootState. The direction of the edge is unchanged: screenshot-plane.ts still holds NO import edge\nto integrations/ - the pins are supplied by the composition root.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND TWO, corrections to the S1 note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): one new edge and one named binding.\n\nNEW EDGE, integrations/definition-store.ts -> integrations/action-evidence-store.ts. The module's\nstanding claim (no runtime dependency on the file-based registry; database-only) is unchanged - the\nevidence store stands on data/ and security/ alone, exactly as captured-calls-store.ts does. The edge\nexists because create()'s replace branch is the ONE removal path an action has, so it is the one\nplace that knows which actions a write dropped: it calls discardEvidenceOfRemovedActions(\n{orgId, integrationKey}, actionsDroppedBy(incoming, existing)) AFTER the put, beside the recipe\ncollector. actionsDroppedBy is a SEPARATE predicate from recipesDroppedBy on purpose - that one\nfilters to actions carrying a compiled recipe, which would skip the commonest evidence-bearing action\nthere is, a plain api-call.\n\nTHE BOOT COMPOSITION IS NAMED AND AWAITED. server.ts exports sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence(),\nthe ONE production composition of actionEvidenceStore.pinnedRunIdsForRetention() ->\nautomation/screenshot-plane.ts sweepExpiredScreenshots({now, pinnedRunIds}), and bootState AWAITS it\n(it was fire-and-forget, so no caller could wait on it and no test could observe it). Two changes make\nthat binding provable rather than assumed: sweepExpiredScreenshots' `pinnedRunIds` option is now\nREQUIRED, so a call that drops or renames it does not compile; and the pin read degrades to an empty\nset on failure, so a mongo blip at boot cannot turn into an UNPINNED sweep - the one failure mode that\ndestroys data. Suite: api/tests/automation/composition-root-screenshot-pins.test.ts, entered at the\nREAL bootState. The direction of the edge is unchanged: screenshot-plane.ts still holds NO import edge\nto integrations/ - the pins are supplied by the composition root."
