    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608320,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820c-s1r3-evidence-reconciler-edges",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 27100,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 700,
      "seed": 202608321,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755860000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND THREE, correcting the ROUND TWO note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): the edges out of integrations/definition-store.ts,\nand one new edge out of integrations/service.ts.\n\nTHE EDGE THAT WAS THERE. definition-store.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts\n(discardEvidenceOfRemovedActions), on create(..., 'replace') only, carrying the WRITER's org. That\nedge could only ever collect rows belonging to the org that AUTHORED the definition, and evidence\nrows are keyed by the org that RAN the action - which the `global` tier makes a different org.\n\nTHE EDGES NOW, and both stay database-only (action-evidence-store.ts stands on data/ + security/\nalone, so no tier boundary moves):\n\n  definition-store.create(..., 'replace') --+\n                                            +--> discardEvidenceOfUnresolvableActions(key, resolve)\n  definition-store.setVisibility -----------+       |\n                                                    +--> ActionEvidenceStore.listOwnerRefsForKey\n                                                    |      (cross-tenant, projected to\n                                                    |       {orgId, ownerUserId, actionName})\n                                                    +--> resolve = definition-store.getForActor\n                                                    |      (the SAME resolver the executor uses,\n                                                    |       asked per (orgId, ownerUserId))\n                                                    +--> ActionEvidenceStore.discardEvidence\n\n  service.ts deleteConfig ------------------------> discardEvidenceOfDisconnectedConfig\n    (DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key)                 +--> discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig\n\nThe resolve callback is INJECTED rather than imported: definition-store owns the resolution and\naction-evidence-store owns the collection, and neither may own both (an import the other way would\ncycle). The reconciler is the only cross-tenant writer in the module, and it returns a COUNT to its\ncaller, never a row.\n\nBOOT COMPOSITION, corrected. The note above says bootState AWAITS\nsweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence and presents the await as what makes the sweep observable. It\nis not: bootState awaits slower things afterwards, so `void sweep(...)` left the pins suite 5/5\ngreen. bootState now READS the returned counts (the retention log line moved out of the composition\nfunction and into the call site), so the mutant does not compile. The await itself is unchanged, and\nscreenshot-plane.ts still holds NO import edge to integrations/.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND THREE, correcting the ROUND TWO note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): the edges out of integrations/definition-store.ts,\nand one new edge out of integrations/service.ts.\n\nTHE EDGE THAT WAS THERE. definition-store.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts\n(discardEvidenceOfRemovedActions), on create(..., 'replace') only, carrying the WRITER's org. That\nedge could only ever collect rows belonging to the org that AUTHORED the definition, and evidence\nrows are keyed by the org that RAN the action - which the `global` tier makes a different org.\n\nTHE EDGES NOW, and both stay database-only (action-evidence-store.ts stands on data/ + security/\nalone, so no tier boundary moves):\n\n  definition-store.create(..., 'replace') --+\n                                            +--> discardEvidenceOfUnresolvableActions(key, resolve)\n  definition-store.setVisibility -----------+       |\n                                                    +--> ActionEvidenceStore.listOwnerRefsForKey\n                                                    |      (cross-tenant, projected to\n                                                    |       {orgId, ownerUserId, actionName})\n                                                    +--> resolve = definition-store.getForActor\n                                                    |      (the SAME resolver the executor uses,\n                                                    |       asked per (orgId, ownerUserId))\n                                                    +--> ActionEvidenceStore.discardEvidence\n\n  service.ts deleteConfig ------------------------> discardEvidenceOfDisconnectedConfig\n    (DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key)                 +--> discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig\n\nThe resolve callback is INJECTED rather than imported: definition-store owns the resolution and\naction-evidence-store owns the collection, and neither may own both (an import the other way would\ncycle). The reconciler is the only cross-tenant writer in the module, and it returns a COUNT to its\ncaller, never a row.\n\nBOOT COMPOSITION, corrected. The note above says bootState AWAITS\nsweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence and presents the await as what makes the sweep observable. It\nis not: bootState awaits slower things afterwards, so `void sweep(...)` left the pins suite 5/5\ngreen. bootState now READS the returned counts (the retention log line moved out of the composition\nfunction and into the call site), so the mutant does not compile. The await itself is unchanged, and\nscreenshot-plane.ts still holds NO import edge to integrations/.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND THREE, correcting the ROUND TWO note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): the edges out of integrations/definition-store.ts,\nand one new edge out of integrations/service.ts.\n\nTHE EDGE THAT WAS THERE. definition-store.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts\n(discardEvidenceOfRemovedActions), on create(..., 'replace') only, carrying the WRITER's org. That\nedge could only ever collect rows belonging to the org that AUTHORED the definition, and evidence\nrows are keyed by the org that RAN the action - which the `global` tier makes a different org.\n\nTHE EDGES NOW, and both stay database-only (action-evidence-store.ts stands on data/ + security/\nalone, so no tier boundary moves):\n\n  definition-store.create(..., 'replace') --+\n                                            +--> discardEvidenceOfUnresolvableActions(key, resolve)\n  definition-store.setVisibility -----------+       |\n                                                    +--> ActionEvidenceStore.listOwnerRefsForKey\n                                                    |      (cross-tenant, projected to\n                                                    |       {orgId, ownerUserId, actionName})\n                                                    +--> resolve = definition-store.getForActor\n                                                    |      (the SAME resolver the executor uses,\n                                                    |       asked per (orgId, ownerUserId))\n                                                    +--> ActionEvidenceStore.discardEvidence\n\n  service.ts deleteConfig ------------------------> discardEvidenceOfDisconnectedConfig\n    (DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key)                 +--> discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig\n\nThe resolve callback is INJECTED rather than imported: definition-store owns the resolution and\naction-evidence-store owns the collection, and neither may own both (an import the other way would\ncycle). The reconciler is the only cross-tenant writer in the module, and it returns a COUNT to its\ncaller, never a row.\n\nBOOT COMPOSITION, corrected. The note above says bootState AWAITS\nsweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence and presents the await as what makes the sweep observable. It\nis not: bootState awaits slower things afterwards, so `void sweep(...)` left the pins suite 5/5\ngreen. bootState now READS the returned counts (the retention log line moved out of the composition\nfunction and into the call site), so the mutant does not compile. The await itself is unchanged, and\nscreenshot-plane.ts still holds NO import edge to integrations/."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608240,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820d-s1r4-one-org-never-deletes-another",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 28100,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 997.5,
      "seed": 202608241,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755900000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (d) - S1 ROUND FOUR: a write by ONE org never deletes ANOTHER org's data.\nRETIRES the reconciler drawn in (c). TWO new modules, ONE new seam, one runtime edge REMOVED.\n\nWHY (c) IS RETIRED AND NOT TUNED\n  (c) drew definition-store -> action-evidence-store as a CROSS-TENANT reconciler asking getForActor\n  per row owner. It deleted across an org boundary, twice over, both reproduced end to end:\n    LIVE vs SNAPSHOT    a consumer resolves the FROZEN publishedSnapshot (crossOrgView ->\n                        publishedViewOf), which the replace branch carries forward deliberately and\n                        setVisibility re-promotes without re-scrubbing. The reconciler asked for the\n                        LIVE row, so org A's re-authoring destroyed org B's only copy of a sample\n                        for an action ORG B COULD STILL RUN.\n    RUNNER vs CUSTODIAN an org-shared credential resolves the definition as the CUSTODIAN and\n                        \"never as the reader\" (definitionActorForCredential). The key is stamped\n                        with the RUNNER, who cannot see the custodian's private row, so the answer\n                        was the empty set and every peer's evidence went on a re-save that dropped\n                        nothing at all.\n  \"Who can still resolve this action\" has a different answer per reader, so a write-time answer on\n  behalf of readers the writer cannot see will keep being wrong - and being wrong there is\n  unrecoverable. Three rounds is evidence about the SHAPE, not the parameter.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/action-resolution.ts (tier 3) - THE ONE RESOLUTION\n  findConfigForOwner -> definitionActorForCredential -> resolveDefinition, extracted from the\n  executor, and action-executor.ts CALLS IT. That is the structural half of the fix: a retention\n  decision cannot believe something a run does not, because if this module is wrong execution is\n  wrong first, loudly. resolvableActionNamesForOwner projects it onto action NAMES with a THREE-WAY\n  answer - null (\"could not find out\") is never the empty set (\"resolves nothing\").\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/evidence-reconcile.ts (tier 3) - THE WRITE-TIME COLLECTOR\n  reconcileOwnOrgEvidence(orgId, integrationKey): the ORG IS A REQUIRED PARAMETER and every query\n  carries it, so the blast radius of the worst bug it can contain is the writing tenant. Bounded by\n  MAX_RECONCILED_OWNERS (25); above it, it stops and says so. Fails towards KEEPING at every step.\n\nTHE EDGE definition-store -> action-evidence-store IS REMOVED, REPLACED BY A SEAM\n  definition-store.ts declares DefinitionEvidenceReconciler + setDefinitionEvidenceReconciler and\n  calls it from create's replace branch, setVisibility AND publishSnapshot. evidence-reconcile.ts\n  implements it; server.ts binds it through bindDefinitionEvidenceReconciler(). A seam because the\n  store cannot import the resolution without a cycle (definition-registry -> definition-store), and\n  because calling it from the four higher-tier write sites would make reachability something four\n  authors must remember. Unbound => collects nothing, which is the safe direction.\n  action-evidence-store's CROSS-TENANT LISTING (listOwnerRefsForKey) IS DELETED, not narrowed: a\n  cross-tenant listing is what made a cross-tenant delete expressible. listOwnerRefsInOrg replaces\n  it, and takes the org as its first argument.\n\nTHE READER COLLECTS ITS OWN (action-executor.ts, third member of the executorDeps bundle)\n  The executor resolves for THIS org, owner, credential and document, so it is the only place the\n  answer is knowable. Its unknown_integration / unknown_action refusals call\n  discardOwnActionEvidence -> ActionEvidenceStore.discardOwnerEvidence, whose scope type REQUIRES\n  both tenancy terms and has no org-wide arm. Bundled with the other two seams so the third could\n  not half-land.\n\nAND THE ORPHAN IS BOUNDED RATHER THAN ARGUED AWAY\n  sweepExpiredEvidence at boot (EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90), ordered BEFORE the pin read inside\n  server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence so an expiring row releases its screenshot pin on\n  the SAME boot; DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence as the owner's own\n  erasure control (auth: 'user'); and deleteConfig's credential erasure, whose org-shared arm is now\n  an EXCLUSION LIST (findConfigForOwner answers a member's own row first, so a peer holding their\n  own credential was never served by the deleted one).",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (d) - S1 ROUND FOUR: a write by ONE org never deletes ANOTHER org's data.\nRETIRES the reconciler drawn in (c). TWO new modules, ONE new seam, one runtime edge REMOVED.\n\nWHY (c) IS RETIRED AND NOT TUNED\n  (c) drew definition-store -> action-evidence-store as a CROSS-TENANT reconciler asking getForActor\n  per row owner. It deleted across an org boundary, twice over, both reproduced end to end:\n    LIVE vs SNAPSHOT    a consumer resolves the FROZEN publishedSnapshot (crossOrgView ->\n                        publishedViewOf), which the replace branch carries forward deliberately and\n                        setVisibility re-promotes without re-scrubbing. The reconciler asked for the\n                        LIVE row, so org A's re-authoring destroyed org B's only copy of a sample\n                        for an action ORG B COULD STILL RUN.\n    RUNNER vs CUSTODIAN an org-shared credential resolves the definition as the CUSTODIAN and\n                        \"never as the reader\" (definitionActorForCredential). The key is stamped\n                        with the RUNNER, who cannot see the custodian's private row, so the answer\n                        was the empty set and every peer's evidence went on a re-save that dropped\n                        nothing at all.\n  \"Who can still resolve this action\" has a different answer per reader, so a write-time answer on\n  behalf of readers the writer cannot see will keep being wrong - and being wrong there is\n  unrecoverable. Three rounds is evidence about the SHAPE, not the parameter.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/action-resolution.ts (tier 3) - THE ONE RESOLUTION\n  findConfigForOwner -> definitionActorForCredential -> resolveDefinition, extracted from the\n  executor, and action-executor.ts CALLS IT. That is the structural half of the fix: a retention\n  decision cannot believe something a run does not, because if this module is wrong execution is\n  wrong first, loudly. resolvableActionNamesForOwner projects it onto action NAMES with a THREE-WAY\n  answer - null (\"could not find out\") is never the empty set (\"resolves nothing\").\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/evidence-reconcile.ts (tier 3) - THE WRITE-TIME COLLECTOR\n  reconcileOwnOrgEvidence(orgId, integrationKey): the ORG IS A REQUIRED PARAMETER and every query\n  carries it, so the blast radius of the worst bug it can contain is the writing tenant. Bounded by\n  MAX_RECONCILED_OWNERS (25); above it, it stops and says so. Fails towards KEEPING at every step.\n\nTHE EDGE definition-store -> action-evidence-store IS REMOVED, REPLACED BY A SEAM\n  definition-store.ts declares DefinitionEvidenceReconciler + setDefinitionEvidenceReconciler and\n  calls it from create's replace branch, setVisibility AND publishSnapshot. evidence-reconcile.ts\n  implements it; server.ts binds it through bindDefinitionEvidenceReconciler(). A seam because the\n  store cannot import the resolution without a cycle (definition-registry -> definition-store), and\n  because calling it from the four higher-tier write sites would make reachability something four\n  authors must remember. Unbound => collects nothing, which is the safe direction.\n  action-evidence-store's CROSS-TENANT LISTING (listOwnerRefsForKey) IS DELETED, not narrowed: a\n  cross-tenant listing is what made a cross-tenant delete expressible. listOwnerRefsInOrg replaces\n  it, and takes the org as its first argument.\n\nTHE READER COLLECTS ITS OWN (action-executor.ts, third member of the executorDeps bundle)\n  The executor resolves for THIS org, owner, credential and document, so it is the only place the\n  answer is knowable. Its unknown_integration / unknown_action refusals call\n  discardOwnActionEvidence -> ActionEvidenceStore.discardOwnerEvidence, whose scope type REQUIRES\n  both tenancy terms and has no org-wide arm. Bundled with the other two seams so the third could\n  not half-land.\n\nAND THE ORPHAN IS BOUNDED RATHER THAN ARGUED AWAY\n  sweepExpiredEvidence at boot (EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90), ordered BEFORE the pin read inside\n  server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence so an expiring row releases its screenshot pin on\n  the SAME boot; DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence as the owner's own\n  erasure control (auth: 'user'); and deleteConfig's credential erasure, whose org-shared arm is now\n  an EXCLUSION LIST (findConfigForOwner answers a member's own row first, so a peer holding their\n  own credential was never served by the deleted one).",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (d) - S1 ROUND FOUR: a write by ONE org never deletes ANOTHER org's data.\nRETIRES the reconciler drawn in (c). TWO new modules, ONE new seam, one runtime edge REMOVED.\n\nWHY (c) IS RETIRED AND NOT TUNED\n  (c) drew definition-store -> action-evidence-store as a CROSS-TENANT reconciler asking getForActor\n  per row owner. It deleted across an org boundary, twice over, both reproduced end to end:\n    LIVE vs SNAPSHOT    a consumer resolves the FROZEN publishedSnapshot (crossOrgView ->\n                        publishedViewOf), which the replace branch carries forward deliberately and\n                        setVisibility re-promotes without re-scrubbing. The reconciler asked for the\n                        LIVE row, so org A's re-authoring destroyed org B's only copy of a sample\n                        for an action ORG B COULD STILL RUN.\n    RUNNER vs CUSTODIAN an org-shared credential resolves the definition as the CUSTODIAN and\n                        \"never as the reader\" (definitionActorForCredential). The key is stamped\n                        with the RUNNER, who cannot see the custodian's private row, so the answer\n                        was the empty set and every peer's evidence went on a re-save that dropped\n                        nothing at all.\n  \"Who can still resolve this action\" has a different answer per reader, so a write-time answer on\n  behalf of readers the writer cannot see will keep being wrong - and being wrong there is\n  unrecoverable. Three rounds is evidence about the SHAPE, not the parameter.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/action-resolution.ts (tier 3) - THE ONE RESOLUTION\n  findConfigForOwner -> definitionActorForCredential -> resolveDefinition, extracted from the\n  executor, and action-executor.ts CALLS IT. That is the structural half of the fix: a retention\n  decision cannot believe something a run does not, because if this module is wrong execution is\n  wrong first, loudly. resolvableActionNamesForOwner projects it onto action NAMES with a THREE-WAY\n  answer - null (\"could not find out\") is never the empty set (\"resolves nothing\").\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/evidence-reconcile.ts (tier 3) - THE WRITE-TIME COLLECTOR\n  reconcileOwnOrgEvidence(orgId, integrationKey): the ORG IS A REQUIRED PARAMETER and every query\n  carries it, so the blast radius of the worst bug it can contain is the writing tenant. Bounded by\n  MAX_RECONCILED_OWNERS (25); above it, it stops and says so. Fails towards KEEPING at every step.\n\nTHE EDGE definition-store -> action-evidence-store IS REMOVED, REPLACED BY A SEAM\n  definition-store.ts declares DefinitionEvidenceReconciler + setDefinitionEvidenceReconciler and\n  calls it from create's replace branch, setVisibility AND publishSnapshot. evidence-reconcile.ts\n  implements it; server.ts binds it through bindDefinitionEvidenceReconciler(). A seam because the\n  store cannot import the resolution without a cycle (definition-registry -> definition-store), and\n  because calling it from the four higher-tier write sites would make reachability something four\n  authors must remember. Unbound => collects nothing, which is the safe direction.\n  action-evidence-store's CROSS-TENANT LISTING (listOwnerRefsForKey) IS DELETED, not narrowed: a\n  cross-tenant listing is what made a cross-tenant delete expressible. listOwnerRefsInOrg replaces\n  it, and takes the org as its first argument.\n\nTHE READER COLLECTS ITS OWN (action-executor.ts, third member of the executorDeps bundle)\n  The executor resolves for THIS org, owner, credential and document, so it is the only place the\n  answer is knowable. Its unknown_integration / unknown_action refusals call\n  discardOwnActionEvidence -> ActionEvidenceStore.discardOwnerEvidence, whose scope type REQUIRES\n  both tenancy terms and has no org-wide arm. Bundled with the other two seams so the third could\n  not half-land.\n\nAND THE ORPHAN IS BOUNDED RATHER THAN ARGUED AWAY\n  sweepExpiredEvidence at boot (EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90), ordered BEFORE the pin read inside\n  server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence so an expiring row releases its screenshot pin on\n  the SAME boot; DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence as the owner's own\n  erasure control (auth: 'user'); and deleteConfig's credential erasure, whose org-shared arm is now\n  an EXCLUSION LIST (findConfigForOwner answers a member's own row first, so a peer holding their\n  own credential was never served by the deleted one)."
