    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820e-s1r5-retention-is-not-synchronous",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 29200,
      "width": 747,
      "height": 1400.0,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (e) - S1 ROUND FIVE: retention stops being answered synchronously.\nRETIRES the collectors drawn in (b), (c) and (d). ONE module DELETED, one seam DELETED, two runtime\nedges REMOVED, one boot-path decision inverted. NO new module and no new edge.\n\nWHY (d) IS RETIRED AND NOT TUNED - AND (c) AND (b) WITH IT\n  (b) drew definition-store -> action-evidence-store as an action-set diff scoped to the writing org.\n  (c) redrew it as a CROSS-TENANT reconciler. (d) replaced both with two collectors that each asked\n  the ONE production resolution (action-resolution.ts): a reader-side one on the executor's refusal\n  branches, and a write-time seam scoped to the writing org. Four rounds, five defects:\n\n    two   the writing org's diff .......... ORPHANED every consumer of a `global` row\n    three every tenant, via getForActor ... DELETED ACROSS A TENANT BOUNDARY, twice over\n    four  the reader's own run ........... DELETED on TRANSIENT unreachability (a blip, a rotation,\n                                            a half-applied write - all the same branch)\n    four  the writing org's tier flip .... DELETED on an `org -> private` flip that was REVERTED\n    four  the boot screenshot sweep ...... SWEPT UNPINNED when the pin read failed\n\n  The cause is not the scope, the actor or the vantage. Every attempt answered \"is this action gone?\"\n  SYNCHRONOUSLY, at one instant, from one vantage, about a row whose lifetime is DURABLE. (d)'s\n  answers came from the best-informed vantage in the system with both tenancy terms required by the\n  type, and still destroyed data that was not stale. So the question is no longer asked.\n\nWHAT IS DELETED (grep these names; they no longer exist)\n  api/src/integrations/evidence-reconcile.ts ......... the whole module (round four's write-time\n                                                        collector, MAX_RECONCILED_OWNERS, and the\n                                                        bindDefinitionEvidenceReconciler binder).\n  definition-store.ts DefinitionEvidenceReconciler ... the seam, its setter, its test reset, and its\n                                                        THREE call sites: create(..., 'replace'),\n                                                        setVisibility and publishSnapshot.\n  action-executor.ts discardOwnActionEvidence ....... the executor seam and its two call sites on\n                                                        the unknown_integration / unknown_action\n                                                        refusals. ExecutorDeps carries CAPTURE seams\n                                                        only now; CapabilityContext.executorEvidence\n                                                        narrows to the same two.\n  action-evidence-store.ts discardOwnerEvidence ..... the reader-side removal primitive.\n  action-evidence-store.ts listOwnerRefsInOrg ....... the write-time collector's listing. Nothing in\n                                                        this codebase enumerates who holds a row.\n  action-resolution.ts resolvableActionNamesForOwner  the retention projection. Its two callers were\n                                                        the two collectors above.\n  server.ts .......................................... the discardOwnActionEvidence binding on the\n                                                        executorDeps bundle, the third member of the\n                                                        executorEvidence bundle handed to the\n                                                        integrations router, and the\n                                                        bindDefinitionEvidenceReconciler() line.\n\nEDGES AFTER THIS NOTE\n  definition-store.ts -> captured-calls-store.ts .... KEPT. A capture pile is named by the recipe ON\n                                                       THIS ROW, so the write durably removes the\n                                                       pointer and removing what it pointed at is a\n                                                       durable consequence. That is the difference\n                                                       from an evidence row, which is named by\n                                                       nothing this write can see.\n  definition-store.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts ... GONE. No edge, no seam, no binder.\n  action-executor.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts .... CAPTURE ONLY (recordActionEvidence via the\n                                                       injected seam). No removal edge.\n  action-executor.ts -> action-resolution.ts ........ KEPT, and now the ONLY consumer. The module\n                                                       answers for a RUN at the instant of the run;\n                                                       its header says DO NOT re-point a collector\n                                                       at it.\n  server.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts ............. sweepExpiredEvidence + pinnedRunIdsForRetention\n                                                       at boot, and recordEvidence on the bundle.\n\nTHE BOOT SWEEP, INVERTED (server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence)\n  It did pinnedRunIdsForRetention().catch(() => new Set()) and then SWEPT ANYWAY - a transient Mongo\n  failure on one read deleted every screenshot behind a LIVE, unexpired evidence row, across every\n  tenant at once (the tree is <root>/<automationId>/<runId> and carries no org), with no restore\n  path. A FAILED PIN READ NOW SKIPS THE SWEEP FOR THAT BOOT: the pin set is a precondition, not an\n  embellishment, and one boot of retained PNGs beats an unrecoverable deletion. Order is unchanged -\n  evidence TTL sweep, then the pin read, then the tree.\n\nWHAT ENDS A ROW NOW - three DURABLE signals, and nothing else\n  TIME ......... sweepExpiredEvidence at boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90. THE collector.\n  THE OWNER .... DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence, and deleteConfig's\n                  credential erasure (the same signal one step out - a durable removal of the\n                  credential whose account the sample holds, by the person who connected it).\n  A NEW SAMPLE   recordEvidence supersedes wholesale; the _id IS the tuple.\n\n  A definition edit, a tier flip, a re-publish and a failed resolve record NOTHING and delete\n  NOTHING. Deliberate trade, journaled in docs/decisions.md (S1 round five); the residual retention\n  window is OPEN in docs/findings.md as evidence-orphan-window-until-ttl and is NOT closed.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (e) - S1 ROUND FIVE: retention stops being answered synchronously.\nRETIRES the collectors drawn in (b), (c) and (d). ONE module DELETED, one seam DELETED, two runtime\nedges REMOVED, one boot-path decision inverted. NO new module and no new edge.\n\nWHY (d) IS RETIRED AND NOT TUNED - AND (c) AND (b) WITH IT\n  (b) drew definition-store -> action-evidence-store as an action-set diff scoped to the writing org.\n  (c) redrew it as a CROSS-TENANT reconciler. (d) replaced both with two collectors that each asked\n  the ONE production resolution (action-resolution.ts): a reader-side one on the executor's refusal\n  branches, and a write-time seam scoped to the writing org. Four rounds, five defects:\n\n    two   the writing org's diff .......... ORPHANED every consumer of a `global` row\n    three every tenant, via getForActor ... DELETED ACROSS A TENANT BOUNDARY, twice over\n    four  the reader's own run ........... DELETED on TRANSIENT unreachability (a blip, a rotation,\n                                            a half-applied write - all the same branch)\n    four  the writing org's tier flip .... DELETED on an `org -> private` flip that was REVERTED\n    four  the boot screenshot sweep ...... SWEPT UNPINNED when the pin read failed\n\n  The cause is not the scope, the actor or the vantage. Every attempt answered \"is this action gone?\"\n  SYNCHRONOUSLY, at one instant, from one vantage, about a row whose lifetime is DURABLE. (d)'s\n  answers came from the best-informed vantage in the system with both tenancy terms required by the\n  type, and still destroyed data that was not stale. So the question is no longer asked.\n\nWHAT IS DELETED (grep these names; they no longer exist)\n  api/src/integrations/evidence-reconcile.ts ......... the whole module (round four's write-time\n                                                        collector, MAX_RECONCILED_OWNERS, and the\n                                                        bindDefinitionEvidenceReconciler binder).\n  definition-store.ts DefinitionEvidenceReconciler ... the seam, its setter, its test reset, and its\n                                                        THREE call sites: create(..., 'replace'),\n                                                        setVisibility and publishSnapshot.\n  action-executor.ts discardOwnActionEvidence ....... the executor seam and its two call sites on\n                                                        the unknown_integration / unknown_action\n                                                        refusals. ExecutorDeps carries CAPTURE seams\n                                                        only now; CapabilityContext.executorEvidence\n                                                        narrows to the same two.\n  action-evidence-store.ts discardOwnerEvidence ..... the reader-side removal primitive.\n  action-evidence-store.ts listOwnerRefsInOrg ....... the write-time collector's listing. Nothing in\n                                                        this codebase enumerates who holds a row.\n  action-resolution.ts resolvableActionNamesForOwner  the retention projection. Its two callers were\n                                                        the two collectors above.\n  server.ts .......................................... the discardOwnActionEvidence binding on the\n                                                        executorDeps bundle, the third member of the\n                                                        executorEvidence bundle handed to the\n                                                        integrations router, and the\n                                                        bindDefinitionEvidenceReconciler() line.\n\nEDGES AFTER THIS NOTE\n  definition-store.ts -> captured-calls-store.ts .... KEPT. A capture pile is named by the recipe ON\n                                                       THIS ROW, so the write durably removes the\n                                                       pointer and removing what it pointed at is a\n                                                       durable consequence. That is the difference\n                                                       from an evidence row, which is named by\n                                                       nothing this write can see.\n  definition-store.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts ... GONE. No edge, no seam, no binder.\n  action-executor.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts .... CAPTURE ONLY (recordActionEvidence via the\n                                                       injected seam). No removal edge.\n  action-executor.ts -> action-resolution.ts ........ KEPT, and now the ONLY consumer. The module\n                                                       answers for a RUN at the instant of the run;\n                                                       its header says DO NOT re-point a collector\n                                                       at it.\n  server.ts -> action-evidence-store.ts ............. sweepExpiredEvidence + pinnedRunIdsForRetention\n                                                       at boot, and recordEvidence on the bundle.\n\nTHE BOOT SWEEP, INVERTED (server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence)\n  It did pinnedRunIdsForRetention().catch(() => new Set()) and then SWEPT ANYWAY - a transient Mongo\n  failure on one read deleted every screenshot behind a LIVE, unexpired evidence row, across every\n  tenant at once (the tree is <root>/<automationId>/<runId> and carries no org), with no restore\n  path. A FAILED PIN READ NOW SKIPS THE SWEEP FOR THAT BOOT: the pin set is a precondition, not an\n  embellishment, and one boot of retained PNGs beats an unrecoverable deletion. Order is unchanged -\n  evidence TTL sweep, then the pin read, then the tree.\n\nWHAT ENDS A ROW NOW - three DURABLE signals, and nothing else\n  TIME ......... sweepExpiredEvidence at boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90. THE collector.\n  THE OWNER .... DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence, and deleteConfig's\n                  credential erasure (the same signal one step out - a durable removal of the\n                  credential whose account the sample holds, by the person who connected it).\n  A NEW SAMPLE   recordEvidence supersedes wholesale; the _id IS the tuple.\n\n  A definition edit, a tier flip, a re-publish and a failed resolve record NOTHING and delete\n  NOTHING. Deliberate trade, journaled in docs/decisions.md (S1 round five); the residual retention\n  window is OPEN in docs/findings.md as evidence-orphan-window-until-ttl and is NOT closed.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (e) - S1 ROUND FIVE: retention stops being answered synchronously.\nRETIRES the collectors drawn in (b), (c) and (d). ONE module DELETED, one seam DELETED, two runtime\nedges REMOVED, one boot-path decision inverted. NO new module and no new edge.\n\nWHY (d) IS RETIRED AND NOT TUNED - AND (c) AND (b) WITH IT\n  (b) drew definition-store -> action-evidence-store as an action-set diff scoped to the writing org.\n  (c) redrew it as a CROSS-TENANT reconciler. (d) replaced both with two collectors that each asked\n  the ONE production resolution (action-resolution.ts): a reader-side one on the executor's refusal\n  branches, and a write-time seam scoped to the writing org. Four rounds, five defects:\n\n    two   the writing org's diff .......... ORPHANED every consumer of a `global` row\n    three every tenant, via getForActor ... DELETED ACROSS A TENANT BOUNDARY, twice over\n    four  the reader's own run ........... DELETED on TRANSIENT unreachability (a blip, a rotation,\n                                            a half-applied write - all the same branch)\n    four  the writing org's tier flip .... DELETED on an `org -> private` flip that was REVERTED\n    four  the boot screenshot sweep ...... SWEPT UNPINNED when the pin read failed\n\n  The cause is not the scope, the actor or the vantage. Every attempt answered \"is this action gone?\"\n  SYNCHRONOUSLY, at one instant, from one vantage, about a row whose lifetime is DURABLE. (d)'s\n  answers came from the best-informed vantage in the system with both tenancy terms required by the\n  type, and still destroyed data that was not stale. So the question is no longer asked.\n\nWHAT IS DELETED (grep these names; they no longer exist)\n  api/src/integrations/evidence-reconcile.ts ......... the whole module (round four's write-time\n                                                        collector, MAX_RECONCILED_OWNERS, and the\n                                                 