    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260821f-s1r7-evidence-seam-carries-the-cut",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 30800,
      "width": 747,
      "height": 490.0,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (f) - S1 ROUND SEVEN: the evidence seam carries the cut, and the screenshot\nsweep stops trusting its own default. AMENDS (e).\n\n1. THE EVIDENCE SEAM CARRIES A THIRD FACT (stored shape in 05-data-model (f)).\n   automation/action-evidence.ts -> [RunEvidenceCollector seam] -> integrations/action-executor.ts\n     -> [recordActionEvidence seam] -> integrations/action-evidence-store.ts\n   The seam type gains `truncated`. It CANNOT be re-derived downstream: the collector slices to 50\n   before the seam, so the store's own length test sees 50 > 50 and is false on every production row,\n   and a 200-step run was stored as an unmarked 50-step trace. Module direction is unchanged - the\n   collector still lives in automation/, and integrations/ still imports nothing from it.\n\n2. THE BOOT SWEEP'S SECOND BOUND IS NOW ENFORCED, AND GUARDED.\n   server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence\n     -> actionEvidenceStore.sweepExpiredEvidence({ now })         EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90\n     -> actionEvidenceStore.pinnedRunIdsForRetention()            (failure SKIPS the sweep - (e))\n     -> automation/screenshot-plane.sweepExpiredScreenshots({ now, pinnedRunIds })\n                                                                  DEFAULT_SCREENSHOT_RETENTION_DAYS = 7\n   The production caller passes NO retentionDays and rides the default, while every suite passed 7\n   EXPLICITLY - so the default was unenforced in both directions (7 -> 1 and 7 -> 36500 each left the\n   estate green). The security suite now exercises the default with no override, straddling the\n   cutoff by half a day either side.\n   sweepExpiredScreenshots also gains the non-positive guard its sibling sweepExpiredEvidence always\n   had: a 0, a negative or a NaN put the cutoff at or after `now` and deleted EVERY unpinned run\n   directory in the tree on the next boot. An unusable retention setting is not an instruction to\n   destroy the archive.\n\n3. NO NEW EDGE, NO NEW MODULE, NO SEAM REMOVED. Everything above is a field on an existing seam and a\n   guard inside an existing function.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (f) - S1 ROUND SEVEN: the evidence seam carries the cut, and the screenshot\nsweep stops trusting its own default. AMENDS (e).\n\n1. THE EVIDENCE SEAM CARRIES A THIRD FACT (stored shape in 05-data-model (f)).\n   automation/action-evidence.ts -> [RunEvidenceCollector seam] -> integrations/action-executor.ts\n     -> [recordActionEvidence seam] -> integrations/action-evidence-store.ts\n   The seam type gains `truncated`. It CANNOT be re-derived downstream: the collector slices to 50\n   before the seam, so the store's own length test sees 50 > 50 and is false on every production row,\n   and a 200-step run was stored as an unmarked 50-step trace. Module direction is unchanged - the\n   collector still lives in automation/, and integrations/ still imports nothing from it.\n\n2. THE BOOT SWEEP'S SECOND BOUND IS NOW ENFORCED, AND GUARDED.\n   server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence\n     -> actionEvidenceStore.sweepExpiredEvidence({ now })         EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90\n     -> actionEvidenceStore.pinnedRunIdsForRetention()            (failure SKIPS the sweep - (e))\n     -> automation/screenshot-plane.sweepExpiredScreenshots({ now, pinnedRunIds })\n                                                                  DEFAULT_SCREENSHOT_RETENTION_DAYS = 7\n   The production caller passes NO retentionDays and rides the default, while every suite passed 7\n   EXPLICITLY - so the default was unenforced in both directions (7 -> 1 and 7 -> 36500 each left the\n   estate green). The security suite now exercises the default with no override, straddling the\n   cutoff by half a day either side.\n   sweepExpiredScreenshots also gains the non-positive guard its sibling sweepExpiredEvidence always\n   had: a 0, a negative or a NaN put the cutoff at or after `now` and deleted EVERY unpinned run\n   directory in the tree on the next boot. An unusable retention setting is not an instruction to\n   destroy the archive.\n\n3. NO NEW EDGE, NO NEW MODULE, NO SEAM REMOVED. Everything above is a field on an existing seam and a\n   guard inside an existing function.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (f) - S1 ROUND SEVEN: the evidence seam carries the cut, and the screenshot\nsweep stops trusting its own default. AMENDS (e).\n\n1. THE EVIDENCE SEAM CARRIES A THIRD FACT (stored shape in 05-data-model (f)).\n   automation/action-evidence.ts -> [RunEvidenceCollector seam] -> integrations/action-executor.ts\n     -> [recordActionEvidence seam] -> integrations/action-evidence-store.ts\n   The seam type gains `truncated`. It CANNOT be re-derived downstream: the collector slices to 50\n   before the seam, so the store's own length test sees 50 > 50 and is false on every production row,\n   and a 200-step run was stored as an unmarked 50-step trace. Module direction is unchanged - the\n   collector still lives in automation/, and integrations/ still imports nothing from it.\n\n2. THE BOOT SWEEP'S SECOND BOUND IS NOW ENFORCED, AND GUARDED.\n   server.ts sweepScreenshotsSparingPinnedEvidence\n     -> actionEvidenceStore.sweepExpiredEvidence({ now })         EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90\n     -> actionEvidenceStore.pinnedRunIdsForRetention()            (failure SKIPS the sweep - (e))\n     -> automation/screenshot-plane.sweepExpiredScreenshots({ now, pinnedRunIds })\n                                                                  DEFAULT_SCREENSHOT_RETENTION_DAYS = 7\n   The production caller passes NO retentionDays and rides the default, while every suite passed 7\n   EXPLICITLY - so the default was unenforced in both directions (7 -> 1 and 7 -> 36500 each left the\n   estate green). The security suite now exercises the default with no override, straddling the\n   cutoff by half a day either side.\n   sweepExpiredScreenshots also gains the non-positive guard its sibling sweepExpiredEvidence always\n   had: a 0, a negative or a NaN put the cutoff at or after `now` and deleted EVERY unpinned run\n   directory in the tree on the next boot. An unusable retention setting is not an instruction to\n   destroy the archive.\n\n3. NO NEW EDGE, NO NEW MODULE, NO SEAM REMOVED. Everything above is a field on an existing seam and a\n   guard inside an existing function.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
