      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (i) - S6: THE PUBLISH DOORS ARE MOUNTED. AMENDS (h).\nNo new module and no new seam. What changes is REACHABILITY: five thin routes over machinery that\nwas built, tested and had ZERO non-test callers.\n\nWHAT WAS UNREACHABLE. `integrations/publish-scrub.ts` (previewPublish, publishDefinition) and\n`integrations/definition-store.ts` (requestPublish, withdrawPublishRequest, listPublishRequests)\nwere called from unit tests and from nothing else. The submit-for-review window slice E2 built -\nthe ONE thing that puts a tenant row in front of a platform reviewer who is not a member of the org\n(isDefinitionVisibleTo) - could not be opened, so the review queue behind it had never been\nreachable in the running product.\n\nNEW EDGES (both from the route layer, both into modules it already reached):\n  routes/integrations.ts -> integrations/publish-scrub.ts     previewPublish, publishDefinition,\n                                                              scrubPublishText\n  routes/integrations.ts -> integrations/definition-store.ts  three more methods on the edge that\n                                                              already carried setVisibility\n\nTHE FIVE ROUTES, all inside TIER 2's literal-segment block (above the `/:key` capability routes, so\n`:key` cannot swallow `definitions`), and inside it the literal before the parameter:\n  GET    /api/v1/integrations/definitions/publish-requests        super-admin  (registered FIRST)\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-request     user\n  DELETE /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-request     user\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-preview     user\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish             super-admin\n\nADMISSION: NONE is `user-or-key`. setGlobal's rule - a key must never publish to every org -\nextends to the three `user` doors for the reason C2's consent routes and C3's lessons are `user`:\nthe note is free text a reviewer reads while deciding to promote a package to every tenant, the\nwithdraw is the tenant's own decision, and the preview's admission set is JWT principals.\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE PUBLIC SPEC: the OpenAPI document is generated from the `user-or-key`\ndescriptors and nothing else, so it is byte-unchanged by this slice, and so is the cortex-cli\nclient generated from it.\n\nTHE CHOKEPOINT IS UNTOUCHED (FIXED-3/8/13). publish-scrub.ts still reaches the model only through\nllm/completeFast; S6 puts an HTTP caller in front of that path and adds no egress. The two\nsuper-admin doors mount requireRole as defense in depth beside the store's own bar, exactly as\n/definitions/:id/global does.\n\nTWO NEW PURE PROJECTIONS in publish-scrub.ts, both read-free and write-free:\n  publishableActionOf    - a WHITELIST over IntegrationAction (see diagram 05)\n  publishableAuthoringOf - the identifying half of the D3 authoring record removed",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (i) - S6: THE PUBLISH DOORS ARE MOUNTED. AMENDS (h).\nNo new module and no new seam. What changes is REACHABILITY: five thin routes over machinery that\nwas built, tested and had ZERO non-test callers.\n\nWHAT WAS UNREACHABLE. `integrations/publish-scrub.ts` (previewPublish, publishDefinition) and\n`integrations/definition-store.ts` (requestPublish, withdrawPublishRequest, listPublishRequests)\nwere called from unit tests and from nothing else. The submit-for-review window slice E2 built -\nthe ONE thing that puts a tenant row in front of a platform reviewer who is not a member of the org\n(isDefinitionVisibleTo) - could not be opened, so the review queue behind it had never been\nreachable in the running product.\n\nNEW EDGES (both from the route layer, both into modules it already reached):\n  routes/integrations.ts -> integrations/publish-scrub.ts     previewPublish, publishDefinition,\n                                                              scrubPublishText\n  routes/integrations.ts -> integrations/definition-store.ts  three more methods on the edge that\n                                                              already carried setVisibility\n\nTHE FIVE ROUTES, all inside TIER 2's literal-segment block (above the `/:key` capability routes, so\n`:key` cannot swallow `definitions`), and inside it the literal before the parameter:\n  GET    /api/v1/integrations/definitions/publish-requests        super-admin  (registered FIRST)\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-request     user\n  DELETE /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-request     user\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-preview     user\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish             super-admin\n\nADMISSION: NONE is `user-or-key`. setGlobal's rule - a key must never publish to every org -\nextends to the three `user` doors for the reason C2's consent routes and C3's lessons are `user`:\nthe note is free text a reviewer reads while deciding to promote a package to every tenant, the\nwithdraw is the tenant's own decision, and the preview's admission set is JWT principals.\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE PUBLIC SPEC: the OpenAPI document is generated from the `user-or-key`\ndescriptors and nothing else, so it is byte-unchanged by this slice, and so is the cortex-cli\nclient generated from it.\n\nTHE CHOKEPOINT IS UNTOUCHED (FIXED-3/8/13). publish-scrub.ts still reaches the model only through\nllm/completeFast; S6 puts an HTTP caller in front of that path and adds no egress. The two\nsuper-admin doors mount requireRole as defense in depth beside the store's own bar, exactly as\n/definitions/:id/global does.\n\nTWO NEW PURE PROJECTIONS in publish-scrub.ts, both read-free and write-free:\n  publishableActionOf    - a WHITELIST over IntegrationAction (see diagram 05)\n  publishableAuthoringOf - the identifying half of the D3 authoring record removed",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (i) - S6: THE PUBLISH DOORS ARE MOUNTED. AMENDS (h).\nNo new module and no new seam. What changes is REACHABILITY: five thin routes over machinery that\nwas built, tested and had ZERO non-test callers.\n\nWHAT WAS UNREACHABLE. `integrations/publish-scrub.ts` (previewPublish, publishDefinition) and\n`integrations/definition-store.ts` (requestPublish, withdrawPublishRequest, listPublishRequests)\nwere called from unit tests and from nothing else. The submit-for-review window slice E2 built -\nthe ONE thing that puts a tenant row in front of a platform reviewer who is not a member of the org\n(isDefinitionVisibleTo) - could not be opened, so the review queue behind it had never been\nreachable in the running product.\n\nNEW EDGES (both from the route layer, both into modules it already reached):\n  routes/integrations.ts -> integrations/publish-scrub.ts     previewPublish, publishDefinition,\n                                                              scrubPublishText\n  routes/integrations.ts -> integrations/definition-store.ts  three more methods on the edge that\n                                                              already carried setVisibility\n\nTHE FIVE ROUTES, all inside TIER 2's literal-segment block (above the `/:key` capability routes, so\n`:key` cannot swallow `definitions`), and inside it the literal before the parameter:\n  GET    /api/v1/integrations/definitions/publish-requests        super-admin  (registered FIRST)\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-request     user\n  DELETE /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-request     user\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish-preview     user\n  POST   /api/v1/integrations/definitions/:id/publish             super-admin\n\nADMISSION: NONE is `user-or-key`. setGlobal's rule - a key must never publish to every org -\nextends to the three `user` doors for the reason C2's consent routes and C3's lessons are `user`:\nthe note is free text a reviewer reads while deciding to promote a package to every tenant, the\nwithdraw is the tenant's own decision, and the preview's admission set is JWT principals.\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE PUBLIC SPEC: the OpenAPI document is generated from the `user-or-key`\ndescriptors and nothing else, so it is byte-unchanged by this slice, and so is the cortex-cli\nclient generated from it.\n\nTHE CHOKEPOINT IS UNTOUCHED (FIXED-3/8/13). publish-scrub.ts still reaches the model only through\nllm/completeFast; S6 puts an HTTP caller in front of that path and adds no egress. The two\nsuper-admin doors mount requireRole as defense in depth beside the store's own bar, exactly as\n/definitions/:id/global does.\n\nTWO NEW PURE PROJECTIONS in publish-scrub.ts, both read-free and write-free:\n  publishableActionOf    - a WHITELIST over IntegrationAction (see diagram 05)\n  publishableAuthoringOf - the identifying half of the D3 authoring record removed",
