      "text": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21f (S4+S5 verification round SIX) - THE COMPOSE RUNG MOVED BELOW THE EXECUTE,\nBECAUSE THAT IS WHERE THE FIELD NAMES ARE. Extends notes (c), (d) and (e); none is wrong, all three\nwere about a rung drawn in the wrong PLACE. Journal: D-S5-5.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWED, AND WHAT WAS WRONG WITH IT\n  achieve.runMatchedAction  --(1)-->  planComposition  --> [model turn] --> plan\n                            --(2)-->  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction --> 200 + rows\n                            --(3)-->  applyComposition(plan, rows) --> items\n  Edge (1) ran FIRST, so the only facts the planning turn could be given were facts known before any\n  request went out: the action's name, its one-line description, \"changes data: no\", and the NAMES of\n  the caller's collections. NOT ONE FIELD NAME, from either side - not a key of the action's\n  response, not a key of a collection row.\n  And composeOutputContract() demanded THREE field names back: where.field, join.resultField,\n  join.collectionField. So the model had no way to answer except to INVENT identifiers, and\n  verifyComposePlan accepted any non-empty string for all three.\n\nWHY THAT IS A DATA-CORRECTION DEFECT AND NOT A PROMPT-QUALITY ONE\n  An invented field name does not fail. matchesSimpleQuery reads an absent field as undefined, which\n  is a VALUE, so the predicate answers definitely for every row:\n    \"age\" for \"idade\" under lt/lte/gt/gte -> Number(undefined) is NaN -> NOTHING matches\n    \"age\" for \"idade\" under neq           -> true for every row -> the filter VANISHES (too wide)\n    \"_id\" for \"id\"                        -> the join key set is empty -> nothing matches\n    \"clientId\" for \"clienteId\"            -> no action row carries the key -> nothing matches\n  Each came back 200 { outcome: \"composed\", items: [...], composition: {...} } - well formed,\n  confident, with a full narrowing report. For the canonical goal the failure shape is A SHORTER LIST\n  OF CASES, and a lawyer cannot tell a correctly-filtered docket from a wrongly-narrowed one.\n\nTHE MAP NOW\n  achieve.runMatchedAction  --(1)-->  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction --> 200 + rows\n                            --(2)-->  composeOver(goal, action, result)\n                                        planComposition -> draftCompositionPlan\n                                          mutates gate (FIRST, unmoved) -> result.success ->\n                                          residue -> seams -> rowsOf -> rows.length ->\n                                          fieldsOf(rows)  ......... the ACTION field set, exact\n                                          appCollections.list ..... the COLLECTION field sets, exact\n                                          allowance -> [model turn] -> verifyComposePlan(plan,\n                                                                 collections, resultFields)\n                                        applyComposition -> read -> composeRows\n\n  TWO SEAM CHANGES ON THE MAP\n   - AppCollections.list now answers ComposeCollection[] = { name, fields }, bound in server.ts to\n     CollectionsEngine.listCollectionFields (replacing listCollections). ONE aggregation, matching on\n     the same single query-binding point every other read uses: appId: scope.scopeKey.\n   - composeSections(action, collections, resultFields) renders both sets. verifyComposePlan refuses\n     any name outside them - a deterministic refusal of the PLAN, never of the CALL.\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE, STATED SO THE EARLIER NOTES ARE NOT READ AS SUPERSEDED\n   - THE mutates GATE IS STILL FIRST. It is the first statement in the planning stage, so a WRITE\n     still reaches no model, no collection lister and no store. Only WHEN the rung runs changed.\n   - THE WORKER/RECORDER SPLIT OF NOTE (e) IS INTACT. draftCompositionPlan/attemptComposition do the\n     work and may throw; planComposition/applyComposition convert every outcome - a rejection\n     included - into exactly one ladder step plus a null. There is still no path from \"the\n     composition could not be built\" to \"the caller loses the executed answer\".\n   - THE EXECUTED ARM IS BYTE-IDENTICAL when the rung stands down.\n\nAND FOUR EDGES THAT USED TO COST A METERED MODEL CALL NOW COST NOTHING: a failed execute, a result\nwith several lists in it, a result with no list at all, and a result with zero rows all leave the\nplanning stage before ctx.planStep is reached.",
      "rawText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21f (S4+S5 verification round SIX) - THE COMPOSE RUNG MOVED BELOW THE EXECUTE,\nBECAUSE THAT IS WHERE THE FIELD NAMES ARE. Extends notes (c), (d) and (e); none is wrong, all three\nwere about a rung drawn in the wrong PLACE. Journal: D-S5-5.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWED, AND WHAT WAS WRONG WITH IT\n  achieve.runMatchedAction  --(1)-->  planComposition  --> [model turn] --> plan\n                            --(2)-->  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction --> 200 + rows\n                            --(3)-->  applyComposition(plan, rows) --> items\n  Edge (1) ran FIRST, so the only facts the planning turn could be given were facts known before any\n  request went out: the action's name, its one-line description, \"changes data: no\", and the NAMES of\n  the caller's collections. NOT ONE FIELD NAME, from either side - not a key of the action's\n  response, not a key of a collection row.\n  And composeOutputContract() demanded THREE field names back: where.field, join.resultField,\n  join.collectionField. So the model had no way to answer except to INVENT identifiers, and\n  verifyComposePlan accepted any non-empty string for all three.\n\nWHY THAT IS A DATA-CORRECTION DEFECT AND NOT A PROMPT-QUALITY ONE\n  An invented field name does not fail. matchesSimpleQuery reads an absent field as undefined, which\n  is a VALUE, so the predicate answers definitely for every row:\n    \"age\" for \"idade\" under lt/lte/gt/gte -> Number(undefined) is NaN -> NOTHING matches\n    \"age\" for \"idade\" under neq           -> true for every row -> the filter VANISHES (too wide)\n    \"_id\" for \"id\"                        -> the join key set is empty -> nothing matches\n    \"clientId\" for \"clienteId\"            -> no action row carries the key -> nothing matches\n  Each came back 200 { outcome: \"composed\", items: [...], composition: {...} } - well formed,\n  confident, with a full narrowing report. For the canonical goal the failure shape is A SHORTER LIST\n  OF CASES, and a lawyer cannot tell a correctly-filtered docket from a wrongly-narrowed one.\n\nTHE MAP NOW\n  achieve.runMatchedAction  --(1)-->  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction --> 200 + rows\n                            --(2)-->  composeOver(goal, action, result)\n                                        planComposition -> draftCompositionPlan\n                                          mutates gate (FIRST, unmoved) -> result.success ->\n                                          residue -> seams -> rowsOf -> rows.length ->\n                                          fieldsOf(rows)  ......... the ACTION field set, exact\n                                          appCollections.list ..... the COLLECTION field sets, exact\n                                          allowance -> [model turn] -> verifyComposePlan(plan,\n                                                                 collections, resultFields)\n                                        applyComposition -> read -> composeRows\n\n  TWO SEAM CHANGES ON THE MAP\n   - AppCollections.list now answers ComposeCollection[] = { name, fields }, bound in server.ts to\n     CollectionsEngine.listCollectionFields (replacing listCollections). ONE aggregation, matching on\n     the same single query-binding point every other read uses: appId: scope.scopeKey.\n   - composeSections(action, collections, resultFields) renders both sets. verifyComposePlan refuses\n     any name outside them - a deterministic refusal of the PLAN, never of the CALL.\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE, STATED SO THE EARLIER NOTES ARE NOT READ AS SUPERSEDED\n   - THE mutates GATE IS STILL FIRST. It is the first statement in the planning stage, so a WRITE\n     still reaches no model, no collection lister and no store. Only WHEN the rung runs changed.\n   - THE WORKER/RECORDER SPLIT OF NOTE (e) IS INTACT. draftCompositionPlan/attemptComposition do the\n     work and may throw; planComposition/applyComposition convert every outcome - a rejection\n     included - into exactly one ladder step plus a null. There is still no path from \"the\n     composition could not be built\" to \"the caller loses the executed answer\".\n   - THE EXECUTED ARM IS BYTE-IDENTICAL when the rung stands down.\n\nAND FOUR EDGES THAT USED TO COST A METERED MODEL CALL NOW COST NOTHING: a failed execute, a result\nwith several lists in it, a result with no list at all, and a result with zero rows all leave the\nplanning stage before ctx.planStep is reached.",
      "originalText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21f (S4+S5 verification round SIX) - THE COMPOSE RUNG MOVED BELOW THE EXECUTE,\nBECAUSE THAT IS WHERE THE FIELD NAMES ARE. Extends notes (c), (d) and (e); none is wrong, all three\nwere about a rung drawn in the wrong PLACE. Journal: D-S5-5.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWED, AND WHAT WAS WRONG WITH IT\n  achieve.runMatchedAction  --(1)-->  planComposition  --> [model turn] --> plan\n                            --(2)-->  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction --> 200 + rows\n                            --(3)-->  applyComposition(plan, rows) --> items\n  Edge (1) ran FIRST, so the only facts the planning turn could be given were facts known before any\n  request went out: the action's name, its one-line description, \"changes data: no\", and the NAMES of\n  the caller's collections. NOT ONE FIELD NAME, from either side - not a key of the action's\n  response, not a key of a collection row.\n  And composeOutputContract() demanded THREE field names back: where.field, join.resultField,\n  join.collectionField. So the model had no way to answer except to INVENT identifiers, and\n  verifyComposePlan accepted any non-empty string for all three.\n\nWHY THAT IS A DATA-CORRECTION DEFECT AND NOT A PROMPT-QUALITY ONE\n  An invented field name does not fail. matchesSimpleQuery reads an absent field as undefined, which\n  is a VALUE, so the predicate answers definitely for every row:\n    \"age\" for \"idade\" under lt/lte/gt/gte -> Number(undefined) is NaN -> NOTHING matches\n    \"age\" for \"idade\" under neq           -> true for every row -> the filter VANISHES (too wide)\n    \"_id\" for \"id\"                        -> the join key set is empty -> nothing matches\n    \"clientId\" for \"clienteId\"            -> no action row carries the key -> nothing matches\n  Each came back 200 { outcome: \"composed\", items: [...], composition: {...} } - well formed,\n  confident, with a full narrowing report. For the canonical goal the failure shape is A SHORTER LIST\n  OF CASES, and a lawyer cannot tell a correctly-filtered docket from a wrongly-narrowed one.\n\nTHE MAP NOW\n  achieve.runMatchedAction  --(1)-->  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction --> 200 + rows\n                            --(2)-->  composeOver(goal, action, result)\n                                        planComposition -> draftCompositionPlan\n                                          mutates gate (FIRST, unmoved) -> result.success ->\n                                          residue -> seams -> rowsOf -> rows.length ->\n                                          fieldsOf(rows)  ......... the ACTION field set, exact\n                                          appCollections.list ..... the COLLECTION field sets, exact\n                                          allowance -> [model turn] -> verifyComposePlan(plan,\n                                                                 collections, resultFields)\n                                        applyComposition -> read -> composeRows\n\n  TWO SEAM CHANGES ON THE MAP\n   - AppCollections.list now answers ComposeCollection[] = { name, fields }, bound in server.ts to\n     CollectionsEngine.listCollectionFields (replacing listCollections). ONE aggregation, matching on\n     the same single query-binding point every other read uses: appId: scope.scopeKey.\n   - composeSections(action, collections, resultFields) renders both sets. verifyComposePlan refuses\n     any name outside them - a deterministic refusal of the PLAN, never of the CALL.\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE, STATED SO THE EARLIER NOTES ARE NOT READ AS SUPERSEDED\n   - THE mutates GATE IS STILL FIRST. It is the first statement in the planning stage, so a WRITE\n     still reaches no model, no collection lister and no store. Only WHEN the rung runs changed.\n   - THE WORKER/RECORDER SPLIT OF NOTE (e) IS INTACT. draftCompositionPlan/attemptComposition do the\n     work and may throw; planComposition/applyComposition convert every outcome - a rejection\n     included - into exactly one ladder step plus a null. There is still no path from \"the\n     composition could not be built\" to \"the caller loses the executed answer\".\n   - THE EXECUTED ARM IS BYTE-IDENTICAL when the rung stands down.\n\nAND FOUR EDGES THAT USED TO COST A METERED MODEL CALL NOW COST NOTHING: a failed execute, a result\nwith several lists in it, a result with no list at all, and a result with zero rows all leave the\nplanning stage before ctx.planStep is reached.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "correction-20260821g-parametrize-gets-the-split",
      "containerId": null,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 33422.5,
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 910,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
