      "originalText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21h (S4+S5 verification round EIGHT) - THE MAP STOPPED AT THE ROUTE, AND SO DID\nSEVEN ROUNDS OF VERIFICATION. Extends notes (c)-(g). Journal: D-S4-4/D-S5-7.\n\nWHAT THE MAP DID NOT DRAW\n  Every note above ends at `routes/integrations.ts`. But a capability is exposed as a versioned\n  public API and its consumers are ordinary API clients (Rule 1, Rule 3) - and this repo SHIPS one,\n  `clients/cortex-cli`, generated from docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json. Nothing on this map said the\n  ladder's answer has to survive it. It did not:\n\n    POST /:key/achieve -> 200 { outcome: 'composed', items: [...], composition: {...} }\n      -> clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts  achieve()\n           if (body.outcome === 'executed') { ... } else { throw RuntimeFailure('authored') }\n      -> exit 1, \"was written ... as provisional and has NOT run\", stdout EMPTY\n\n  A trusted read ran, the rows were narrowed against the caller's own collection, and the client\n  reported a FAILED goal that had minted something. A rung whose answer is correct at the route and\n  wrong at the client is wrong; this one was correct at the route for seven rounds.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWS NOW - THE EDGE, AND THE TEST THAT STANDS ON IT\n  api/src/routes/integrations.ts   POST /:key/achieve\n    ONE projection for BOTH arms that ran the action (executed | composed), through\n    capabilityWireOutcome. `composed` used to bypass it entirely on a bare res.json(result), which\n    is how it reached the wire with no `result` at all.\n      |\n      v\n  clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts   achieve()\n    executed | composed -> refuseFailedAction(result) -> print (printComposedResult for composed)\n    authored  | refused -> exit 1\n    the consent 403 -> reportingConsent + modelDecisionLines: the descriptor, then the arguments a\n    model filled WITH THEIR VALUES, then the rungs\n      ^\n      |\n  clients/cortex-cli/tests/achieve-ladder.e2e.test.ts   (NEW FILE)\n    the BUILT binary spawned against buildApp over mongodb-memory-server: argv, the generated\n    client, HTTP, the real routers, the real executor and the process exit code. Two fakes, both at\n    the edges - guardedFetch and agents/authoring-core - exactly the pair the api contract suite\n    uses, and nothing between them is stubbed.\n\nONE NEW AUDIT WRITER IN integration-achieve.ts\n  auditParametrized(ctx, key, action, filled, result), beside auditComposed and auditAuthored:\n  the durable copy of the VALUES a model chose, written after the ONE gated execute and before\n  either exit of runMatchedAction, whatever the call then did. The row itself is in 05-data-model\n  note (h).\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  - the PICK is still `matchActionForGoal`, lexical and deterministic; the ONE call to the gated\n    executor is still exactly one call, in the same place.\n  - no module changed tier and no import boundary moved: `clients/<pkg>/src` + `bin` still import\n    `shared/` only. The e2e TEST imports `api/` under the carve-out `e2e.test.ts` already documents\n    (a harness that boots the provider is not a consumer reaching into it).",
      "rawText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21h (S4+S5 verification round EIGHT) - THE MAP STOPPED AT THE ROUTE, AND SO DID\nSEVEN ROUNDS OF VERIFICATION. Extends notes (c)-(g). Journal: D-S4-4/D-S5-7.\n\nWHAT THE MAP DID NOT DRAW\n  Every note above ends at `routes/integrations.ts`. But a capability is exposed as a versioned\n  public API and its consumers are ordinary API clients (Rule 1, Rule 3) - and this repo SHIPS one,\n  `clients/cortex-cli`, generated from docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json. Nothing on this map said the\n  ladder's answer has to survive it. It did not:\n\n    POST /:key/achieve -> 200 { outcome: 'composed', items: [...], composition: {...} }\n      -> clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts  achieve()\n           if (body.outcome === 'executed') { ... } else { throw RuntimeFailure('authored') }\n      -> exit 1, \"was written ... as provisional and has NOT run\", stdout EMPTY\n\n  A trusted read ran, the rows were narrowed against the caller's own collection, and the client\n  reported a FAILED goal that had minted something. A rung whose answer is correct at the route and\n  wrong at the client is wrong; this one was correct at the route for seven rounds.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWS NOW - THE EDGE, AND THE TEST THAT STANDS ON IT\n  api/src/routes/integrations.ts   POST /:key/achieve\n    ONE projection for BOTH arms that ran the action (executed | composed), through\n    capabilityWireOutcome. `composed` used to bypass it entirely on a bare res.json(result), which\n    is how it reached the wire with no `result` at all.\n      |\n      v\n  clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts   achieve()\n    executed | composed -> refuseFailedAction(result) -> print (printComposedResult for composed)\n    authored  | refused -> exit 1\n    the consent 403 -> reportingConsent + modelDecisionLines: the descriptor, then the arguments a\n    model filled WITH THEIR VALUES, then the rungs\n      ^\n      |\n  clients/cortex-cli/tests/achieve-ladder.e2e.test.ts   (NEW FILE)\n    the BUILT binary spawned against buildApp over mongodb-memory-server: argv, the generated\n    client, HTTP, the real routers, the real executor and the process exit code. Two fakes, both at\n    the edges - guardedFetch and agents/authoring-core - exactly the pair the api contract suite\n    uses, and nothing between them is stubbed.\n\nONE NEW AUDIT WRITER IN integration-achieve.ts\n  auditParametrized(ctx, key, action, filled, result), beside auditComposed and auditAuthored:\n  the durable copy of the VALUES a model chose, written after the ONE gated execute and before\n  either exit of runMatchedAction, whatever the call then did. The row itself is in 05-data-model\n  note (h).\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  - the PICK is still `matchActionForGoal`, lexical and deterministic; the ONE call to the gated\n    executor is still exactly one call, in the same place.\n  - no module changed tier and no import boundary moved: `clients/<pkg>/src` + `bin` still import\n    `shared/` only. The e2e TEST imports `api/` under the carve-out `e2e.test.ts` already documents\n    (a harness that boots the provider is not a consumer reaching into it).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21h (S4+S5 verification round EIGHT) - THE MAP STOPPED AT THE ROUTE, AND SO DID\nSEVEN ROUNDS OF VERIFICATION. Extends notes (c)-(g). Journal: D-S4-4/D-S5-7.\n\nWHAT THE MAP DID NOT DRAW\n  Every note above ends at `routes/integrations.ts`. But a capability is exposed as a versioned\n  public API and its consumers are ordinary API clients (Rule 1, Rule 3) - and this repo SHIPS one,\n  `clients/cortex-cli`, generated from docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json. Nothing on this map said the\n  ladder's answer has to survive it. It did not:\n\n    POST /:key/achieve -> 200 { outcome: 'composed', items: [...], composition: {...} }\n      -> clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts  achieve()\n           if (body.outcome === 'executed') { ... } else { throw RuntimeFailure('authored') }\n      -> exit 1, \"was written ... as provisional and has NOT run\", stdout EMPTY\n\n  A trusted read ran, the rows were narrowed against the caller's own collection, and the client\n  reported a FAILED goal that had minted something. A rung whose answer is correct at the route and\n  wrong at the client is wrong; this one was correct at the route for seven rounds.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWS NOW - THE EDGE, AND THE TEST THAT STANDS ON IT\n  api/src/routes/integrations.ts   POST /:key/achieve\n    ONE projection for BOTH arms that ran the action (executed | composed), through\n    capabilityWireOutcome. `composed` used to bypass it entirely on a bare res.json(result), which\n    is how it reached the wire with no `result` at all.\n      |\n      v\n  clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts   achieve()\n    executed | composed -> refuseFailedAction(result) -> print (printComposedResult for composed)\n    authored  | refused -> exit 1\n    the consent 403 -> reportingConsent + modelDecisionLines: the descriptor, then the arguments a\n    model filled WITH THEIR VALUES, then the rungs\n      ^\n      |\n  clients/cortex-cli/tests/achieve-ladder.e2e.test.ts   (NEW FILE)\n    the BUILT binary spawned against buildApp over mongodb-memory-server: argv, the generated\n    client, HTTP, the real routers, the real executor and the process exit code. Two fakes, both at\n    the edges - guardedFetch and agents/authoring-core - exactly the pair the api contract suite\n    uses, and nothing between them is stubbed.\n\nONE NEW AUDIT WRITER IN integration-achieve.ts\n  auditParametrized(ctx, key, action, filled, result), beside auditComposed and auditAuthored:\n  the durable copy of the VALUES a model chose, written after the ONE gated execute and before\n  either exit of runMatchedAction, whatever the call then did. The row itself is in 05-data-model\n  note (h).\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  - the PICK is still `matchActionForGoal`, lexical and deterministic; the ONE call to the gated\n    executor is still exactly one call, in the same place.\n  - no module changed tier and no import boundary moved: `clients/<pkg>/src` + `bin` still import\n    `shared/` only. The e2e TEST imports `api/` under the carve-out `e2e.test.ts` already documents\n    (a harness that boots the provider is not a consumer reaching into it)."
    },
