      "originalText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21i (S4+S5 verification round NINE) - THE RECORD MOVES ABOVE THE WRITE, THE\nMINT RUNG APPEARS ON THE MAP, AND THE CLIENT EDGE GROWS ITS SECOND HALF. Extends notes (c)-(h).\nJournal: D-S4-5/D-S5-8.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWED, AND WHAT WAS WRONG WITH IT\n  Note (h) drew the durable record of a model's choice as a step of runMatchedAction sitting AFTER\n  the one gated execute, with its own catch:\n\n    runMatchedAction\n      RUNG 2  parametrizeArgs  -> args\n      RUNG 1  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction   <-- the irreversible third-party call\n              auditParametrized (try/catch, swallow)  <-- the ONLY record of what a model chose\n      RUNG 3  composeOver\n\n  The record could therefore be absent EXACTLY when the write it describes had succeeded. An audit\n  row that goes missing on the runs that mattered is not an audit trail.\n\n  The author arm was drawn as a plain branch of achieveIntegrationGoal with no rung on it at all,\n  which is why AchieveRung published `mint` and nothing anywhere pushed it.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWS NOW\n  integration-achieve.ts\n    achieveIntegrationGoal\n      match = matchActionForGoal            LEXICAL, DETERMINISTIC, unchanged\n        one + trusted -> runMatchedAction\n        none          -> THE MINT RUNG (the author arm)\n                         ladder = [ reuse: skipped ]  <- why anything is being minted\n                         ... draft -> verify -> persist ...\n                         ladder += [ mint: taken ]    <- the rung that answered\n                         every other exit here is a REFUSAL, and a refusal carries NO ladder\n\n    runMatchedAction\n      RUNG 2  parametrizeArgs           RECORDER  one try per guarded await, one ladder step\n                |- draftParametrizedArgs   WORKER  seams, MAY throw, writes nothing\n                `- recordParametrization   WRITE   activityLogs, MAY throw, does NOT catch\n                                                   rejection -> rung STANDS DOWN (caller's args,\n                                                   ladder `unavailable`) - never a refusal\n      RUNG 1  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction -> auditExecute (capability_execute)\n      RUNG 3  composeOver -> planComposition / applyComposition  (unchanged)\n\n  The order is the invariant: the choice is RECORDED, then the third party is CALLED, then what\n  happened is recorded. If the record cannot be written, the choice is not made.\n\nTHE CLIENT EDGE, SECOND HALF\n  clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts\n    achieve --json   -> the whole body, unchanged\n    achieve (human)  -> ok line (+ upstream status)\n                        composed line (+ \"PART of the answer\" when either cap fired)\n                        THE ACTION'S OWN ANSWER, WHOLE   <-- new; was dropped entirely\n                        rows kept\n\n  Note (h) fixed the machine path and left the human one printing `items` alone, so a `nextPage`\n  cursor beside the list reached --json and never reached a person. The envelope is printed ABOVE\n  the rows because `items` is capped at 200.\n\n  clients/cortex-cli/SKILL.md is on this edge too, and is now CHECKED-AGAINST rather than\n  hand-kept: its outcome table is tested against docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json and its exit column\n  against the exit code the built binary really produces.\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  - the PICK is still matchActionForGoal, lexical and deterministic; the ONE call to the gated\n    executor is still exactly one call, in the same place.\n  - no module changed tier and no import boundary moved.",
      "rawText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21i (S4+S5 verification round NINE) - THE RECORD MOVES ABOVE THE WRITE, THE\nMINT RUNG APPEARS ON THE MAP, AND THE CLIENT EDGE GROWS ITS SECOND HALF. Extends notes (c)-(h).\nJournal: D-S4-5/D-S5-8.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWED, AND WHAT WAS WRONG WITH IT\n  Note (h) drew the durable record of a model's choice as a step of runMatchedAction sitting AFTER\n  the one gated execute, with its own catch:\n\n    runMatchedAction\n      RUNG 2  parametrizeArgs  -> args\n      RUNG 1  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction   <-- the irreversible third-party call\n              auditParametrized (try/catch, swallow)  <-- the ONLY record of what a model chose\n      RUNG 3  composeOver\n\n  The record could therefore be absent EXACTLY when the write it describes had succeeded. An audit\n  row that goes missing on the runs that mattered is not an audit trail.\n\n  The author arm was drawn as a plain branch of achieveIntegrationGoal with no rung on it at all,\n  which is why AchieveRung published `mint` and nothing anywhere pushed it.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWS NOW\n  integration-achieve.ts\n    achieveIntegrationGoal\n      match = matchActionForGoal            LEXICAL, DETERMINISTIC, unchanged\n        one + trusted -> runMatchedAction\n        none          -> THE MINT RUNG (the author arm)\n                         ladder = [ reuse: skipped ]  <- why anything is being minted\n                         ... draft -> verify -> persist ...\n                         ladder += [ mint: taken ]    <- the rung that answered\n                         every other exit here is a REFUSAL, and a refusal carries NO ladder\n\n    runMatchedAction\n      RUNG 2  parametrizeArgs           RECORDER  one try per guarded await, one ladder step\n                |- draftParametrizedArgs   WORKER  seams, MAY throw, writes nothing\n                `- recordParametrization   WRITE   activityLogs, MAY throw, does NOT catch\n                                                   rejection -> rung STANDS DOWN (caller's args,\n                                                   ladder `unavailable`) - never a refusal\n      RUNG 1  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction -> auditExecute (capability_execute)\n      RUNG 3  composeOver -> planComposition / applyComposition  (unchanged)\n\n  The order is the invariant: the choice is RECORDED, then the third party is CALLED, then what\n  happened is recorded. If the record cannot be written, the choice is not made.\n\nTHE CLIENT EDGE, SECOND HALF\n  clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts\n    achieve --json   -> the whole body, unchanged\n    achieve (human)  -> ok line (+ upstream status)\n                        composed line (+ \"PART of the answer\" when either cap fired)\n                        THE ACTION'S OWN ANSWER, WHOLE   <-- new; was dropped entirely\n                        rows kept\n\n  Note (h) fixed the machine path and left the human one printing `items` alone, so a `nextPage`\n  cursor beside the list reached --json and never reached a person. The envelope is printed ABOVE\n  the rows because `items` is capped at 200.\n\n  clients/cortex-cli/SKILL.md is on this edge too, and is now CHECKED-AGAINST rather than\n  hand-kept: its outcome table is tested against docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json and its exit column\n  against the exit code the built binary really produces.\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  - the PICK is still matchActionForGoal, lexical and deterministic; the ONE call to the gated\n    executor is still exactly one call, in the same place.\n  - no module changed tier and no import boundary moved.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "CORRECTION 2026-08-21i (S4+S5 verification round NINE) - THE RECORD MOVES ABOVE THE WRITE, THE\nMINT RUNG APPEARS ON THE MAP, AND THE CLIENT EDGE GROWS ITS SECOND HALF. Extends notes (c)-(h).\nJournal: D-S4-5/D-S5-8.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWED, AND WHAT WAS WRONG WITH IT\n  Note (h) drew the durable record of a model's choice as a step of runMatchedAction sitting AFTER\n  the one gated execute, with its own catch:\n\n    runMatchedAction\n      RUNG 2  parametrizeArgs  -> args\n      RUNG 1  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction   <-- the irreversible third-party call\n              auditParametrized (try/catch, swallow)  <-- the ONLY record of what a model chose\n      RUNG 3  composeOver\n\n  The record could therefore be absent EXACTLY when the write it describes had succeeded. An audit\n  row that goes missing on the runs that mattered is not an audit trail.\n\n  The author arm was drawn as a plain branch of achieveIntegrationGoal with no rung on it at all,\n  which is why AchieveRung published `mint` and nothing anywhere pushed it.\n\nWHAT THE MAP SHOWS NOW\n  integration-achieve.ts\n    achieveIntegrationGoal\n      match = matchActionForGoal            LEXICAL, DETERMINISTIC, unchanged\n        one + trusted -> runMatchedAction\n        none          -> THE MINT RUNG (the author arm)\n                         ladder = [ reuse: skipped ]  <- why anything is being minted\n                         ... draft -> verify -> persist ...\n                         ladder += [ mint: taken ]    <- the rung that answered\n                         every other exit here is a REFUSAL, and a refusal carries NO ladder\n\n    runMatchedAction\n      RUNG 2  parametrizeArgs           RECORDER  one try per guarded await, one ladder step\n                |- draftParametrizedArgs   WORKER  seams, MAY throw, writes nothing\n                `- recordParametrization   WRITE   activityLogs, MAY throw, does NOT catch\n                                                   rejection -> rung STANDS DOWN (caller's args,\n                                                   ladder `unavailable`) - never a refusal\n      RUNG 1  executeIntegrationCapabilityAction -> auditExecute (capability_execute)\n      RUNG 3  composeOver -> planComposition / applyComposition  (unchanged)\n\n  The order is the invariant: the choice is RECORDED, then the third party is CALLED, then what\n  happened is recorded. If the record cannot be written, the choice is not made.\n\nTHE CLIENT EDGE, SECOND HALF\n  clients/cortex-cli/src/commands/integrations.ts\n    achieve --json   -> the whole body, unchanged\n    achieve (human)  -> ok line (+ upstream status)\n                        composed line (+ \"PART of the answer\" when either cap fired)\n                        THE ACTION'S OWN ANSWER, WHOLE   <-- new; was dropped entirely\n                        rows kept\n\n  Note (h) fixed the machine path and left the human one printing `items` alone, so a `nextPage`\n  cursor beside the list reached --json and never reached a person. The envelope is printed ABOVE\n  the rows because `items` is capped at 200.\n\n  clients/cortex-cli/SKILL.md is on this edge too, and is now CHECKED-AGAINST rather than\n  hand-kept: its outcome table is tested against docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json and its exit column\n  against the exit code the built binary really produces.\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  - the PICK is still matchActionForGoal, lexical and deterministic; the ONE call to the gated\n    executor is still exactly one call, in the same place.\n  - no module changed tier and no import boundary moved."
