    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s3-note-9344481343",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 27990.0,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 927.5,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S3, PER-USER ACTION FEEDBACK): one new store, one new two-view module,\none new automation seam, three new `auth: 'user'` routes, and one new client affordance. Appended;\nno element above is edited. Journal: docs/decisions.md \"2026-08-22 - S3: a person's own notes about\nan action, and why an agent may never write one\".\n\nAPI SIDE\n  integrations/action-feedback-store.ts   the Rule 5 store over `integration_action_feedback`.\n                                          Deterministic `_id` = sha256(JSON([orgId, userId,\n                                          integrationKey, actionName, stepRef ?? null])). Write is\n                                          insert-as-claim then `_rev` CAS - NOT a `put`, because a\n                                          `put` restamps `createdAt` on every edit. No unique index.\n                                          Removal: the author's delete, or a newer note superseding.\n                                          No sweep (contrast S1: no third-party bytes, no pin).\n  integrations/action-feedback.ts          THE TWO VIEWS, and the one place a row becomes prompt\n                                          text. AUTHOR view byte-exact (an editor seeded from a\n                                          scrubbed body burns the redaction in); PROMPT view through\n                                          `scrubSecretText`, capped, ordered, labelled. Every read\n                                          takes the whole Actor and passes orgId AND userId.\n  routes/integrations.ts                   GET  /:key/feedback\n                                          PUT  /:key/actions/:actionName/feedback\n                                          DEL  /:key/actions/:actionName/feedback?stepRef=\n                                          All three BELOW the requireAuth blanket - that position IS\n                                          the admission (D2: a key that could write here would be\n                                          authoring its own next prompt). None reaches the OpenAPI\n                                          spec: the generator filters on auth === 'user-or-key'.\n  data/store.ts                            `find` gains `opts.limit` (additive, beside `projection`):\n                                          a projection bounds each ROW, this bounds the COUNT.\n\nTHE THREE PROMPT SEAMS - all through `feedbackPromptSection`, so there is ONE floor to remove\n  (1) server.ts loadContextContent -> feedbackForPrompt(actor, key)\n                                   -> composeIntegrationContext(skillMd, lessons, feedback)\n                                      3rd arg OPTIONAL: every pre-S3 call site composes identically.\n                                      Order = widest provenance first: package, org, person.\n  (2) automation/seams.ts  setIntegrationFeedbackResolver / integrationFeedbackSections(ownerUserId)\n      automation/planner.ts    contentSections += the owner's notes (before the output contract)\n      automation/rehearsal.ts  the USER text, NEVER FIXER_SYSTEM (the most injectable surface here)\n      server.ts binds it and RESOLVES THE ORG from the users store - the seam takes a user id and\n      nothing else, so the automation tier cannot pass a wrong tenant.\n  (3) integrations/integration-achieve.ts  drafting contentSections += feedbackForPrompt(ctx.actor)\n\nWEB SIDE\n  stores/integration-detail.ts     `feedback` keyed by feedbackSlot(actionName, stepRef?), its own\n                                    read-failure channel (a failed read renders the editors READ-ONLY\n                                    rather than opening empty over a real note), per-slot write\n                                    errors, and the same requestedKey stale-guard as every other read.\n  components/integrations/action-detail.tsx  the notes section UNDER the read-only steps view: the\n                                    action's own note plus one per step that carries a `stepId`.\n                                    A step without one is not addressable and gets no box - a note\n                                    keyed by POSITION would move when the plan does.\n\nSUITES  security/action-feedback-isolation.test.ts (Rule 5 + all three seams),\n        contract/integrations-action-feedback.test.ts, integrations/action-feedback-seams.test.ts,\n        automation/feedback-prompt-seams.test.ts, e2e integration-detail.spec.ts (3rd test).",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S3, PER-USER ACTION FEEDBACK): one new store, one new two-view module,\none new automation seam, three new `auth: 'user'` routes, and one new client affordance. Appended;\nno element above is edited. Journal: docs/decisions.md \"2026-08-22 - S3: a person's own notes about\nan action, and why an agent may never write one\".\n\nAPI SIDE\n  integrations/action-feedback-store.ts   the Rule 5 store over `integration_action_feedback`.\n                                          Deterministic `_id` = sha256(JSON([orgId, userId,\n                                          integrationKey, actionName, stepRef ?? null])). Write is\n                                          insert-as-claim then `_rev` CAS - NOT a `put`, because a\n                                          `put` restamps `createdAt` on every edit. No unique index.\n                                          Removal: the author's delete, or a newer note superseding.\n                                          No sweep (contrast S1: no third-party bytes, no pin).\n  integrations/action-feedback.ts          THE TWO VIEWS, and the one place a row becomes prompt\n                                          text. AUTHOR view byte-exact (an editor seeded from a\n                                          scrubbed body burns the redaction in); PROMPT view through\n                                          `scrubSecretText`, capped, ordered, labelled. Every read\n                                          takes the whole Actor and passes orgId AND userId.\n  routes/integrations.ts                   GET  /:key/feedback\n                                          PUT  /:key/actions/:actionName/feedback\n                                          DEL  /:key/actions/:actionName/feedback?stepRef=\n                                          All three BELOW the requireAuth blanket - that position IS\n                                          the admission (D2: a key that could write here would be\n                                          authoring its own next prompt). None reaches the OpenAPI\n                                          spec: the generator filters on auth === 'user-or-key'.\n  data/store.ts                            `find` gains `opts.limit` (additive, beside `projection`):\n                                          a projection bounds each ROW, this bounds the COUNT.\n\nTHE THREE PROMPT SEAMS - all through `feedbackPromptSection`, so there is ONE floor to remove\n  (1) server.ts loadContextContent -> feedbackForPrompt(actor, key)\n                                   -> composeIntegrationContext(skillMd, lessons, feedback)\n                                      3rd arg OPTIONAL: every pre-S3 call site composes identically.\n                                      Order = widest provenance first: package, org, person.\n  (2) automation/seams.ts  setIntegrationFeedbackResolver / integrationFeedbackSections(ownerUserId)\n      automation/planner.ts    contentSections += the owner's notes (before the output contract)\n      automation/rehearsal.ts  the USER text, NEVER FIXER_SYSTEM (the most injectable surface here)\n      server.ts binds it and RESOLVES THE ORG from the users store - the seam takes a user id and\n      nothing else, so the automation tier cannot pass a wrong tenant.\n  (3) integrations/integration-achieve.ts  drafting contentSections += feedbackForPrompt(ctx.actor)\n\nWEB SIDE\n  stores/integration-detail.ts     `feedback` keyed by feedbackSlot(actionName, stepRef?), its own\n                                    read-failure channel (a failed read renders the editors READ-ONLY\n                                    rather than opening empty over a real note), per-slot write\n                                    errors, and the same requestedKey stale-guard as every other read.\n  components/integrations/action-detail.tsx  the notes section UNDER the read-only steps view: the\n                                    action's own note plus one per step that carries a `stepId`.\n                                    A step without one is not addressable and gets no box - a note\n                                    keyed by POSITION would move when the plan does.\n\nSUITES  security/action-feedback-isolation.test.ts (Rule 5 + all three seams),\n        contract/integrations-action-feedback.test.ts, integrations/action-feedback-seams.test.ts,\n        automation/feedback-prompt-seams.test.ts, e2e integration-detail.spec.ts (3rd test).",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S3, PER-USER ACTION FEEDBACK): one new store, one new two-view module,\none new automation seam, three new `auth: 'user'` routes, and one new client affordance. Appended;\nno element above is edited. Journal: docs/decisions.md \"2026-08-22 - S3: a person's own notes about\nan action, and why an agent may never write one\".\n\nAPI SIDE\n  integrations/action-feedback-store.ts   the Rule 5 store over `integration_action_feedback`.\n                                          Deterministic `_id` = sha256(JSON([orgId, userId,\n                                          integrationKey, actionName, stepRef ?? null])). Write is\n                                          insert-as-claim then `_rev` CAS - NOT a `put`, because a\n                                          `put` restamps `createdAt` on every edit. No unique index.\n                                          Removal: the author's delete, or a newer note superseding.\n                                          No sweep (contrast S1: no third-party bytes, no pin).\n  integrations/action-feedback.ts          THE TWO VIEWS, and the one place a row becomes prompt\n                                          text. AUTHOR view byte-exact (an editor seeded from a\n                                          scrubbed body burns the redaction in); PROMPT view through\n                                          `scrubSecretText`, capped, ordered, labelled. Every read\n                                          takes the whole Actor and passes orgId AND userId.\n  routes/integrations.ts                   GET  /:key/feedback\n                                          PUT  /:key/actions/:actionName/feedback\n                                          DEL  /:key/actions/:actionName/feedback?stepRef=\n                                          All three BELOW the requireAuth blanket - that position IS\n                                          the admission (D2: a key that could write here would be\n                                          authoring its own next prompt). None reaches the OpenAPI\n                                          spec: the generator filters on auth === 'user-or-key'.\n  data/store.ts                            `find` gains `opts.limit` (additive, beside `projection`):\n                                          a projection bounds each ROW, this bounds the COUNT.\n\nTHE THREE PROMPT SEAMS - all through `feedbackPromptSection`, so there is ONE floor to remove\n  (1) server.ts loadContextContent -> feedbackForPrompt(actor, key)\n                                   -> composeIntegrationContext(skillMd, lessons, feedback)\n                                      3rd arg OPTIONAL: every pre-S3 call site composes identically.\n                                      Order = widest provenance first: package, org, person.\n  (2) automation/seams.ts  setIntegrationFeedbackResolver / integrationFeedbackSections(ownerUserId)\n      automation/planner.ts    contentSections += the owner's notes (before the output contract)\n      automation/rehearsal.ts  the USER text, NEVER FIXER_SYSTEM (the most injectable surface here)\n      server.ts binds it and RESOLVES THE ORG from the users store - the seam takes a user id and\n      nothing else, so the automation tier cannot pass a wrong tenant.\n  (3) integrations/integration-achieve.ts  drafting contentSections += feedbackForPrompt(ctx.actor)\n\nWEB SIDE\n  stores/integration-detail.ts     `feedback` keyed by feedbackSlot(actionName, stepRef?), its own\n                                    read-failure channel (a failed read renders the editors READ-ONLY\n                                    rather than opening empty over a real note), per-slot write\n                                    errors, and the same requestedKey stale-guard as every other read.\n  components/integrations/action-detail.tsx  the notes section UNDER the read-only steps view: the\n                                    action's own note plus one per step that carries a `stepId`.\n                                    A step without one is not addressable and gets no box - a note\n                                    keyed by POSITION would move when the plan does.\n\nSUITES  security/action-feedback-isolation.test.ts (Rule 5 + all three seams),\n        contract/integrations-action-feedback.test.ts, integrations/action-feedback-seams.test.ts,\n        automation/feedback-prompt-seams.test.ts, e2e integration-detail.spec.ts (3rd test).",
