    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s3r2-note-9857821812",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 29037.5,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 700.0,
      "text": "REVIEW ROUND 2026-08-22 (slice S3) - what the adversarial pass changed. Appended; no element above\nis edited. Journal: docs/decisions.md, the REVIEW ROUND section of \"2026-08-22 - S3: a person's own\nnotes about an action\".\n\nBINDINGS - TWO in server.ts, and only one was pinned\n  (1) load_context join          server.ts setLoadContextContent -> feedbackForPrompt ->\n                                 composeIntegrationContext(skillMd, lessons, feedback)\n                                 WAS UNTESTED: dropping the third argument left the whole estate\n                                 green (typecheck too - the parameter defaults). Now driven through\n                                 the REAL loadContextContent by\n                                 tests/automation/composition-root-feedback-seam.test.ts, the\n                                 precedent contract/integrations-lessons.test.ts set for C3.\n  (2) automation resolver        setIntegrationFeedbackResolver - pinned since the first cut (M7).\n  (3) achieve                    NOT A BINDING. integration-achieve.ts calls feedbackForPrompt\n                                 directly, so its production path IS the module; there is nothing in\n                                 server.ts for it to lose.\n\nTHE FLOOR NOW COVERS THE LINE, NOT ONE FIELD\n  feedbackPromptSection scrubbed row.note and interpolated row.stepRef RAW into the same line.\n  stepRef is caller-supplied free text, never validated against a plan, so `api_key: sk_live_...`\n  written as a step ref reached ALL THREE seams unredacted while the same bytes in the note body\n  were redacted. scrubSecretText now runs over the whole composed line (no over-redaction: the regex\n  anchors on a credential-named key, then scans tokens). Plus a store-side stepRef ceiling.\n\nBOUNDED READS ON EVERY PROMPT PATH, AND A WRITE CAP\n  listNewestForIntegration   NEW: sorted + limited IN THE QUERY, for seams 1 and 3. They used to\n                             share the page's unbounded read - a bounded ANSWER over an unbounded\n                             READ, the distinction this slice's own Store.find docblock draws.\n  listForIntegration         unchanged and deliberately unbounded: the AUTHOR'S page, where\n                             completeness is the contract.\n  ACTION_FEEDBACK_MAX_NOTES_PER_ACTION = 50, checked only when the write would CREATE a row, so an\n                             edit at the ceiling still lands.\n\nWEB - ORPHANS ARE VISIBLE AND ERASABLE (the major)\n  ActionNotes.orphanedSteps      a note whose stepRef names no current step: rendered stranded,\n                                 labeled, editable AND deletable (the write ignores stepRef).\n  DepartedActionNotes            a note whose ACTION is off the capability: its own section,\n                                 ERASE-ONLY, because the write refuses an action off the definition.\n  Both were claimed by the component header, by action-feedback.ts and by findings.md, and neither\n  existed. The no-retention-sweep decision rests on exactly this control.",
      "rawText": "REVIEW ROUND 2026-08-22 (slice S3) - what the adversarial pass changed. Appended; no element above\nis edited. Journal: docs/decisions.md, the REVIEW ROUND section of \"2026-08-22 - S3: a person's own\nnotes about an action\".\n\nBINDINGS - TWO in server.ts, and only one was pinned\n  (1) load_context join          server.ts setLoadContextContent -> feedbackForPrompt ->\n                                 composeIntegrationContext(skillMd, lessons, feedback)\n                                 WAS UNTESTED: dropping the third argument left the whole estate\n                                 green (typecheck too - the parameter defaults). Now driven through\n                                 the REAL loadContextContent by\n                                 tests/automation/composition-root-feedback-seam.test.ts, the\n                                 precedent contract/integrations-lessons.test.ts set for C3.\n  (2) automation resolver        setIntegrationFeedbackResolver - pinned since the first cut (M7).\n  (3) achieve                    NOT A BINDING. integration-achieve.ts calls feedbackForPrompt\n                                 directly, so its production path IS the module; there is nothing in\n                                 server.ts for it to lose.\n\nTHE FLOOR NOW COVERS THE LINE, NOT ONE FIELD\n  feedbackPromptSection scrubbed row.note and interpolated row.stepRef RAW into the same line.\n  stepRef is caller-supplied free text, never validated against a plan, so `api_key: sk_live_...`\n  written as a step ref reached ALL THREE seams unredacted while the same bytes in the note body\n  were redacted. scrubSecretText now runs over the whole composed line (no over-redaction: the regex\n  anchors on a credential-named key, then scans tokens). Plus a store-side stepRef ceiling.\n\nBOUNDED READS ON EVERY PROMPT PATH, AND A WRITE CAP\n  listNewestForIntegration   NEW: sorted + limited IN THE QUERY, for seams 1 and 3. They used to\n                             share the page's unbounded read - a bounded ANSWER over an unbounded\n                             READ, the distinction this slice's own Store.find docblock draws.\n  listForIntegration         unchanged and deliberately unbounded: the AUTHOR'S page, where\n                             completeness is the contract.\n  ACTION_FEEDBACK_MAX_NOTES_PER_ACTION = 50, checked only when the write would CREATE a row, so an\n                             edit at the ceiling still lands.\n\nWEB - ORPHANS ARE VISIBLE AND ERASABLE (the major)\n  ActionNotes.orphanedSteps      a note whose stepRef names no current step: rendered stranded,\n                                 labeled, editable AND deletable (the write ignores stepRef).\n  DepartedActionNotes            a note whose ACTION is off the capability: its own section,\n                                 ERASE-ONLY, because the write refuses an action off the definition.\n  Both were claimed by the component header, by action-feedback.ts and by findings.md, and neither\n  existed. The no-retention-sweep decision rests on exactly this control.",
      "originalText": "REVIEW ROUND 2026-08-22 (slice S3) - what the adversarial pass changed. Appended; no element above\nis edited. Journal: docs/decisions.md, the REVIEW ROUND section of \"2026-08-22 - S3: a person's own\nnotes about an action\".\n\nBINDINGS - TWO in server.ts, and only one was pinned\n  (1) load_context join          server.ts setLoadContextContent -> feedbackForPrompt ->\n                                 composeIntegrationContext(skillMd, lessons, feedback)\n                                 WAS UNTESTED: dropping the third argument left the whole estate\n                                 green (typecheck too - the parameter defaults). Now driven through\n                                 the REAL loadContextContent by\n                                 tests/automation/composition-root-feedback-seam.test.ts, the\n                                 precedent contract/integrations-lessons.test.ts set for C3.\n  (2) automation resolver        setIntegrationFeedbackResolver - pinned since the first cut (M7).\n  (3) achieve                    NOT A BINDING. integration-achieve.ts calls feedbackForPrompt\n                                 directly, so its production path IS the module; there is nothing in\n                                 server.ts for it to lose.\n\nTHE FLOOR NOW COVERS THE LINE, NOT ONE FIELD\n  feedbackPromptSection scrubbed row.note and interpolated row.stepRef RAW into the same line.\n  stepRef is caller-supplied free text, never validated against a plan, so `api_key: sk_live_...`\n  written as a step ref reached ALL THREE seams unredacted while the same bytes in the note body\n  were redacted. scrubSecretText now runs over the whole composed line (no over-redaction: the regex\n  anchors on a credential-named key, then scans tokens). Plus a store-side stepRef ceiling.\n\nBOUNDED READS ON EVERY PROMPT PATH, AND A WRITE CAP\n  listNewestForIntegration   NEW: sorted + limited IN THE QUERY, for seams 1 and 3. They used to\n                             share the page's unbounded read - a bounded ANSWER over an unbounded\n                             READ, the distinction this slice's own Store.find docblock draws.\n  listForIntegration         unchanged and deliberately unbounded: the AUTHOR'S page, where\n                             completeness is the contract.\n  ACTION_FEEDBACK_MAX_NOTES_PER_ACTION = 50, checked only when the write would CREATE a row, so an\n                             edit at the ceiling still lands.\n\nWEB - ORPHANS ARE VISIBLE AND ERASABLE (the major)\n  ActionNotes.orphanedSteps      a note whose stepRef names no current step: rendered stranded,\n                                 labeled, editable AND deletable (the write ignores stepRef).\n  DepartedActionNotes            a note whose ACTION is off the capability: its own section,\n                                 ERASE-ONLY, because the write refuses an action off the definition.\n  Both were claimed by the component header, by action-feedback.ts and by findings.md, and neither\n  existed. The no-retention-sweep decision rests on exactly this control.",
