    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260822-s7-migration-report",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 36655.0,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 875.0,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S7, the automations -> integrations MIGRATION REPORT): one new module,\ntwo callers, and NO NEW STATE ANYWHERE - the slice adds no collection, no field and no write.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 \"S7: the migration is a REPORT, and the report says what it costs\".\n\nNEW api/src/automation/migration-report.ts (tier 5, beside the engine it classifies)\n\n  It reads ONE collection and writes NOTHING. There is no write path in the module to disable:\n\n    data/stores.ts  automations.find(filter, {updatedAt:-1}, {projection})     <-- the only edge out\n      -> classifyAutomation(doc)                              (pure; no I/O, no model, no clock)\n           tier          'flatten' | 'wrap'\n           flattenRefusals[]        why it is not one request\n           engineInternal[]         what the wrapper would hide\n           degradations[]           what a person would lose\n           shapeHash                sha256 over exactly what was classified\n\n  WHY IT LIVES IN automation/ AND NOT IN integrations/. The tier table allows automation/ -> integrations/\n  and forbids the reverse (`integrations/` may not import `automation/` - the S1 evidence collector is\n  the standing proof, which is why THAT one is a seam). This module needs the automation step union AND\n  the action's http-config shape, so it sits on the side that may reach both, and the route reaches it\n  the way routes reach any tier-5 module.\n\nTWO CALLERS, AND THEY ARE DIFFERENT SCOPES ON PURPOSE\n\n  1. PER-CALLER (the reachable report)\n       routes/integrations.ts  GET /api/v1/integrations/automation-migration-report   auth: 'user'\n         -> buildMigrationReport({ orgId: actor.orgId, readerUserId: actor.userId })\n       Registered with the other LITERAL first segments (/active, /configs, /definitions/..., /recipes)\n       ABOVE the `:key` block - a registration below it would make this endpoint answer as the\n       capability handler for an integration named \"automation-migration-report\", i.e. an ordinary 404.\n\n       Tenancy is the automation service's own rule, applied in the same shape and not re-derived:\n         orgId filter (query)  +  `visibility !== 'private' || ownerUserId === reader`  (in memory)\n       so the report can never name a row `listAutomations` would refuse the same caller.\n\n  2. ESTATE (the boot obligation)\n       server.ts bootState()  -> buildMigrationReport()      no org, no reader\n         -> console.log(migrationBootSummary(report))        COUNTS ONLY; no automation name is logged\n       Guarded by try/catch like the legacy import beside it: a classification pass must not stop boot.\n\nWHAT THE SLICE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT TOUCH\n  - /api/v1/automations descriptors and routes: unchanged (public capability API, pinned by the gates).\n  - integrations/authored-action.ts: the api-call-only guardrail is NOT widened. When the write half\n    lands it mints bindings through the BUILDER SAVE path, never through achieve.\n  - The engine: every step type this report calls \"engine-internal\" keeps running exactly as it does.\n\nRULE 10. Shadow (both surfaces run side by side) -> compare (the report IS the instrument; shapeHash\ndiffs between boots) -> CUTOVER-OR-REMOVE by 2026-11-14: either the write half lands with its own\nflag and its own entry, or this module and its endpoint are deleted. No third option, and no report\nthat becomes furniture.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S7, the automations -> integrations MIGRATION REPORT): one new module,\ntwo callers, and NO NEW STATE ANYWHERE - the slice adds no collection, no field and no write.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 \"S7: the migration is a REPORT, and the report says what it costs\".\n\nNEW api/src/automation/migration-report.ts (tier 5, beside the engine it classifies)\n\n  It reads ONE collection and writes NOTHING. There is no write path in the module to disable:\n\n    data/stores.ts  automations.find(filter, {updatedAt:-1}, {projection})     <-- the only edge out\n      -> classifyAutomation(doc)                              (pure; no I/O, no model, no clock)\n           tier          'flatten' | 'wrap'\n           flattenRefusals[]        why it is not one request\n           engineInternal[]         what the wrapper would hide\n           degradations[]           what a person would lose\n           shapeHash                sha256 over exactly what was classified\n\n  WHY IT LIVES IN automation/ AND NOT IN integrations/. The tier table allows automation/ -> integrations/\n  and forbids the reverse (`integrations/` may not import `automation/` - the S1 evidence collector is\n  the standing proof, which is why THAT one is a seam). This module needs the automation step union AND\n  the action's http-config shape, so it sits on the side that may reach both, and the route reaches it\n  the way routes reach any tier-5 module.\n\nTWO CALLERS, AND THEY ARE DIFFERENT SCOPES ON PURPOSE\n\n  1. PER-CALLER (the reachable report)\n       routes/integrations.ts  GET /api/v1/integrations/automation-migration-report   auth: 'user'\n         -> buildMigrationReport({ orgId: actor.orgId, readerUserId: actor.userId })\n       Registered with the other LITERAL first segments (/active, /configs, /definitions/..., /recipes)\n       ABOVE the `:key` block - a registration below it would make this endpoint answer as the\n       capability handler for an integration named \"automation-migration-report\", i.e. an ordinary 404.\n\n       Tenancy is the automation service's own rule, applied in the same shape and not re-derived:\n         orgId filter (query)  +  `visibility !== 'private' || ownerUserId === reader`  (in memory)\n       so the report can never name a row `listAutomations` would refuse the same caller.\n\n  2. ESTATE (the boot obligation)\n       server.ts bootState()  -> buildMigrationReport()      no org, no reader\n         -> console.log(migrationBootSummary(report))        COUNTS ONLY; no automation name is logged\n       Guarded by try/catch like the legacy import beside it: a classification pass must not stop boot.\n\nWHAT THE SLICE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT TOUCH\n  - /api/v1/automations descriptors and routes: unchanged (public capability API, pinned by the gates).\n  - integrations/authored-action.ts: the api-call-only guardrail is NOT widened. When the write half\n    lands it mints bindings through the BUILDER SAVE path, never through achieve.\n  - The engine: every step type this report calls \"engine-internal\" keeps running exactly as it does.\n\nRULE 10. Shadow (both surfaces run side by side) -> compare (the report IS the instrument; shapeHash\ndiffs between boots) -> CUTOVER-OR-REMOVE by 2026-11-14: either the write half lands with its own\nflag and its own entry, or this module and its endpoint are deleted. No third option, and no report\nthat becomes furniture.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S7, the automations -> integrations MIGRATION REPORT): one new module,\ntwo callers, and NO NEW STATE ANYWHERE - the slice adds no collection, no field and no write.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 \"S7: the migration is a REPORT, and the report says what it costs\".\n\nNEW api/src/automation/migration-report.ts (tier 5, beside the engine it classifies)\n\n  It reads ONE collection and writes NOTHING. There is no write path in the module to disable:\n\n    data/stores.ts  automations.find(filter, {updatedAt:-1}, {projection})     <-- the only edge out\n      -> classifyAutomation(doc)                              (pure; no I/O, no model, no clock)\n           tier          'flatten' | 'wrap'\n           flattenRefusals[]        why it is not one request\n           engineInternal[]         what the wrapper would hide\n           degradations[]           what a person would lose\n           shapeHash                sha256 over exactly what was classified\n\n  WHY IT LIVES IN automation/ AND NOT IN integrations/. The tier table allows automation/ -> integrations/\n  and forbids the reverse (`integrations/` may not import `automation/` - the S1 evidence collector is\n  the standing proof, which is why THAT one is a seam). This module needs the automation step union AND\n  the action's http-config shape, so it sits on the side that may reach both, and the route reaches it\n  the way routes reach any tier-5 module.\n\nTWO CALLERS, AND THEY ARE DIFFERENT SCOPES ON PURPOSE\n\n  1. PER-CALLER (the reachable report)\n       routes/integrations.ts  GET /api/v1/integrations/automation-migration-report   auth: 'user'\n         -> buildMigrationReport({ orgId: actor.orgId, readerUserId: actor.userId })\n       Registered with the other LITERAL first segments (/active, /configs, /definitions/..., /recipes)\n       ABOVE the `:key` block - a registration below it would make this endpoint answer as the\n       capability handler for an integration named \"automation-migration-report\", i.e. an ordinary 404.\n\n       Tenancy is the automation service's own rule, applied in the same shape and not re-derived:\n         orgId filter (query)  +  `visibility !== 'private' || ownerUserId === reader`  (in memory)\n       so the report can never name a row `listAutomations` would refuse the same caller.\n\n  2. ESTATE (the boot obligation)\n       server.ts bootState()  -> buildMigrationReport()      no org, no reader\n         -> console.log(migrationBootSummary(report))        COUNTS ONLY; no automation name is logged\n       Guarded by try/catch like the legacy import beside it: a classification pass must not stop boot.\n\nWHAT THE SLICE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT TOUCH\n  - /api/v1/automations descriptors and routes: unchanged (public capability API, pinned by the gates).\n  - integrations/authored-action.ts: the api-call-only guardrail is NOT widened. When the write half\n    lands it mints bindings through the BUILDER SAVE path, never through achieve.\n  - The engine: every step type this report calls \"engine-internal\" keeps running exactly as it does.\n\nRULE 10. Shadow (both surfaces run side by side) -> compare (the report IS the instrument; shapeHash\ndiffs between boots) -> CUTOVER-OR-REMOVE by 2026-11-14: either the write half lands with its own\nflag and its own entry, or this module and its endpoint are deleted. No third option, and no report\nthat becomes furniture.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 202608220,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608221,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
