    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260822-s8-hide",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 37730.0,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 1190.0,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S8, THE HIDE): the automations surface leaves the map as a set of PAGES\nand stays on it as an ENGINE. Nothing under api/src changed shape; what moved is which addresses a\nperson can reach and what the product calls things.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 \"S8: the automations surface is hidden, and the word goes with it\".\n\nWHAT CAME OUT OF THE SHELL\n\n  web/lib/navigation.ts  NAV_ITEMS\n    - { href: \"/automations\", icon: Play, labelKey: \"automations\" }     <-- row deleted\n      (and locales' sidebar.automations with it, en/pt/types in lockstep)\n\nTHE THREE ADDRESSES, AND WHY THEY DIFFER\n\n  /automations              app/(dashboard)/automations/page.tsx\n                              server redirect() -> /integrations        (replaces, never pushes)\n\n  /automations/<id>         app/(dashboard)/automations/[id]/page.tsx\n                              client resolve, ONE read, then router.replace:\n                                stores/automations.fetchOne(id)\n                                  -> automation.source.integrationKey ? /integrations/<key>\n                                                                      : /integrations\n                              A server component cannot resolve this: the bearer is in the browser.\n                              Every failure (absent, refused, network, no provenance) lands on\n                              /integrations. There is no not-found state - the page that could act\n                              on one is gone.\n\n  /automations/new          app/(dashboard)/automations/new/route.ts\n                              GET -> 410 Gone. A ROUTE HANDLER, not a page: notFound() is 404 and a\n                              page cannot set a status. A handler and a page cannot share a segment,\n                              so the page is deleted.\n\nTHE AFFORDANCES, RE-POINTED AT SOMETHING SPECIFIC\n\n  integrations list row   \"Ver passos\"  -> /integrations/<key>?action=<name>   (S2's deep link)\n  integrations list       \"Preparar passos\"  -> UNCHANGED behaviour: POST /:key/provision-automations\n  schedules/[id]          automation target -> /integrations/<key> when the row has provenance,\n                                               otherwise the sequence is NAMED and not linked\n  schedules/[id]          per-run chip      -> plain text (the detail page's runs are keyed by\n                                               ACTION and cannot be addressed by an automation run id)\n\nWHAT STAYED LIVE, AND IS VERIFIED SO\n\n  stores/automations.ts        <- pause overlay, schedules form, schedule detail, the [id] redirect\n  hooks/useAutomationRun.ts    <- (dashboard)/layout.tsx\n  components/automations/pause-for-user-overlay.tsx (+ canvas)  <- BOTH layouts; it pops for\n                                 headless runs whatever started them, so it is reworded, not removed\n  api/src/routes/automations.ts and every /api/v1/automations descriptor  <- UNTOUCHED\n\nWHAT BECAME UNREACHABLE AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT DELETED (findings:\ns8-automation-authoring-components-unreachable, closing at S7's Rule 10 review date 2026-11-14)\n\n  components/automations/{automation-empty-state, goal-editor, run-activity-bar, run-history,\n    run-viewer, step-list, trigger-picker}                       <- lost their only importer\n  components/automations/{step-card, inline-edit, integration-action-picker, step-forms,\n    step-type-selector, sub-automation-picker, consent-dialog}   <- reachable only through those\n  most of the `automations` locale slice                         <- goes with them\n\nTHE SERVER PROSE (D4), AND WHERE IT STOPS\n\n  reworded: action-consent actionTarget (ALSO the approval key - findings:\n            s8-consent-reword-retires-standing-approvals), engine's run-level terminal message,\n            shared/run-errors RUN_FAILED (pt+en), routes/triggers 404, schedules/service validation,\n            catalog.ts heading + PT trigger caveat, web/lib/privacy-claims commandsEmpty\n  NOT reworded, deliberately: routes/automations.ts and automation/service.ts's plan guidance - that\n            is the /api/v1/automations CONTRACT's own vocabulary, read by outside clients through the\n            OpenAPI document and the generated client\n  NOT renamed, deliberately: call_automation / list_automations / call_integration_action - they are\n            identifiers a model must emit exactly, not prose",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S8, THE HIDE): the automations surface leaves the map as a set of PAGES\nand stays on it as an ENGINE. Nothing under api/src changed shape; what moved is which addresses a\nperson can reach and what the product calls things.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 \"S8: the automations surface is hidden, and the word goes with it\".\n\nWHAT CAME OUT OF THE SHELL\n\n  web/lib/navigation.ts  NAV_ITEMS\n    - { href: \"/automations\", icon: Play, labelKey: \"automations\" }     <-- row deleted\n      (and locales' sidebar.automations with it, en/pt/types in lockstep)\n\nTHE THREE ADDRESSES, AND WHY THEY DIFFER\n\n  /automations              app/(dashboard)/automations/page.tsx\n                              server redirect() -> /integrations        (replaces, never pushes)\n\n  /automations/<id>         app/(dashboard)/automations/[id]/page.tsx\n                              client resolve, ONE read, then router.replace:\n                                stores/automations.fetchOne(id)\n                                  -> automation.source.integrationKey ? /integrations/<key>\n                                                                      : /integrations\n                              A server component cannot resolve this: the bearer is in the browser.\n                              Every failure (absent, refused, network, no provenance) lands on\n                              /integrations. There is no not-found state - the page that could act\n                              on one is gone.\n\n  /automations/new          app/(dashboard)/automations/new/route.ts\n                              GET -> 410 Gone. A ROUTE HANDLER, not a page: notFound() is 404 and a\n                              page cannot set a status. A handler and a page cannot share a segment,\n                              so the page is deleted.\n\nTHE AFFORDANCES, RE-POINTED AT SOMETHING SPECIFIC\n\n  integrations list row   \"Ver passos\"  -> /integrations/<key>?action=<name>   (S2's deep link)\n  integrations list       \"Preparar passos\"  -> UNCHANGED behaviour: POST /:key/provision-automations\n  schedules/[id]          automation target -> /integrations/<key> when the row has provenance,\n                                               otherwise the sequence is NAMED and not linked\n  schedules/[id]          per-run chip      -> plain text (the detail page's runs are keyed by\n                                               ACTION and cannot be addressed by an automation run id)\n\nWHAT STAYED LIVE, AND IS VERIFIED SO\n\n  stores/automations.ts        <- pause overlay, schedules form, schedule detail, the [id] redirect\n  hooks/useAutomationRun.ts    <- (dashboard)/layout.tsx\n  components/automations/pause-for-user-overlay.tsx (+ canvas)  <- BOTH layouts; it pops for\n                                 headless runs whatever started them, so it is reworded, not removed\n  api/src/routes/automations.ts and every /api/v1/automations descriptor  <- UNTOUCHED\n\nWHAT BECAME UNREACHABLE AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT DELETED (findings:\ns8-automation-authoring-components-unreachable, closing at S7's Rule 10 review date 2026-11-14)\n\n  components/automations/{automation-empty-state, goal-editor, run-activity-bar, run-history,\n    run-viewer, step-list, trigger-picker}                       <- lost their only importer\n  components/automations/{step-card, inline-edit, integration-action-picker, step-forms,\n    step-type-selector, sub-automation-picker, consent-dialog}   <- reachable only through those\n  most of the `automations` locale slice                         <- goes with them\n\nTHE SERVER PROSE (D4), AND WHERE IT STOPS\n\n  reworded: action-consent actionTarget (ALSO the approval key - findings:\n            s8-consent-reword-retires-standing-approvals), engine's run-level terminal message,\n            shared/run-errors RUN_FAILED (pt+en), routes/triggers 404, schedules/service validation,\n            catalog.ts heading + PT trigger caveat, web/lib/privacy-claims commandsEmpty\n  NOT reworded, deliberately: routes/automations.ts and automation/service.ts's plan guidance - that\n            is the /api/v1/automations CONTRACT's own vocabulary, read by outside clients through the\n            OpenAPI document and the generated client\n  NOT renamed, deliberately: call_automation / list_automations / call_integration_action - they are\n            identifiers a model must emit exactly, not prose",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S8, THE HIDE): the automations surface leaves the map as a set of PAGES\nand stays on it as an ENGINE. Nothing under api/src changed shape; what moved is which addresses a\nperson can reach and what the product calls things.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 \"S8: the automations surface is hidden, and the word goes with it\".\n\nWHAT CAME OUT OF THE SHELL\n\n  web/lib/navigation.ts  NAV_ITEMS\n    - { href: \"/automations\", icon: Play, labelKey: \"automations\" }     <-- row deleted\n      (and locales' sidebar.automations with it, en/pt/types in lockstep)\n\nTHE THREE ADDRESSES, AND WHY THEY DIFFER\n\n  /automations              app/(dashboard)/automations/page.tsx\n                              server redirect() -> /integrations        (replaces, never pushes)\n\n  /automations/<id>         app/(dashboard)/automations/[id]/page.tsx\n                              client resolve, ONE read, then router.replace:\n                                stores/automations.fetchOne(id)\n                                  -> automation.source.integrationKey ? /integrations/<key>\n                                                                      : /integrations\n                              A server component cannot resolve this: the bearer is in the browser.\n                              Every failure (absent, refused, network, no provenance) lands on\n                              /integrations. There is no not-found state - the page that could act\n                              on one is gone.\n\n  /automations/new          app/(dashboard)/automations/new/route.ts\n                              GET -> 410 Gone. A ROUTE HANDLER, not a page: notFound() is 404 and a\n                              page cannot set a status. A handler and a page cannot share a segment,\n                              so the page is deleted.\n\nTHE AFFORDANCES, RE-POINTED AT SOMETHING SPECIFIC\n\n  integrations list row   \"Ver passos\"  ->