    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "correction-20260822-s7-review-round",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 39120.0,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 735.0,
      "text": "CORRECTION 2026-08-22 (S7 review round) - THE UNITS WERE WRONG IN THREE PLACES, AND THE GATE THAT\nSHOULD HAVE CAUGHT THE FIRST ONE COULD NOT FAIL. Extends the S7 as-built note above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 S7, REVIEW ROUND section.\n\nTHE TENANCY GATE, MOVED TO THE UNIT IT GUARDS\n\n  BEFORE (what the map implied was covered)\n    automation-migration-isolation.test.ts  -> buildMigrationReport(scope)      [MODULE]\n      ...and nothing at all           -> GET /automations-migration-report      [ROUTE]\n    So: routes/integrations.ts's two scope arguments were asserted by no test. Replacing them with\n    buildMigrationReport({}) - every tenant's automation names to any authenticated caller - left\n    all 46 tests green.\n\n  AFTER (two layers of ONE gate)\n    integrations-migration-report.test.ts \"tenancy AT THE ROUTE\"                [ROUTE]\n      layer 1: buildMigrationReport({})        -> proves the foreign row EXISTS\n      layer 2: GET .../automation-migration-report -> proves the response OMITS it\n      (an absence assertion alone also passes on an empty database - that is why layer 1 is there)\n    automation-migration-isolation.test.ts     -> keeps the module filter arithmetic beside it\n\nTHE READ IS NOW BOUNDED WHERE THE HAZARD IS\n\n  BEFORE   automations.find(filter, sort, {projection})   -> whole collection materialised\n             .slice(0, MIGRATION_SCAN_CAP)                -> \"bounded\" in JS, after the allocation\n  AFTER    data/store.ts  Store.find(..., {projection, limit})   <-- NEW additive option\n           automations.find(filter, sort, {projection, limit: cap + 1})\n             cap + 1 is what distinguishes \"at the cap\" from \"past it\" without a second page\n\nTHE CLASSIFIER GAINED ONE INPUT, AND STAYED PURE\n\n    buildMigrationReport\n      reservedIntegrationKeys()          <-- integrations/definitions.ts, ONCE per pass\n        -> classifyAutomation(doc, reservedKeys)          [pure; no I/O, no registry, no clock]\n             org-visible-narrows-to-owner   asked of the DESTINATION row, not the automation row\n                                            (a SHIPPED key cannot be a fresh private builder row)\n             mid-run-pause-collapses        asked of the ENGINE's shouldAttemptFix set, not of\n                                            \"has a browser step\" (+ sub_automation, unseen child)\n      markContestedDestinations(entries)   <-- set-level: two owners, one destination key\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  The write path still does not exist. Nothing in this correction adds one, and the Rule 10 review\n  date (2026-11-14) is unchanged.",
      "rawText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-22 (S7 review round) - THE UNITS WERE WRONG IN THREE PLACES, AND THE GATE THAT\nSHOULD HAVE CAUGHT THE FIRST ONE COULD NOT FAIL. Extends the S7 as-built note above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 S7, REVIEW ROUND section.\n\nTHE TENANCY GATE, MOVED TO THE UNIT IT GUARDS\n\n  BEFORE (what the map implied was covered)\n    automation-migration-isolation.test.ts  -> buildMigrationReport(scope)      [MODULE]\n      ...and nothing at all           -> GET /automations-migration-report      [ROUTE]\n    So: routes/integrations.ts's two scope arguments were asserted by no test. Replacing them with\n    buildMigrationReport({}) - every tenant's automation names to any authenticated caller - left\n    all 46 tests green.\n\n  AFTER (two layers of ONE gate)\n    integrations-migration-report.test.ts \"tenancy AT THE ROUTE\"                [ROUTE]\n      layer 1: buildMigrationReport({})        -> proves the foreign row EXISTS\n      layer 2: GET .../automation-migration-report -> proves the response OMITS it\n      (an absence assertion alone also passes on an empty database - that is why layer 1 is there)\n    automation-migration-isolation.test.ts     -> keeps the module filter arithmetic beside it\n\nTHE READ IS NOW BOUNDED WHERE THE HAZARD IS\n\n  BEFORE   automations.find(filter, sort, {projection})   -> whole collection materialised\n             .slice(0, MIGRATION_SCAN_CAP)                -> \"bounded\" in JS, after the allocation\n  AFTER    data/store.ts  Store.find(..., {projection, limit})   <-- NEW additive option\n           automations.find(filter, sort, {projection, limit: cap + 1})\n             cap + 1 is what distinguishes \"at the cap\" from \"past it\" without a second page\n\nTHE CLASSIFIER GAINED ONE INPUT, AND STAYED PURE\n\n    buildMigrationReport\n      reservedIntegrationKeys()          <-- integrations/definitions.ts, ONCE per pass\n        -> classifyAutomation(doc, reservedKeys)          [pure; no I/O, no registry, no clock]\n             org-visible-narrows-to-owner   asked of the DESTINATION row, not the automation row\n                                            (a SHIPPED key cannot be a fresh private builder row)\n             mid-run-pause-collapses        asked of the ENGINE's shouldAttemptFix set, not of\n                                            \"has a browser step\" (+ sub_automation, unseen child)\n      markContestedDestinations(entries)   <-- set-level: two owners, one destination key\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  The write path still does not exist. Nothing in this correction adds one, and the Rule 10 review\n  date (2026-11-14) is unchanged.",
      "originalText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-22 (S7 review round) - THE UNITS WERE WRONG IN THREE PLACES, AND THE GATE THAT\nSHOULD HAVE CAUGHT THE FIRST ONE COULD NOT FAIL. Extends the S7 as-built note above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 S7, REVIEW ROUND section.\n\nTHE TENANCY GATE, MOVED TO THE UNIT IT GUARDS\n\n  BEFORE (what the map implied was covered)\n    automation-migration-isolation.test.ts  -> buildMigrationReport(scope)      [MODULE]\n      ...and nothing at all           -> GET /automations-migration-report      [ROUTE]\n    So: routes/integrations.ts's two scope arguments were asserted by no test. Replacing them with\n    buildMigrationReport({}) - every tenant's automation names to any authenticated caller - left\n    all 46 tests green.\n\n  AFTER (two layers of ONE gate)\n    integrations-migration-report.test.ts \"tenancy AT THE ROUTE\"                [ROUTE]\n      layer 1: buildMigrationReport({})        -> proves the foreign row EXISTS\n      layer 2: GET .../automation-migration-report -> proves the response OMITS it\n      (an absence assertion alone also passes on an empty database - that is why layer 1 is there)\n    automation-migration-isolation.test.ts     -> keeps the module filter arithmetic beside it\n\nTHE READ IS NOW BOUNDED WHERE THE HAZARD IS\n\n  BEFORE   automations.find(filter, sort, {projection})   -> whole collection materialised\n             .slice(0, MIGRATION_SCAN_CAP)                -> \"bounded\" in JS, after the allocation\n  AFTER    data/store.ts  Store.find(..., {projection, limit})   <-- NEW additive option\n           automations.find(filter, sort, {projection, limit: cap + 1})\n             cap + 1 is what distinguishes \"at the cap\" from \"past it\" without a second page\n\nTHE CLASSIFIER GAINED ONE INPUT, AND STAYED PURE\n\n    buildMigrationReport\n      reservedIntegrationKeys()          <-- integrations/definitions.ts, ONCE per pass\n        -> classifyAutomation(doc, reservedKeys)          [pure; no I/O, no registry, no clock]\n             org-visible-narrows-to-owner   asked of the DESTINATION row, not the automation row\n                                            (a SHIPPED key cannot be a fresh private builder row)\n             mid-run-pause-collapses        asked of the ENGINE's shouldAttemptFix set, not of\n                                            \"has a browser step\" (+ sub_automation, unseen child)\n      markContestedDestinations(entries)   <-- set-level: two owners, one destination key\n\nWHAT DID NOT MOVE\n  The write path still does not exist. Nothing in this correction adds one, and the Rule 10 review\n  date (2026-11-14) is unchanged.",
