      "height": 665.0,
      "text": "CORRECTION 2026-08-22 (S8 review round) - THE CENSUS MISSED FOUR REACHABLE STRINGS, AND THREE OF THE\nSURFACES IT REWROTE HAD NO TEST THAT COULD FAIL. Extends the S8 as-built note above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 S8, REVIEW ROUND section.\n\nTHE FOUR STRINGS THE SWEEP MISSED, and where they actually lived\n\n  web/components/artifacts/artifact-backend-panel.tsx   \"configuram-se em Automa\u00e7\u00f5es.\"\n      <- the harmful one: live guidance naming the REMOVED surface as the place to act,\n         rendered in the ordinary no-backend case on /artifacts\n  web/stores/integrations.ts        provision fallback toast, behind the very button S8 reworded\n  web/app/(dashboard)/cofre/page.tsx   the lock-all confirm dialog\n  web/lib/privacy-claims.ts         ledgerKindLabels.automation, in a file this commit already edited\n\n  WHY THEY SURVIVED: completeness was checked by grepping the LOCALE files, which is the one place\n  the word was not hiding. Hardcoded JSX and store-level fallbacks are the census surface.\n\nTHE OVERLAY NAMES THE RUN, WITH THE RUN'S OWN ID\n\n  BEFORE   {t.runIdPrefix}{activeRun.automationId.slice(0,8)}     <- label renamed, value not\n  AFTER    {t.runIdPrefix}{activeRun.runId.slice(0,8)}            <- data-testid pause-overlay-run-id\n  + web/__tests__/components/pause-for-user-overlay.test.tsx      <- it had NO test at any layer\n\nTHE [id] RESOLVER, NOW EXERCISED THROUGH THE REAL STORE\n\n  BEFORE   vi.mock('@/stores/automations')  -> the resolver was mocked out of its own test\n             (patching the real fetchOne to return null left 613/613 web tests green)\n  AFTER    vi.mock('@/lib/api') only        -> real store, real normalizeWireAutomation, real\n             error branches; the wire shape is in the path, which is where `source` and `orgId` live\n  + a foreign-org row now falls back to /integrations rather than replacing a super-admin onto\n    THEIR OWN org's page for that key (a wrong answer that looks right)\n\nTHE SCHEDULE TARGET, RESOLVED AT THE ROW AND NOT THE LIST\n\n  BEFORE   useAutomationsStore.automations.find(id)   -> the VIEWER's list; a peer's private row,\n             a list still loading and a failed fetch all rendered one raw UUID\n  AFTER    api.automations.get({id}) via tryCall, ApiError kept   -> four distinguishable states:\n             resolving | linked (provenance) | named (no provenance) | not-visible (404) | unreadable\n           + schedule-detail-page.test.tsx covers each, and pins that no /automations anchor remains",
      "rawText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-22 (S8 review round) - THE CENSUS MISSED FOUR REACHABLE STRINGS, AND THREE OF THE\nSURFACES IT REWROTE HAD NO TEST THAT COULD FAIL. Extends the S8 as-built note above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 S8, REVIEW ROUND section.\n\nTHE FOUR STRINGS THE SWEEP MISSED, and where they actually lived\n\n  web/components/artifacts/artifact-backend-panel.tsx   \"configuram-se em Automa\u00e7\u00f5es.\"\n      <- the harmful one: live guidance naming the REMOVED surface as the place to act,\n         rendered in the ordinary no-backend case on /artifacts\n  web/stores/integrations.ts        provision fallback toast, behind the very button S8 reworded\n  web/app/(dashboard)/cofre/page.tsx   the lock-all confirm dialog\n  web/lib/privacy-claims.ts         ledgerKindLabels.automation, in a file this commit already edited\n\n  WHY THEY SURVIVED: completeness was checked by grepping the LOCALE files, which is the one place\n  the word was not hiding. Hardcoded JSX and store-level fallbacks are the census surface.\n\nTHE OVERLAY NAMES THE RUN, WITH THE RUN'S OWN ID\n\n  BEFORE   {t.runIdPrefix}{activeRun.automationId.slice(0,8)}     <- label renamed, value not\n  AFTER    {t.runIdPrefix}{activeRun.runId.slice(0,8)}            <- data-testid pause-overlay-run-id\n  + web/__tests__/components/pause-for-user-overlay.test.tsx      <- it had NO test at any layer\n\nTHE [id] RESOLVER, NOW EXERCISED THROUGH THE REAL STORE\n\n  BEFORE   vi.mock('@/stores/automations')  -> the resolver was mocked out of its own test\n             (patching the real fetchOne to return null left 613/613 web tests green)\n  AFTER    vi.mock('@/lib/api') only        -> real store, real normalizeWireAutomation, real\n             error branches; the wire shape is in the path, which is where `source` and `orgId` live\n  + a foreign-org row now falls back to /integrations rather than replacing a super-admin onto\n    THEIR OWN org's page for that key (a wrong answer that looks right)\n\nTHE SCHEDULE TARGET, RESOLVED AT THE ROW AND NOT THE LIST\n\n  BEFORE   useAutomationsStore.automations.find(id)   -> the VIEWER's list; a peer's private row,\n             a list still loading and a failed fetch all rendered one raw UUID\n  AFTER    api.automations.get({id}) via tryCall, ApiError kept   -> four distinguishable states:\n             resolving | linked (provenance) | named (no provenance) | not-visible (404) | unreadable\n           + schedule-detail-page.test.tsx covers each, and pins that no /automations anchor remains",
      "originalText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-22 (S8 review round) - THE CENSUS MISSED FOUR REACHABLE STRINGS, AND THREE OF THE\nSURFACES IT REWROTE HAD NO TEST THAT COULD FAIL. Extends the S8 as-built note above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-22 S8, REVIEW ROUND section.\n\nTHE FOUR STRINGS THE SWEEP MISSED, and where they actually lived\n\n  web/components/artifacts/artifact-backend-panel.tsx   \"configuram-se em Automa\u00e7\u00f5es.\"\n      <- the harmful one: live guidance naming the REMOVED surface as the place to act,\n         rendered in the ordinary no-backend case on /artifacts\n  web/stores/integrations.ts        provision fallback toast, behind the very button S8 reworded\n  web/app/(dashboard)/cofre/page.tsx   the lock-all confirm dialog\n  web/lib/privacy-claims.ts         ledgerKindLabels.automation, in a file this commit already edited\n\n  WHY THEY SURVIVED: completeness was checked by grepping the LOCALE files, which is the one place\n  the word was not hiding. Hardcoded JSX and store-level fallbacks are the census surface.\n\nTHE OVERLAY NAMES THE RUN, WITH THE RUN'S OWN ID\n\n  BEFORE   {t.runIdPrefix}{activeRun.automationId.slice(0,8)}     <- label renamed, value not\n  AFTER    {t.runIdPrefix}{activeRun.runId.slice(0,8)}            <- data-testid pause-overlay-run-id\n  + web/__tests__/components/pause-for-user-overlay.test.tsx      <- it had NO test at any layer\n\nTHE [id] RESOLVER, NOW EXERCISED THROUGH THE REAL STORE\n\n  BEFORE   vi.mock('@/stores/automations')  -> the resolver was mocked out of its own test\n             (patching the real fetchOne to return null left 613/613 web tests green)\n  AFTER    vi.mock('@/lib/api') only        -> real store, real normalizeWireAutomation, real\n             error branches; the wire shape is in the path, which is where `source` and `orgId` live\n  + a foreign-org row now falls back to /integrations rather than replacing a super-admin onto\n    THEIR OWN org's page for that key (a wrong answer that looks right)\n\nTHE SCHEDULE TARGET, RESOLVED AT THE ROW AND NOT THE LIST\n\n  BEFORE   useAutomationsStore.automations.find(id)   -> the VIEWER's list; a peer's private row,\n             a list still loading and a failed fetch all rendered one raw UUID\n  AFTER    api.automations.get({id}) via tryCall, ApiError kept   -> four distinguishable states:\n             resolving | linked (provenance) | named (no provenance) | not-visible (404) | unreadable\n           + schedule-detail-page.test.tsx covers each, and pins that no /automations anchor remains",
