    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "correction-20260823-s8-live-capability-id",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 40920.0,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 665.0,
      "text": "CORRECTION 2026-08-23 (S8 live pass) - ONE IDENTIFIER MEANT TWO THINGS, AND THE CLIENT READ THE\nUSELESS ONE. Extends the S8 as-built and review-round notes above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-23 \"S8 live pass: the capability tells a client which automation is THEIRS\".\n\nTHE TWO IDENTIFIERS\n\n  api/assets/integrations/citius/config.json          (the SHIPPED package, global, one copy)\n    automationBinding: { automationId: 'citius-notificacoes-template',   <-- A PLACEHOLDER.\n                         automationTemplate: 'notificacoes' }                names nothing, ever\n\n  automation/integration-automations.ts  provisionIntegrationAutomations  (PER ORG, on demand)\n    managedAutomationId(orgId, 'citius', 'notificacoes') = <sha256>       <-- the row that RUNS\n    stored with source: { integrationKey, templateKey }                   <-- the only join back\n\n  BEFORE: web/lib/integrations/action-view.ts automationIdOf\n            capability.integration.actions[].automationBinding.automationId   -> 404, always\n  AFTER:  capability.actions[].automationId                                   -> the org's row\n\nTHE SEAM THAT RESOLVES BETWEEN THEM (integrations/ may not import automation/ - the S1 evidence\ncollector is the standing precedent, and this is the second instance of the same edge)\n\n    server.ts  integrationsRouter({ ..., resolveManagedAutomationIds })\n      -> routes/integrations.ts  capabilityCtxOf  (threaded like platformConnected)\n        -> integrations/integration-capability.ts  getIntegrationCapability\n             ONE call per capability read, before the per-action loop\n             managedAutomationIdFor(action, ids) keys on automationTemplate, NEVER on automationId\n        -> automation/integration-automations.ts  managedAutomationIdsFor(actor, key)\n             one provenance query: { orgId, 'source.integrationKey' }\n\n  ABSENT is meaningful and is two honest states: an api-call action has no automation, and a bound\n  action nobody has provisioned has no ROW - the id is deterministic and could be computed, and\n  emitting it would promise an automation that 404s one fetch later.\n\nWHAT THE HERMETIC TESTS HAD ENCODED\n  Both S2 fixtures mocked automationBinding.automationId AS the org's real id - a shape no production\n  writer can emit - so they did not merely miss the bug, they encoded its inverse as the expected\n  world. Both now carry the placeholder on the definition and the real id on the typed action, with\n  the two values deliberately different.",
      "rawText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-23 (S8 live pass) - ONE IDENTIFIER MEANT TWO THINGS, AND THE CLIENT READ THE\nUSELESS ONE. Extends the S8 as-built and review-round notes above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-23 \"S8 live pass: the capability tells a client which automation is THEIRS\".\n\nTHE TWO IDENTIFIERS\n\n  api/assets/integrations/citius/config.json          (the SHIPPED package, global, one copy)\n    automationBinding: { automationId: 'citius-notificacoes-template',   <-- A PLACEHOLDER.\n                         automationTemplate: 'notificacoes' }                names nothing, ever\n\n  automation/integration-automations.ts  provisionIntegrationAutomations  (PER ORG, on demand)\n    managedAutomationId(orgId, 'citius', 'notificacoes') = <sha256>       <-- the row that RUNS\n    stored with source: { integrationKey, templateKey }                   <-- the only join back\n\n  BEFORE: web/lib/integrations/action-view.ts automationIdOf\n            capability.integration.actions[].automationBinding.automationId   -> 404, always\n  AFTER:  capability.actions[].automationId                                   -> the org's row\n\nTHE SEAM THAT RESOLVES BETWEEN THEM (integrations/ may not import automation/ - the S1 evidence\ncollector is the standing precedent, and this is the second instance of the same edge)\n\n    server.ts  integrationsRouter({ ..., resolveManagedAutomationIds })\n      -> routes/integrations.ts  capabilityCtxOf  (threaded like platformConnected)\n        -> integrations/integration-capability.ts  getIntegrationCapability\n             ONE call per capability read, before the per-action loop\n             managedAutomationIdFor(action, ids) keys on automationTemplate, NEVER on automationId\n        -> automation/integration-automations.ts  managedAutomationIdsFor(actor, key)\n             one provenance query: { orgId, 'source.integrationKey' }\n\n  ABSENT is meaningful and is two honest states: an api-call action has no automation, and a bound\n  action nobody has provisioned has no ROW - the id is deterministic and could be computed, and\n  emitting it would promise an automation that 404s one fetch later.\n\nWHAT THE HERMETIC TESTS HAD ENCODED\n  Both S2 fixtures mocked automationBinding.automationId AS the org's real id - a shape no production\n  writer can emit - so they did not merely miss the bug, they encoded its inverse as the expected\n  world. Both now carry the placeholder on the definition and the real id on the typed action, with\n  the two values deliberately different.",
      "originalText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-23 (S8 live pass) - ONE IDENTIFIER MEANT TWO THINGS, AND THE CLIENT READ THE\nUSELESS ONE. Extends the S8 as-built and review-round notes above.\nJournal: docs/decisions.md 2026-08-23 \"S8 live pass: the capability tells a client which automation is THEIRS\".\n\nTHE TWO IDENTIFIERS\n\n  api/assets/integrations/citius/config.json          (the SHIPPED package, global, one copy)\n    automationBinding: { automationId: 'citius-notificacoes-template',   <-- A PLACEHOLDER.\n                         automationTemplate: 'notificacoes' }                names nothing, ever\n\n  automation/integration-automations.ts  provisionIntegrationAutomations  (PER ORG, on demand)\n    managedAutomationId(orgId, 'citius', 'notificacoes') = <sha256>       <-- the row that RUNS\n    stored with source: { integrationKey, templateKey }                   <-- the only join back\n\n  BEFORE: web/lib/integrations/action-view.ts automationIdOf\n            capability.integration.actions[].automationBinding.automationId   -> 404, always\n  AFTER:  capability.actions[].automationId                                   -> the org's row\n\nTHE SEAM THAT RESOLVES BETWEEN THEM (integrations/ may not import automation/ - the S1 evidence\ncollector is the standing precedent, and this is the second instance of the same edge)\n\n    server.ts  integrationsRouter({ ..., resolveManagedAutomationIds })\n      -> routes/integrations.ts  capabilityCtxOf  (threaded like platformConnected)\n        -> integrations/integration-capability.ts  getIntegrationCapability\n             ONE call per capability read, before the per-action loop\n             managedAutomationIdFor(action, ids) keys on automationTemplate, NEVER on automationId\n        -> automation/integration-automations.ts  managedAutomationIdsFor(actor, key)\n             one provenance query: { orgId, 'source.integrationKey' }\n\n  ABSENT is meaningful and is two honest states: an api-call action has no automation, and a bound\n  action nobody has provisioned has no ROW - the id is deterministic and could be computed, and\n  emitting it would promise an automation that 404s one fetch later.\n\nWHAT THE HERMETIC TESTS HAD ENCODED\n  Both S2 fixtures mocked automationBinding.automationId AS the org's real id - a shape no production\n  writer can emit - so they did not merely miss the bug, they encoded its inverse as the expected\n  world. Both now carry the placeholder on the definition and the real id on the typed action, with\n  the two values deliberately different.",
