    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s9-note-8421451881",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 36535.0,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 945.0,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S9, THE CITIUS REFERENCE CASE): one new module, one new injected seam,\none new ACTION BACKING, and NO new store. Appended; no element above is edited. Journal:\ndocs/decisions.md \"2026-08-22 - S9: the Citius reference case\", D-S9-1 through D-S9-5.\n\nNEW MODULE\n  legal/citius-processos.ts (tier 5)   The READ side of the Citius rail. Projects the notification\n                                       metadata citius-sync.ts has ALREADY LANDED into one row per\n                                       process: {processo, tribunal, ultimoAto, ultimaNotificacao,\n                                       primeiraNotificacao, notificacoes, comDocumento} + origem.\n                                       Holds NO collection handle: every read of citius_notifications\n                                       stays inside citius-sync.ts behind syncStateKeyFor, so the\n                                       per-MANDATARIO scoping (hazard 4) cannot be dropped by a\n                                       reader that only remembered the org.\n                                       Exports legalTenantReadHandler - the seam implementation,\n                                       here rather than as a lambda in server.ts, because a lambda in\n                                       the composition root has no suite behind it (A2 review).\n\nNEW INJECTED SEAM (the sixth; integrations/ -> legal/)\n  ExecutorDeps.readTenantDataset       Bound ONCE in server.ts to legalTenantReadHandler and threaded\n                                       to ALL FOUR executor call sites: the automation-seam executor,\n                                       the schedule supervisor's runIntegrationAction, the capability\n                                       rail (CapabilityContext), and achieve. ABSENT-MEANS-REFUSE,\n                                       not absent-means-skip: an unbound seam answers\n                                       unsupported_backing_type, because the alternative - an empty\n                                       list - reads to a lawyer as \"you have no processes\".\n                                       Pinned against the REAL buildApp by\n                                       tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts.\n\nNEW BACKING: tenant-read (the fourth, beside api-call / browser-steps / bash-cli)\n  Shape          backingType: 'tenant-read' + tenantRead: { dataset }. DERIVED when a tenantRead is\n                 present and no automationBinding is; an automationBinding still WINS, so no action\n                 shipped before S9 changes meaning. Refuses a dead httpConfig or binding beside it.\n  The property   A TENANT-READ ACTION NEVER CAUSES A CREDENTIAL TO BE DECRYPTED. Its dispatch sits\n                 ABOVE decryptCredentialFields, so the decrypt, the WS-C shadow comparator, the\n                 provider credential resolver and the egress binding are UNREACHED, not unused.\n                 Proved behaviourally: the suite corrupts the owner's ciphertext, watches an api-call\n                 action on the same row fail credential_decrypt_failed, and the tenant read answer.\n  Still gated    The write gate answers FIRST (a mutating tenant-read action is refused\n                 awaiting_consent and the reader is never called); not_connected/disabled still\n                 refuse. No secret spent is not the same as no gate met.\n  actionShape    Gains its new term ONLY WHEN tenantRead IS PRESENT. That string is DURABLE STATE on\n                 every standing approval and every authored action's authoring.shape; an\n                 unconditional seventh tuple element would have unmatched every approval already\n                 given and demoted every trusted action to provisional.\n\nTHE SHIPPED INSTANCE\n  citius / processos                   dataset citius.processos, mutates:false, NO declared arguments\n                                       (D-S9-2: every argument of a mutates:false action is one the\n                                       parametrize rung may hand a model, and a model narrowing a\n                                       list the caller did not ask to narrow is a silently shorter\n                                       answer). Named `processos` because matchActionForGoal requires\n                                       the goal to name EVERY token of the action's name - which is\n                                       why get-ongoing-processes was unreachable (D-S9-4).\n                                       COVERAGE: processes WITH NOTIFICATIONS, not all processes.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S9, THE CITIUS REFERENCE CASE): one new module, one new injected seam,\none new ACTION BACKING, and NO new store. Appended; no element above is edited. Journal:\ndocs/decisions.md \"2026-08-22 - S9: the Citius reference case\", D-S9-1 through D-S9-5.\n\nNEW MODULE\n  legal/citius-processos.ts (tier 5)   The READ side of the Citius rail. Projects the notification\n                                       metadata citius-sync.ts has ALREADY LANDED into one row per\n                                       process: {processo, tribunal, ultimoAto, ultimaNotificacao,\n                                       primeiraNotificacao, notificacoes, comDocumento} + origem.\n                                       Holds NO collection handle: every read of citius_notifications\n                                       stays inside citius-sync.ts behind syncStateKeyFor, so the\n                                       per-MANDATARIO scoping (hazard 4) cannot be dropped by a\n                                       reader that only remembered the org.\n                                       Exports legalTenantReadHandler - the seam implementation,\n                                       here rather than as a lambda in server.ts, because a lambda in\n                                       the composition root has no suite behind it (A2 review).\n\nNEW INJECTED SEAM (the sixth; integrations/ -> legal/)\n  ExecutorDeps.readTenantDataset       Bound ONCE in server.ts to legalTenantReadHandler and threaded\n                                       to ALL FOUR executor call sites: the automation-seam executor,\n                                       the schedule supervisor's runIntegrationAction, the capability\n                                       rail (CapabilityContext), and achieve. ABSENT-MEANS-REFUSE,\n                                       not absent-means-skip: an unbound seam answers\n                                       unsupported_backing_type, because the alternative - an empty\n                                       list - reads to a lawyer as \"you have no processes\".\n                                       Pinned against the REAL buildApp by\n                                       tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts.\n\nNEW BACKING: tenant-read (the fourth, beside api-call / browser-steps / bash-cli)\n  Shape          backingType: 'tenant-read' + tenantRead: { dataset }. DERIVED when a tenantRead is\n                 present and no automationBinding is; an automationBinding still WINS, so no action\n                 shipped before S9 changes meaning. Refuses a dead httpConfig or binding beside it.\n  The property   A TENANT-READ ACTION NEVER CAUSES A CREDENTIAL TO BE DECRYPTED. Its dispatch sits\n                 ABOVE decryptCredentialFields, so the decrypt, the WS-C shadow comparator, the\n                 provider credential resolver and the egress binding are UNREACHED, not unused.\n                 Proved behaviourally: the suite corrupts the owner's ciphertext, watches an api-call\n                 action on the same row fail credential_decrypt_failed, and the tenant read answer.\n  Still gated    The write gate answers FIRST (a mutating tenant-read action is refused\n                 awaiting_consent and the reader is never called); not_connected/disabled still\n                 refuse. No secret spent is not the same as no gate met.\n  actionShape    Gains its new term ONLY WHEN tenantRead IS PRESENT. That string is DURABLE STATE on\n                 every standing approval and every authored action's authoring.shape; an\n                 unconditional seventh tuple element would have unmatched every approval already\n                 given and demoted every trusted action to provisional.\n\nTHE SHIPPED INSTANCE\n  citius / processos                   dataset citius.processos, mutates:false, NO declared arguments\n                                       (D-S9-2: every argument of a mutates:false action is one the\n                                       parametrize rung may hand a model, and a model narrowing a\n                                       list the caller did not ask to narrow is a silently shorter\n                                       answer). Named `processos` because matchActionForGoal requires\n                                       the goal to name EVERY token of the action's name - which is\n                                       why get-ongoing-processes was unreachable (D-S9-4).\n                                       COVERAGE: processes WITH NOTIFICATIONS, not all processes.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-22 (slice S9, THE CITIUS REFERENCE CASE): one new module, one new injected seam,\none new ACTION BACKING, and NO new store. Appended; no element above is edited. Journal:\ndocs/decisions.md \"2026-08-22 - S9: the Citius reference case\", D-S9-1 through D-S9-5.\n\nNEW MODULE\n  legal/citius-processos.ts (tier 5)   The READ side of the Citius rail. Projects the notification\n                                       metadata citius-sync.ts has ALREADY LANDED into one row per\n                                       process: {processo, tribunal, ultimoAto, ultimaNotificacao,\n                                       primeiraNotificacao, notificacoes, comDocumento} + origem.\n                                       Holds NO collection handle: every read of citius_notifications\n                                       stays inside citius-sync.ts behind syncStateKeyFor, so the\n                                       per-MANDATARIO scoping (hazard 4) cannot be dropped by a\n                                       reader that only remembered the org.\n                                       Exports legalTenantReadHandler - the seam implementation,\n                                       here rather than as a lambda in server.ts, because a lambda in\n                                       the composition root has no suite behind it (A2 review).\n\nNEW INJECTED SEAM (the sixth; integrations/ -> legal/)\n  ExecutorDeps.readTenantDataset       Bound ONCE in server.ts to legalTenantReadHandler and threaded\n                                       to ALL FOUR executor call sites: the automation-seam executor,\n                                       the schedule supervisor's runIntegrationAction, the capability\n                                       rail (CapabilityContext), and achieve. ABSENT-MEANS-REFUSE,\n                                       not absent-means-skip: an unbound seam answers\n                                       unsupported_backing_type, because the alternative - an empty\n                                       list - reads to a lawyer as \"you have no processes\".\n                                       Pinned against the REAL buildApp by\n                                       tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts.\n\nNEW BACKING: tenant-read (the fourth, beside api-call / browser-steps / bash-cli)\n  Shape          backingType: 'tenant-read' + tenantRead: { dataset }. DERIVED when a tenantRead is\n                 present and no automationBinding is; an automationBinding still WINS, so no action\n                 shipped before S9 changes meaning. Refuses a dead httpConfig or binding beside it.\n  The property   A TENANT-READ ACTION NEVER CAUSES A CREDENTIAL TO BE DECRYPTED. Its dispatch sits\n                 ABOVE decryptCredentialFields, so the decrypt, the WS-C shadow comparator, the\n                 provider credential resolver and the egress binding are UNREACHED, not unused.\n                 Proved behaviourally: the suite corrupts the owner's ciphertext, watches an api-call\n                 action on the same row fail credential_decrypt_failed, and the tenant read answer.\n  Still gated    The write gate answers FIRST (a mutating tenant-read action is refused\n                 awaiting_consent and the reader is never called); not_connected/disabled still\n                 refuse. No secret spent is not the same as no gate met.\n  actionShape    Gains its new term ONLY WHEN tenantRead IS PRESENT. That string is DURABLE STATE on\n                 every standing approval and every authored action's authoring.shape; an\n                 unconditional seventh tuple element would have unmatched every approval already\n                 given and demoted every trusted action to provisional.\n\nTHE SHIPPED INSTANCE\n  citius / processos                   dataset citius.processos, mutates:false, NO declared arguments\n                                       (D-S9-2: every argument of a mutates:false action is one the\n                                       parametrize rung may hand a model, and a model narrowing a\n                                       list the caller did not ask to narrow is a silently shorter\n                                       answer). Named `processos` because matchActionForGoal requires\n                                       the goal to name EVERY token of the action's name - which is\n                                       why get-ongoing-processes was unreachable (D-S9-4).\n                                       COVERAGE: processes WITH NOTIFICATIONS, not all processes.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
